ises\",\"blocking_defects\":[],\"code_observations\":[\"s1-event-1 runs 0.64 to 1.24 inside street-yard (0 to 3.91). The water tops the curb and climbs to the ankle mark, reward at 1.00 s. No station stands in the yard.\"],\"module_sha256\":\"916e12f7be70b88b289e29b42c6e4961fe22dfd0e70027943339dc61edf3de91\",\"source_claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\"},{\"action_id\":\"carry-signal\",\"blocking_defects\":[],\"code_observations\":[\"s5-event-2 runs 29.097 to 29.965 inside radio-rings (27.08 to 31.13). The rings pass the half-mile tag over 'more than a half-mile'. The range is shown as described, not measured.\"],\"module_sha256\":\"916e12f7be70b88b289e29b42c6e4961fe22dfd0e70027943339dc61edf3de91\",\"source_claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\"},{\"action_id\":\"spread-map\",\"blocking_defects\":[],\"code_observations\":[\"s6-event-2 runs 38.172 to 39.112 wholly inside flood-paths (38.10 to 40.94), with paths=s6e2 performed from 0 to 1 over 'maps flood paths' and its reward at 38.736 in the same shot.\"],\"module_sha256\":\"916e12f7be70b88b289e29b42c6e4961fe22dfd0e70027943339dc61edf3de91\",\"source_claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\"}],\"blocking_defects\":[],\"board_path\":\"{REPO}/out/dispatch/storyboard.json\",\"board_sha256\":\"5a1b8e26cba9ccb64d48e5741a2b56a5175ea25f9ba7a46e9ef393c7698cf4a6\",\"code_observations\":[\"Current-bytes diff by my own reading: the board and the reviewed board are identical except timing_provenance.word_content_sha256. words.json and the reviewed words file have identical acoustic_matching, speech_runs, internal_pauses_joined, counts (38 boundaries measured, 132 words, 37 anchored, 95 modelled) and all 132 word entries. They differ only in duration_s (65.0 to 64.4) and in provenance voice_sha256 (0565b771 to 57f9c656) and mix_sha256 (35e67958 to 4a96b35f). asr_sha256 (9ee66440), analysis_duration_s (58.566208), model and command are unchanged.\",\"captions.json (a6b0e45a) carries the same 16 cues as the board's captions. sfx_events.json carries 5 events at the board's event starts. mix.json records 64.40 s (3,091,200 samples at 48 kHz, equal to runtime 59.4 s plus the 5 s credits), time_stretch 1.0 on every track, and the voice stem at the same sample count.\",\"n1a (0.58 to 3.58): street-yard. s1-event-1 0.64 to 1.24 shows water topping the curb to the ankle mark (reward 1.00). s1-event-2 2.14 to 2.86 shows water reaching the boots while the phone stays dark. n1b (4.24 to 8.28): phone-late. s1-event-3 5.452 to 6.502 slides the late banner on over 'says the phone'.\",\"n2a (8.96 to 11.22): station-wide. s2-event-1 9.231 to 9.819 reveals the prototype and pins its tag. n2b (11.90 to 14.96): panel-charge, where s2-event-2 12.145 to 12.879 fills the battery over 'charges itself'. Then no-tower, where s2-event-3 13.675 to 14.409 runs the dashed link to half way and pins 'No cell tower needed' over 'needs no cell'.\",\"n3a (15.90 to 19.14): sensor-stack, s3-event-1 16.030 to 16.742 (glints, 'Four optical sensors' tag). water-marks, s3-event-2 17.131 to 17.909 (second mark goes under and lights). weather-row, s3-event-3 18.395 to 19.043 (Rain, Temperature, Humidity and Light lamps). 'watch the water' falls on weather-row about 0.4 s after the crossing. Non-blocking.\",\"n4a (19.94 to 23.18): chip-glow close, s4-event-1 21.722 to 22.532 (readings along the traces, chip glow 0.35). n4b (23.80 to 26.52): chip-glow detail, whose push lands at 24.562, then s4-event-2 24.562 to 25.160 lights the lamp and pins 'Judged on the station' over 'judges flood risk'. no-server wide carries risk=1, and s4-event-3 25.704 to 26.357 draws the dark server outline over 'central server'.\",\"n5a (27.36 to 30.70): radio-rings. s5-event-1 27.494 to 28.228 is the pulse. s5-event-2 29.097 to 29.965 pins the half-mile tag over 'more than a half-mile'. n5b (31.56 to 34.74): radio-open. s5-event-3 32.514 to 33.532: the ring reaches the mast at mid-event, the lamp lights and the five-mile tag pins.\",\"n6a (35.54 to 40.24): hub-desk. s6-event-1 35.728 to 36.762 brings the dots, the forearm and the 'A second, larger model' tag, with paths at 0.15*s6e1. flood-paths: s6-event-2 38.172 to 39.112 spreads paths=s6e2 over 'maps flood paths', straddling the measured 38.58/38.70 cue boundary. s6-event-3 39.300 to 40.146 brings zones=s6e3 and the responders tag over 'for responders'.\",\"n7a (41.22 to 44.52): validation-card close. s7-event-1 42.540 to 43.530 fills the bar to share 0.9882 with '98.82%'; the blank card is off-frame. n7b (45.24 to 48.48): validation-card detail. s7-event-2 46.212 to 47.054 pins 'Initial assessments after training'. s7-event-3 47.573 to 48.318 slides the unstamped blank card to the right edge.\",\"n8a (49.48 to 51.82): no-field-card detail with the s8 ids. The push ends at 50.182. s8-event-0 50.182 to 50.931 stamps 'none reported', the result holds 1.23 s, and the cut falls in the 51.82 to 52.50 silence. n8b (52.50 to 54.80): empty-map close, with s8-event-1 52.592 settling the map, s8-event-2 53.374 sweeping the search ring and s8-event-3 54.202 pinning 'No installation named'.\",\"n9a (55.78 to 57.36): station-return wide, with the tag kept. s9-event-1 55.843 hovers the goal pin, s9-event-2 56.380 draws the dashed station outline and s9-event-3 56.949 pins the 'Deployment goal' tag. A 2.10 s closing hold follows.\",\"Figure attribution in the current bytes: n7a 'The university reports early chip AI validation.' has claims c4 and c18, and the s7-card label reads 'validation accuracy card reading 98.82 percent, the university reported figure'. The 'Initial assessments after training' tag carries 'early'. The s4-chip label is 'small chip on the station running the AI, marked TinyML', which ties the figure to the on-device chip model with the university as reporter. The