 at_s, and each lies wholly inside the shot whose view draws it: s2-event-3 13.675 to 14.409 in no-tower (13.59 to 15.62); s3-event-3 18.395 to 19.043 in weather-row (18.313 to 19.66); s4-event-2 24.562 to 25.160 in chip-glow detail (23.49 to 25.285); s6-event-2 38.172 to 39.112 and s6-event-3 39.300 to 40.146 in flood-paths (38.10 to 40.94); s7-event-3 47.573 to 48.318 in validation-card detail (44.88 to 49.20); s8-event-0 50.182 to 50.931 in no-field-card (49.20 to 52.16). The first reward is at 1.00 s. The largest reward gaps are 3.58 s (43.134 to 46.717) and 3.51 s, the gap would be 3.91 s even without the s7 slide, and the end gap is 2.24 s. Wall views are 5 of 20 shots, 17.40 of 59.4 s (29.3 percent). The sfx file and the mix sound cues sit at the moved event starts (chip-hum 24.562, mark-tone 17.131, blank-card-quiet 50.182). B's old ids don't apply here: the current A board has s8-event-0, so the renderer takes moved=true with the s8-valcard, s8-valbar, s8-assess, s8-card2 and s8-blank ids, all present in the s8 planes and registered for no-field-card in db04f225. Non-blocking cautions for the phone pass are unchanged: the s4 'Judged on the station' tag is fully opaque about 0.52 s and complete 0.125 s before its cut; the three s3 shots last 1.347 s each; 'watch the water' is heard over the weather-row lamps; the s7-event-3 blank-card edge is about 78 px; four wall shots run consecutively 40.94 to 55.50; the s9 closing events are 0.35 to 0.38 s wide in a wide. Cosmetic: the cue_plan string is still stale under measured timing. Erratum to my report 23 (preserved unchanged, not edited by anyone): its opening_a strongest_frame contains a typo, '17.131 to 18.909'. The correct window, stated in the same sentence and everywhere else, is 17.131 to 17.909. A code-plan pass authorizes a phone test only.\",\"quality_contract_sha256\":\"f54137adf7cf5181ff077cb8b9fd85a44131cee44b1fb8139def2f12a088fdfa\",\"renderer_sha256\":\"cdc9d67ed208f239a62c702fcfbfa44980fba73a25a840545cc97ea6a757c246\",\"review_scope\":\"code-plan\",\"reviewed_at\":\"2026-10-16T23:30:00Z\",\"reviewer_identity\":\"claude-opus-5-5 storyboard-critic (Opus High), independent read-only reviewer in a same-worker charged continuation (storyboard_critics 24 per the caller; I did not verify the reservation on the ledger), distinct from the claude-sonnet-5-5 director. Limits: code-plan scope only. I rendered and viewed no pixels and heard no audio. I ran no command and computed no hash. All digests are the director's mechanically supplied values; they agree with delta-machine.json as text.\",\"story_review\":{\"blocking_defects\":[],\"claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"one_viewing_summary\":\"Planned chain, not observed. A San Antonio yard floods to the ankle mark while the porch phone stays dark, and the warning lands late. A self-charging prototype station at a curb needs no cell tower. Its four lenses at four heights catch the light, the water lights the second as it goes under, and the weather lamps come on. Inside the housing the readings reach one chip, which lights an amber risk lamp while a far server outline stays dark. A radio pulse runs past a half-mile tag and across five miles of open country to a hub's mast. At the hub a second, larger model's map spreads flood paths and risk zones for responders. The limit follows: the university's 98.82% validation figure pinned as initial assessments after training, a blank field card stamped none reported, and a map searched with no installation named. The close is the empty curb, a dashed station outline and a hovering goal pin.\",\"opening_to_ending\":\"The opening question, whether a flood station can judge rising street water with no power line and no cell tower, is staged as water arriving before the phone warning. The film ends at the same kind of curb with no flood and no installed station: a dashed outline draws itself, a goal pin hovers without landing and the deployment goal tag pins. The answer is yes in design. The proof so far is only reported early validation accuracy, and no installation is named. The ending answers what happens next without promising an unreported outcome.\",\"policy_sha256\":\"01bff5185647039cf6cbefefda605e424cf6cbb35557b198dc3a31e336efd7c0\",\"story_sha256\":\"d82de390d3657d5ddfdd03fc5b6b11fb69c5749a526169b3fe9ff20031f5fb5e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"weakest_transition\":\"s6 to s7, at 40.94 s: the flood-paths dashboard with its responders tag cuts to the validation card. The only visible bridge is the amber accent, and the narration 'The university reports early chip AI validation' carries the cause. That leaves a false-inference risk that the figure belongs to the hub's larger model, which the spoken and captioned 'chip AI' prevents textually. Non-blocking.\"},\"strongest_frame\":\"s3-shot-2 water-marks close (16.967 to 18.313 s). On s3-event-2 (17.131 to 17.909) brown water rises past the already-lit first lens and the second lights as it goes under (podLit from the level lerp LEVEL.ankle to LEVEL.second). This is the whole sensing mechanism as one performed change on the one station the film carries. The caution is that it lasts only 1.347 s.\",\"treatment\":\"a\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"weakest_frame\":\"s7-shot-2 validation-card detail (44.88 to 49.20 s), the second consecutive shot on the same card. From 43.53 (bar complete) to 46.212 (tag starts) the only motion is the 1 s push-in at 44.88. After that come a small 'Initial assessments after training' tag and a blank-card edge about 78 px wide sliding in at 47.573 to 48.318. The hold is motivated, because the figure is read as it is spoken, and the gap stays at 3.58 s. It is still the least active picture and opens a 14.56 s run of wall views.\"},\"sha256\":\"4b9294fd5664d9f77c434623c1dd423de7d5f835e6c16ed2732fb84ab38c27e7\"},\"opening-b-critic.json\":{\"path\":\"{REPO}/out/dispatch/opening-b-critic.json\",\"report\":{\"action_reviews\":[{\"action_id\":\"charge-battery\",\"blocking_defects\":[],\"code_observations\":\"s2-event-2, 12.145 to 12.879, in panel-charge close (11.56 to 15.62) under 'charges itself from light' (n2b 11.9 to 14.96). The panel glint and battery fill are performed on the hero group by the film clock. Claims c5, c6 and c14.\",\"module_sha256\":\"f3dbf42717bbea88758c825d05cfeda588ebbe2ddbfcf493e3c5ddd86cc5461c\",\"source_claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\"},{\"action_id\":\"cross-marks\",\"blocking_defects\":[],\"code_observations\":\"Lenses catch the light at s3-event-1 (16.03 to 16.742). The second lens goes under at s3-event-2 (16.872 to 17.52). Both are in water-marks detail (15.62 to 17.64), where cam scale is lerp(1.25, 1, ease(s3e1)). In B the four lenses glint in place of a 'Four optical sensors' tag. The lit state holds 0.12 s before the cut, which is a phone check. Claim c2.\",\"module_sha256\":\"f3dbf42717bbea88758c825d05cfeda588ebbe2ddbfcf493e3c5ddd86cc5461c\",\"source_claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\"},{\"action_id\":\"judge-locally\",\"blocking_defects\":[],\"code_observations\":\"Traces reach the chip at s4-event-1 (21.722 to 22.532, no-server close). The amber risk lamp and 'judged on the station' tag come at s4-event-2 (24.562 to 25.16, chip-glow detail 23.49 to 25.285). The dark server outline comes at s4-event-3 (25.704 to 26.357, no-server wide). The tag holds 0.125 s before the cut, which is a phone check. Claims c3 and c18.\",\"module_sha256\":\"f3dbf42717bbea88758c825d05cfeda588ebbe2ddbfcf493e3c5ddd86cc5461c\",\"source_claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\"},{\"action_id\":\"water-rises\",\"blocking_defects\":[],\"code_observations\":\"s1-event-0 (0.64 to 1.24) is the lowest lens going under in detail. In street-yard wide, water passes the ankle mark at s1-event-1 (2.08 to 2.74) and rises to the boots at s1-event-2 (2.8 to 3.46). The pull-back from scale 2.2 to 1 runs 1.955 to 2.74, which is fast. Claim c12. The lens-to-yard match cut carries a false-continuity risk, a sensor seeming to stand in the yard. The board says no station stands in this yard, and that must read on the phone.\",\"module_sha256\":\"f3dbf42717bbea88758c825d05cfeda588ebbe2ddbfcf493e3c5ddd86cc5461c\",\"source_claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\"},{\"action_id\":\"carry-signal\",\"blocking_defects\":[],\"code_observations\":\"Overhead rings at s5-event-1 (27.494 to 28.228). The half-mile tag is passed at s5-event-2 (29.164 to 30.032, radio-rings wide, ringStart = shot start) over 'more than a half-mile'. The ring reaches the mast at s5-event-3 (32.514 to 33.532, hub-wide). The radio-map five-mile label appears at lead > 0.92, around 28.0 s, ahead of n5b. That previews 'five miles' early but is not false. Claim c6.\",\"module_sha256\":\"916e12f7be70b88b289e29b42c6e4961fe22dfd0e70027943339dc61edf3de91\",\"source_claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\"},{\"action_id\":\"spread-map\",\"blocking_defects\":[],\"code_observations\":\"Dots and the 'second, larger model' tag at s6-event-1 (35.728 to 36.762). Paths at s6-event-2 (36.95 to 37.89), both in flood-paths overhead (35.26 to 38.1). Zones, forearm and responders tag at s6-event-3 (39.018 to 40.052, hub-desk close). The paths finish before the word 'maps' (about 38.27 to 39.21), so that word plays over the desk with the paths already drawn. This is mild early anticipation, not a mismatch. Claims c7, c16, c17 and c20.\",\"module_sha256\":\"916e12f7be70b88b289e29b42c6e4961fe22dfd0e70027943339dc61edf3de91\",\"source_claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"verdict\":\"pass\"}],\"blocking_defects\":[],\"board_path\":\"{REPO}/out/dispatch/opening-b.json\",\"board_sha256\":\"9fa8f52a4753b72dbc80e1f3c2c86d8f193ae340eaf54b588b597ca6de3ba92b\",\"code_observations\":[\"Shared body. runtime_s is 59.4. Scene starts and durations are s1 0/8.68, s2 8.68/6.94, s3 15.62/4.04, s4 19.66/7.42, s5 27.08/8.18, s6 35.26/5.68, s7 40.94/8.26, s8 49.2/6.3 and s9 55.5/3.9. These agree with measured-intervals-b.md and with A's measured body from report 24. s7 vo has two sentences with claims c4 and c18. s8 vo is 'The announcement reports no field result. It names no town with an installed station.' with claims c1, c4 and c10. delta-b-machine.json reports body_equal_to_A true, opening_digests_differ true and events_crossing_cuts [].\",\"Ceilings. The longest scene is s1 at 8.68 s, against the 9.5 s ceiling. The longest shots are s1-shot-3 at 4.77 s, s7-shot-2 at 4.32 s, s5-shot-3 at 4.13 s and s2-shot-2 at 4.06 s, all under 5.0 s.\",\"Containment, by my arithmetic. Each of the 29 events lies wholly inside its listed shot. The tightest event ends before a cut are: s3-event-2 ends 17.52 with the cut at 17.64 (0.12 s); s4-event-2 ends 25.16 with the cut at 25.285 (0.125 s); s6-event-2 ends 37.89 with the cut at 38.1 (0.21 s). In each case the reward lands 0.36 to 0.59 s before the cut. They pass at code scope and are listed as phone checks.\",\"The five moved windows match the build_split_b.py FIX fractions. Clause start + fraction x clause length gives: s1-event-1 2.08 to 2.74 in street-yard (1.955 to 3.91); s3-event-2 16.872 to 17.52 in water-marks (15.62 to 17.64); s4-event-2 24.562 to 25.16 in chip-glow (23.49 to 25.285); s5-event-2 29.164 to 30.032 in radio-rings (29.105 to 31.13); s6-event-2 36.95 to 37.89 in flood-paths (35.26 to 38.1).\",\"Rewards are placed at event start + 0.6 x width. The first reward is at 1.00 s. The largest gap is 3.583 s (43.134 to 46.717, s7-event-1 to s7-event-2). Without the s7-event-3 slide, the gap from s7-event-2 to s8-event-0 would be 3.914 s, still under 4.0. The last reward is 57.158 and the end gap is 2.242 s. All 29 rewards in film_direction match my values, including s7-event-3 at 48.02.\",\"Wall share. Six of 20 shots are wall or card views (radio-map, flood-paths, validation-card twice, no-field-card, empty-map). They total 19.985 s of 59.4 s, which is 33.6%, under the 40% limit.\",\"s7 slide-in. s7-event-3, 47.573 to 48.318, uses travel motion over n7b at fractions 0.72 to 0.95. In the renderer, moved = !!W['s8-event-0'] is true for B, so the slide is ease(s7e3) with resAt x = lerp(-730, -330, slide) at y 470, scale 0.85. s7-shot-2 is detail framing, so the 1.3 push about x 560 applies there. The visible slice of the blank card at the left edge is inferred at about 88 px and is not proven. The reward gap holds without it.\",\"s8 stamp, then station-return. s8-event-0, 50.182 to 50.931, sits in s8-shot-1 (no-field-card, close, 49.2 to 52.16). Its items are s8-blank and s8-card2, and the five s8 planes now carry s8-card2, s8-valcard, s8-valbar, s8-assess and s8-blank. The stamp holds 1.23 s and the cut at 52.16 falls in the silence between n8a (ends 51.82) and n8b (starts 52.5). The blank-card-quiet sound cue moved to s8-event-0 at gain 0.3. The station-return wide then performs settle, search ring and tag.\",\"s9 empty-map. The goal pin hovers 55.843 to 56.191, the dashed spot draws 56.38 to 56.76 and the deployment goal tag pins 56.949 to 57.297, all over n9a (55.78 to 57.36). They use s9-fence, s9-map, s9-goal, s9-spot, s9-notown and s9-tag. The final state holds 2.10 s. The pin never lands, so no installation is implied.\",\"Divergence from A is real. B opens on a lens detail instead of A's wide yard. It cranes down the station and then holds the panel close through the tower beat. It sees the readings from the street through the housing window, reads the radio from overhead before street level, and shows the hub map before the desk. It closes on the map close up, not the curb-outline close. s7 shares A's card composition except for the blank-card side. This shared limit composition is acceptable and not a relabel.\",\"Figure attribution. The s7 card reads 'the university reported figure', with the 'initial assessments after training' tag on s7-event-2. The s4 chip carries the TinyML claim c3/c18 and the figure carries c4. The board's source_limit is honest about validation versus field results.\",\"Region. San Antonio (Bexar) uses a limestone, storm gray and flood brown palette. Hill Country limestone fits a San Antonio street.\",\"Non-blocking cosmetic leftovers, with no visible or gate effect. The build_split_b.py docstring still says 'R12 proposal' and 'build_split.py'. The s8-shot-2 purpose text mentions a station outline that only s9 draws. quality_plan s7 source_basis says 'Claims c4' and omits c18, which vo_claims carries. The s7 attention beats' sound_action still mentions 'a dull stamp on the blank card', which now plays in s8. The narration_picture cue_plan prose still calls the cues provisional, although timing_mode is measured_caption_boundaries and all 16 captions carry start_measured and end_measured true. retime_evidence shows 9 of 9 cuts on measured word starts.\"],\"concept_sha256\":\"114e5443f51b0bda6f67373c0edb30e232d215e5c96f45d8a6b98c4c9ff67a64\",\"quality_contract_sha256\":\"f54137adf7cf5181ff077cb8b9fd85a44131cee44b1fb8139def2f12a088fdfa\",\"renderer_sha256\":\"cdc9d67ed208f239a62c702fcfbfa44980fba73a25a840545cc97ea6a757c246\",\"review_scope\":\"code-plan\",\"reviewed_at\":\"2026-10-17T01:00:00Z\",\"reviewer_identity\":\"claude-opus-5-5 independent read-only storyboard-critic (distinct from director claude-sonnet-5-5)\",\"story_review\":{\"blocking_defects\":[],\"claims_sha256\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"one_viewing_summary\":\"Planned chain, not observed pixels. A lens goes under water, and the same ankle-high water fills a yard while the porch phone stays dark until a late banner. The prototype station is craned down, charges from the sun and sends no line to a tower. Its four lenses get wet in turn and the weather lamps light. Readings run to the chip, which lights a local risk lamp while a central server stays dark. Radio rings cross the map, pass a half-mile tag and reach a hub mast five miles out. The hub map spreads flood paths and a responder's forearm settles beside the screen. Then come the limits: a reported validation figure tagged as initial assessments, a blank field-result card stamped none reported, a fence map with no pin, and a dashed goal pin that never lands.\",\"opening_to_ending\":\"Opening question: can a flood station judge rising street water with no power line and no cell tower? The design chain answers yes in pictures (charge, marks, chip, radio, hub map). The ending answers the 'how do we know' question honestly. The proof is validation accuracy, there is no field result, no town is named, and deployment is still the goal. The close states what happens next without promising an unreported outcome.\",\"policy_sha256\":\"01bff5185647039cf6cbefefda605e424cf6cbb35557b198dc3a31e336efd7c0\",\"story_sha256\":\"92983b6a52c2fe26539d40446ad6e5a351b0ab8ec2f963e648be537ecde49445\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"weakest_transition\":\"s6 to s7, at 40.94. The cut goes from the hub desk with the responder's forearm and the 'for emergency responders' tag to the validation card. The only bridge is the amber accent carried from the map onto the bar. This consequence-to-limit jump is the most abstract cut in the film. It reads as intended only if the n7a line lands with the bar fill (42.54 to 43.53). Within s8, the cut from the no-field-card close to the station-return wide at 52.16 is second weakest, but it falls cleanly in silence.\"},\"strongest_frame\":\"s1-shot-1, water-marks detail, 0.0 to 1.955. The plan is that brown water climbs over the lowest optical lens and the lens lights as it goes under (s1-event-0, 0.64 to 1.24, reward at 1.00 s, hook_payoff_s 0.934). The planned lit state then holds 0.715 s before the match cut on ankle height to the yard. The opening picture is the mechanism itself, inside the 1.5 s first-reward limit. Runner-up is the s3-shot-1 signature, where the second lens goes under at 16.872 to 17.52.\",\"treatment\":\"b\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"weakest_frame\":\"s8-shot-2, station-return wide, 52.16 to 55.5. The clause 'It names no town with an installed station' (n8b, 52.5 to 54.8) is carried by the small 300x336 paper map card on the fence inside a wide street frame. The settle (52.592 to 53.098), the dashed search ring (53.374 to 53.926) and the 'no installation named' tag (54.202 to 54.708) all play on that small card. The plan is sound, but the limit image is the one most at risk at phone size. Check that the ring and the tag read at 270 px.\"},\"sha256\":\"ae07cc3e9cd5115efea4a2c1dc104cf6cc86d24fe8f2562481ce8c5881a59382\"}},\"schema\":\"dispatch_verified_code_plan_context/1\",\"scope\":\"Current code-plan passes only. They provide no phone observation, selection or film approval.\"},\"verified_code_source_inventory\":[{\"bytes\":35659,\"path\":\"video-engine/src/Dispatch.tsx\",\"sha256\":\"482b10e0d23c8f5bed626d8d62e92056ab9bfe7cc77a328ce7126ceea7bece1f\"},{\"bytes\":1168,\"path\":\"video-engine/src/branding/DocketMark.tsx\",\"sha256\":\"1711186b55d89308069607d749a38a9c8740b6c6dbca433430b5f4cfc8188019\"},{\"bytes\":4301,\"path\":\"video-engine/src/lib/DispatchOverlays.tsx\",\"sha256\":\"cf2f2ad89339249d312d5ea157c4097462a6485fa758b31d1c4ffab2a80d51a2\"},{\"bytes\":3503,\"path\":\"video-engine/src/lib/artDirection.tsx\",\"sha256\":\"e3baef95838476732079875b9d922195be4b421ae9b2d8bcf08480f6b98ab5c6\"},{\"bytes\":3214,\"path\":\"video-engine/src/lib/cinema/CinematicStage.tsx\",\"sha256\":\"af1001e96075fc4358426f01ef5dcf0d6d338df2a23493c4c253562ed680f9b2\"},{\"bytes\":716,\"path\":\"video-engine/src/lib/cinema/ProofContext.tsx\",\"sha256\":\"07079c7ba2ac11926032acc2ac7b55c2e23e74db86a70a605f88e74d0aea81f0\"},