ps performing board events on the film clock.\",\"47\":\"From the street the housing window glows as readings arrive; wide, a dashed central server far off stays dark with no line to the station.\",\"49\":\"The dashboard assesses risk levels and shows how flooding could spread across monitored locations, highlighting higher-risk zones so local officials can act quickly.\",\"5\":\"These low-power signals can travel more than a half-mile through city streets and up to five miles in open areas without needing cell towers or power lines. The data arrives instantly at a local central hub, where emergency teams can monitor conditions from miles away.\",\"50\":\"Our system is an off-grid solution. It generates its own power, evaluates flood risk locally right on the device and sends timely warnings without needing external electricity or expensive network lines.\",\"51\":\"The validation bar fills across its card and the university's reported figure appears and holds. An initial assessments after training tag pins under the validation card. The blank field result card slides in at the edge, beside the validation card.\",\"52\":\"At the central monitoring site, custom server software aggregates data from multiple deployed nodes across a town or watershed.\",\"53\":\"A second, larger AI model analyzes spatial and temporal patterns across the network to generate an interactive web dashboard with predictive maps.\",\"54\":\"Readings run in along thin traces from the four lenses and four weather sensors to one small chip, which begins to glow. The chip lights the amber risk lamp on the board and a judged on the station tag pins. Far from the station a dashed outline of a central server draws itself and stays dark, with no line running to it.\",\"55\":\"Brown water tops the limestone curb, spreads across a San Antonio yard with no station in it and climbs a chain link post to its orange ankle mark.\",\"56\":\"A disclosed design detail with no yard around it: brown water climbs o