g pins beside its housing.\",\"89\":\"https://news.utsa.edu/2026/09/ut-san-antonio-researcher-builds-self-powered-smart-warning-system-to-catch-local-floods-before-disaster-strikes/\",\"9\":[{\"id\":\"s5-halfmile\",\"kind\":\"applicationRecord\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"more than a half mile tag through city streets\"},\"scale\":1,\"x\":540,\"y\":900}],\"90\":\"Researchers at The University of Texas at San Antonio have developed a self-sustaining, artificial intelligence-powered flood warning system designed to spot dangerous water accumulation at the street level.\",\"91\":\"On the same ankle height the picture cuts to a San Antonio yard with no station in it, the water spreading past the orange ankle mark on a chain link post as the view pulls back.\"}}",
