                "one_viewing_summary": "Planned chain, not observed pixels. A lens goes under water, and the same ankle-high water fills a yard while the porch phone stays dark until a late banner. The prototype station is craned down, charges from the sun and sends no line to a tower. Its four lenses get wet in turn and the weather lamps light. Readings run to the chip, which lights a local risk lamp while a central server stays dark. Radio rings cross the map, pass a half-mile tag and reach a hub mast five miles out. The hub map spreads flood paths and a responder's forearm settles beside the screen. Then come the limits: a reported validation figure tagged as initial assessments, a blank field-result card stamped none reported, a fence map with no pin, and a dashed goal pin that never lands.",
