for voice, masking, sync and motivated sound. Never infer a listening verdict from captions.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"review_rule\\\": \\\"Ground blocking findings in a timed observed defect and its effect on comprehension or finish. Distinguish uncertainty and optional preferences without weakening mandatory standards. Readable evidence and completed-result holds are judged for their purpose; continuous motion alone earns no approval. A weakest interval is required even for a passing film. A preference for another style is not itself a blocking defect. Existing rubric hard fails, cinematic requirements and source limits remain mandatory.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"config/source_validation_completion_v1.json\":\"{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"dispatch_source_validation_completion/1\\\",\\n  \\\"effective_date\\\": \\\"2026-10-15\\\",\\n  \\\"authorization_source_label\\\": \\\"Standing owner mandatory source, caption and audio completion instruction from October 3rd and October 16th, 2026\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": \\\"A charged independent source-pivot rejection requires a source-backed script correction and fresh source validation; mixed artistic blockers remain blocking and retain standard repair accounting\\\",\\n  \\\"minimum_remaining\\\": {\\\"validator_agents\\\": 1, \\\"storyboard_critics\\\": 4, \\\"tts_calls\\\": 2},\\n  \\\"invariants\\\": [\\n    \\\"Retain the original frozen allocation, every charge, exact rejection and original classification.\\\",\\n    \\\"Require the actual independent source-pivot diagnosis, charged reservation, current source closure and exact proposed script.\\\",\\n    \\\"Adopt this amendment separately and grant only complete remaining-path deficits.\\\",\\n    \\\"Precharge the fresh Opus High validator and bind its actual PASS to the current script and claims before dependent production.\\\",\\n    \\\"Renew the same two treatments when their authored concept changes; retain all old comparisons.\\\",\\n    \\\"No source, rights, action, native PNG/CRF16, audio, caption, scoring or shipment gate is waived.\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\",\"config/story_art.json\":\"{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"dispatch-story-art-policy/1\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"fresh-story-art-v1\\\",\\n  \\\"effective_date\\\": \\\"2026-10-08\\\",\\n  \\\"tool\\\": \\\"built-in ImageGen\\\",\\n  \\\"min_images\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"max_images\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"roles\\\": [\\\"hero\\\", \\\"support\\\"],\\n  \\\"min_long_edge\\\": 1024,\\n  \\\"note\\\": \\\"Generate two fresh relevant images per edition before animation: a finished hero and supporting prop atlas or purposeful environment. Share these new assets across exactly two treatments. Native overlays own exact facts and captions. Generated illustrations are disclosed and never treated as observational evidence. Charge every attempt, including rejected assets.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"config/story_visuals.json\":\"{\\n  \\\"effective_date\\\": \\\"2026-09-29\\\",\\n  \\\"max_searches\\\": 6,\\n  \\\"max_candidates\\\": 8\\n}\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/ART_DIRECTION.md\":\"# Direct a world before building a scene\\n\\nTeaching sources: [Pixar's cinematography account](https://renderman.pixar.com/stories/incredible-cinematography)\\nfor coordinated staging, light and camera; [OpenAI evaluation practices](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/evaluation-best-practices)\\nfor reference calibration, pairwise comparison and order bias. Current filmed evidence decides\\nwhich choices work here.\\n\\nRead this with the viewer method, selected approach dossier, fixed quality contract and\\ncurrent rubric. It adds executable craft inputs and calibration, not a score, quota,\\nnew judge or extra paid attempt. Existing source, rights, action, native, audio, captions,\\ncumulative resources, finite artistic recovery and shipment requirements continue.\\n\\n## Director\\n\\nBefore coding, choose the visual approach from actual source access. Think through four\\nlenses in the existing director assignment: the comedian finds an observable mismatch;\\nthe dramatist finds pressure and a changed state; the explainer finds the causal relation;\\nthe enthusiast finds a specific surprising detail. Do not invent a joke, conflict or\\noutcome. Choose exactly two complete treatments within the current comparison allowance.\\n\\nWrite `art_direction` in each board using `config/art_direction.json`. Explain seven palette\\nroles, contrasting shapes, the recognizable hero silhouette and its finish, motivated\\nlight, focal hierarchy, action timing, and one signature shot tied to an actual event.\\nName the current asset and actual subject ids. Use the source image itself when it is the\\nhero. Give a dimensional scene a `shots[scene_id]` camera position, target, lens and reason;\\nan event-bound `to` pose is optional. For the illustrated carton route, use `flat_shots`\\nwith native-coordinate offsets, scale and a reason. Numeric shot choices must be executed\\nby the routed scene, not left as board prose. A custom renderer must consume the same\\nprofile or explain its retained source lighting and implement its relevant choices.\\n\\nThe focal object stays sharp. Depth blur must arise from actual separation and preserve\\ncontact detail. Never add blur, floating shapes, lens flares, camera kicks or orbiting as\\nautomatic cinematic decoration. Hold the camera while an object performs. Move it to reveal\\na relation or follow a finite action. Give a completed result a comprehension hold.\\n\\n## Scene builder and render owner\\n\\nUse `prompts/roles/scene-builder.md` in the existing code assignment. Build the finished\\nhero first, then light and stage it before extending the scene. Recognizable geometry,\\nedges, seams, hardware, texture and grounded shadows beat a field of placeholder primitives.\\nAuthored 2.5D, useful footage and a readable source image can outperform complicated 3D.\\nDo not restrict the daily story to the demonstration subject or copy reference b-roll.\\n\\nThe shared `ArtDirectionProvider` carries current choices in both entry points. Three.js\\n`CinematicStage`/`Studio` execute the light recipe and exposure. `directedShot` executes\\nauthored event-bound cameras. The illustrated carton component executes its flat framing,\\nfinished surfaces, occlusion and contact assemblies. Source footage retains original speed\\nand practical lighting. Existing boards without this profile retain their original defaults.\\n\\nEvery new event specifies a motion curve within its existing measured window: `travel`\\naccelerates and brakes; `contact` approaches and settles; `linear` serves constant-speed\\nmovement; `smoothstep` is available for a justified gentle transition. `anticipation` and\\n`settle` reserve fractions inside that window, never new runtime or voice stretching.\\n`landing` has a small overshoot and needs a free-prop reason; never use it for a constrained\\ncontact, a foot planted on ground, or a source-implied machine limit. Check music and foley\\nagainst the executed contact, not the old curve. No incidental sway substitutes for action.\\n\\nJudge motion at the delivered 30 fps. A regular frame clock does not excuse abrupt starts,\\nfast screen-space travel or repeated stop-and-go strokes. Directed `travel` and `contact`\\ncurves start and finish with zero velocity and acceleration. Give a heavy load enough of\\nthe existing scene window to accelerate and brake. Holds consume that window; do not squeeze\\nthe entire stroke into the remaining few frames. Inspect velocity at event joins as well\\nas the start and end. Keep a clear contact view and a stable camera when tracking amplifies\\nthe load's movement. Do not conceal stepping with blur, frame interpolation or faster audio.\\nAn event-bound moving camera uses `travel` or `contact`; the input check refuses constant-speed\\nstarts and landing overshoot on a camera. Hold it when the object needs a different curve.\\n\\nWhen two named events describe successive stages of one uninterrupted movement, author\\nadjacent windows with no interior anticipation or settle, then explicitly use\\n`joinedActionWindow`. The helper rejects gaps, scene boundaries and erased rests. The\\nillustrated carton route consumes `continuous_withdrawal_event_ids` only in its withdrawal\\nscene. Retiming a movement keeps the source relation, scene runtime and measured captions.\\n\\n## Existing independent critic and three scorers\\n\\nWatch the actual muted sequence first. Name the object, action, changed state and answered\\nquestion before reading the profile. Then test whether its choices are visible: compare\\nsilhouette, contact, surface finish, hierarchy, framing, rhythm and hold at phone size and\\nnative crop scale. Inspect the beginning, contact and end of every action. Keep narration\\nand labels covered on the first pass. A good explanation in the profile cannot clear an\\noccluded grip, generic slab, unrecognizable subject or absent transformation.\\n\\nWatch uninterrupted playback at normal speed. Check for velocity jumps, stop-and-go camera\\ntracking, repeated frames during movement and excessively large per-frame displacement.\\nSeparate deliberate shot cuts and completed holds from a continuous stroke that stutters.\\nRecord the exact interval and affected object or camera. Smooth motion is a visible property,\\nnot a consequence of a passing score or a high frame rate.\\n\\nRead `knowledge/craft/cinematic_reference_bank.json`. Its frozen passages teach specific\\ndecisions; their old scores use different rubrics and are not comparable ratings. They are\\nreferences, never production assets or current approval. Compare two current complete cuts,\\ndescribe a preference with exact times, then record mandatory defects under the existing\\ncriteria. A different palette preference alone does not create another correction. Retain\\nall original rejections. At the configured artistic boundary, finish the strongest credible\\ncut; source, comprehension and technical failures still take the mandatory recovery route.\\n\\n## Learn from shipped and failed footage\\n\\n`scripts/cinematic_learning.py` records the next five editions from the policy's effective\\ndate, including unfinished editions, first-panel success, scores, all actual resource usage,\\nprovider tokens, elapsed time, correction counts and artistic deferrals. Unknown account\\ntokens remain null. Do not claim future results or a numerical improvement multiplier.\\n\\nAfter durable shipment, refresh the report and the recurring-defect packet from the last\\nfourteen days. At most once per seven days, give the existing builder a fresh compact packet:\\nup to five recurring findings, exact rejected evidence and one proposed shared capability.\\nReproduce the failed interval; add a useful regression; prove the correction inside the next\\nedition's already reserved two-treatment comparison. Mark the actual advance or honest skip\\nin the packet. This is one shared engineering advance, not five new stylistic attempts.\\nFund the entire remaining production/review/delivery path before changing the renderer.\\nDo not delay an accepted cut for optional engineering or add roles, reviews or resource grants.\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/AUTHORED_STORY_ART.md\":\"# Fresh authored story pictures\\n\\nThe owner selected this Claude substitute on October 9th, 2026. It applies only to a board with\\n`story_art.version` set to `authored-story-art-v1` and runtime `claude-sonnet-v1`. Older boards\\ncontinue to use their original raster ImageGen policy. The finished-art, modern engagement and\\nindependent rendered observations remain unchanged.\\n\\nCreate two original story-specific source groups, hero and support, in\\n`video-engine/src/modern/episodes/<edition-id>/`. Use source-bound physical actions to choose the\\nforms. Design recognizable silhouettes, purposeful surface detail, coherent perspective and\\nlighting, grounded weight and contact, and a performed answer. Use the current regional stage.\\nShared primitives can support the work; a renamed old hero or untouched decorative module is not\\nfresh story artwork. No previous edition's footage or generated art becomes this edition's hero.\\n\\nThe board's `story_art` plan has `version`, `runtime`, `edition_id`, exactly two `requests` and\\nexactly two recorded `entries`. Each request declares `id`, `role`, source `file`, named `export`,\\n`scene_ids`, the directed `prompt`, `purpose`, `source_limit` and concrete `action_uses`. An action\\nuse declares `scene_id`, `event_id`, `view`, `action_id` and `subject_ids`. Bind each to the actual\\nscene event, directed shot and registry narration view. Register the two files in the episode's\\n`assets` and its `authored_art` rows, each with `role`, `module`, `export` and implemented `views`.\\nUse those exports in the episode's actual source. Keep the full renderer closure hash-bound.\\n\\nReserve the existing builder reboard before authoring either group. That one actual worker can\\ncreate both source groups; it is not two external image calls. Do not consume `image_generations`\\nor invent generation ids, image sizes, PNG source files or image-service charges. Record actual\\nsource file creation times, exact bytes, unique creation identities, current claims and the prior\\nbuilder reservation through the helper. It retains original modules and receipts in scratch;\\nlater corrections must retain those actual failures and cumulative charges.\\n\\n```sh\\npython scripts/authored_story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json record --state out/dispatch/run_state.json\\npython scripts/authored_story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json verify\\npython scripts/story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json stage\\n```\\n\\nShare the two source groups across exactly two complete treatments. Both phone films execute the\\ndeclared actions. Before narration inspect their actual pictures with labels covered, identify\\nthe principal subject and result, and select the stronger chain. A module, export, receipt or\\naction id proves a binding only. The existing critic, native hero review, three audiovisual\\nlenses and three final scorers judge the current pixels and audible performance. Reject unused\\ndecoration, generic boxes, static slideshow sequences and ambiguous physical contact.\\n\\nPreserve the current caption, source, rights, timing, modern engagement, native PNG/CRF16 and\\nshipment gates. The substitute changes the artwork's origin, not the finished film standard.\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/AUTONOMOUS_COMPLETION.md\":\"# Autonomous completion capacity\\n\\nEffective October 3rd, 2026. The owner prohibits ending an autonomous Dispatch run at an internal resource ceiling or host review capacity error. Done means an accepted shipped video, deployed permanent bytes, canonical phone playback and the verified correctly addressed unsent Gmail draft.\\n\\nThis standing instruction authorizes the mandatory completion capacity policy in config/autonomous_completion.json. Preserve each run's original frozen envelope and every cumulative charge. Record necessary completion increments as separate evidence-bound controller events. Never reset usage or treat a grant as picture, score or shipment approval.\\n\\nBefore a correction, consolidate exact independent failures, preserve the strongest complete cut and run production-budget with its repair plan. A failed minimum action or held-slide treatment has no finish-current route. Use the independent source-backed pivot and the controller completion-capacity command to fund the complete remaining code, silent phone, final timed phone, native hero, final audiovisual, scorer and delivery path before paid work. Reserve every attempt first.\\n\\nThe creative cap still ends optional polish. Mandatory minimum action, factual, source, rights, legibility, comprehension, audio, captions, runtime and release integrity failures require autonomous correction. A standing grant funds only this completion work. It does not authorize duplicate research, speculative rigs, extra treatment shopping or a new edition that hides an unfinished one.\\n\\nFor an actual unavailable host, preserve the observed transport error and follow prompts/phases/review-availability.md through the configured independent provider with the same role, guides and fixed rubric. A resource deficit is not a transport error. Keep all three final audiovisual lenses and three separate independent scorers.\\n\\nAfter normal or bounded creative release authorization, stop creative editing and finish exact-head CI, merges, deployment, permanent byte verification, canonical phone playback and unsent draft readback. Retain real rejected verdicts and scores. Neither a preview, checkpoint, resource boundary nor a local publishable package ends production. Never send email or post socially.\\n\\nThis dated owner instruction overrides older text that made an internal exhausted envelope an approval stop. The original envelope remains an accounting baseline, and audited standing completion increments are its authorized exception.\\n\\n## Independently classified technical failures\\n\\nThe existing `retained-integrity` route also covers an actual paid voice take that passes an\\nearlier soundcheck but fails strict alignment. It requires a fresh independent REVISE and a\\ncomplete one-to-one `technical_repair.findings` classification of the exact current findings.\\nThe allowed categories include `technical_audio`, `captions` and `runtime`; the critic must\\nsupport its actual classification. A director-written Markdown finding or a previous pivot\\nPASS cannot substitute for that response. Keep all original responses and charged attempts.\\n\\nUse `repair_scope: technical-integrity` with the actual independent report and retained\\nchanged-input baselines. This admission precedes the film-hash branch in the controller and\\ncan fund required correction before a finished film exists. It adds only actual complete-path\\ndeficits, including a replacement take and soundcheck. If authored event changes invalidate\\nthe retained comparison, include `capture_completion_budget.py` for those same two treatments\\nbefore correction. Every actual attempt still needs its own reservation. Independent\\nclassification approves no sound, caption, film, score or shipment and cannot waive a gate.\\n\\nFor a required source-backed script pivot, the separate dated\\nconfig/source_validation_completion_v1.json adds one necessary validator to the complete\\nremaining path. The original policy bytes, frozen allocation, every original classification\\nand every actual charge remain unchanged. Use validation_completion.py to bind the actual\\ncharged independent report, current source closure and exact proposed script, then include\\nthe retained same-treatment comparison through capture_completion_budget.py before the grant.\\nThe new mandatory-source-pivot route keeps mixed source and artistic blockers under standard\\nrepair accounting; every blocker stays blocking. It does not reclassify a finding, defer a\\nmodern-film requirement or approve the rejected admission proposal. A fully classified\\ntechnical plan retains its existing stricter route. Fresh source validation is required even if existing capacity makes\\nthe increment zero. Its actual precharged Opus High PASS must bind the current script and\\nclaims before any dependent paid production. See the executable source-pivot sequence in\\nprompts/phases/repair.md. This capacity is not review, source or film approval.\\n\\n## Current modern-film editions\\n\\nFrom October 8th, initialization adopts config/autonomous_completion_v2.json. The earlier policy\\nand its exact retained bytes stay valid for historical ledgers. The current complete remaining\\npath includes necessary fresh ImageGen story art. An independent exact-film failed modern\\nengagement or finish observation admits modern-film-floor recovery. Retain original resource\\nallocation, failed cut, actual observations and cumulative charges. No capacity event approves\\nartwork or restores a legacy renderer. Optional polish stops; the mandatory current floor is\\nrepaired through the existing source-backed completion path.\\n\\n## Mandatory code defects before a film exists\\n\\nThe October 9th Claude pilot exposed a dead end before voice. Its independent code critic\\nrejected a missing narrated chart and an unreadable ending, but capacity admission required a\\nfilm hash. From October 9th, config/autonomous_completion_v3.json adds a separate code-evidence\\namendment for current unfinished production. It preserves the original adoption and policy bytes.\\n\\nRetain the exact independent code rejection and the before-files in the repair plan. Use\\nscripts/autonomous_completion.py --prepare-code-plan with that plan, the current claims and a\\nnew output path. It verifies current board, renderer, claims and baseline hashes without editing\\nthe original report or plan. Run production-budget and completion-capacity on the new plan\\nbefore begin-repair or a correction. The grant funds the conservative complete remaining path.\\nEvery actual worker and render still needs its own reservation. An unused earlier reservation\\nremains charged. Code evidence never approves pixels, a score or shipment. Both complete phone\\ntreatments, all modern observations, native, sound, captions and delivery gates still run.\\nOptional polish, stale inputs, self-review and extra research remain ineligible.\\n\\nAfter the independent code review passes, stop optional editing. If charged review failures have\\nconsumed the protected capacity, retain those failures and use a new finish-current plan bound to\\nthe actual fresh independent passing report, with no changed_inputs. Do not reuse an earlier\\nfailed attempt's grant. On the adopted code route, the finish budget protects two pending phone\\ncritics: the silent two-treatment comparison and the final measured timed phone. Run\\nproduction-budget and completion-capacity on that finish plan; any real deficit becomes a\\nseparate existing mandatory_completion_grant. Keep the original grant, envelope and all charges.\\nThis grants no review approval and never replaces either film review.\\n\\n## Incomplete independent code coverage\\n\\nIf a returned code critic's own retained handback discloses unread mandatory guides or incomplete\\nboards, retain the entire original handback and its actual limits. A partial pass authorizes no\\ncapture. The October 10th coverage amendment, config/autonomous_completion_coverage_v1.json,\\nfunds completion of that same assignment on unchanged production inputs. It is a separate\\nadoption and capacity event; the original policy, envelope and every charge remain intact.\\n\\nCreate a receipt with schema dispatch_review_coverage/1, the actual run_id and agent_id, role\\ncode, status completed, model claude-opus-5-5, effort high, provider_unavailable false and action\\nSendMessage_same_id. Include director_identity, the original reviewer's exact reviewer_identity,\\nreport_sha256, reservation_event_index and reservation_sha256 (canonical JSON of that original\\nreserved event), reported_limits copied verbatim from the independent handback, and missing_inputs\\nwith each original packet path, sha256 and read_complete false. Do not invent a disclosure.\\n\\nGenerate a fresh current code packet with both complete treatments and the measured board.\\nRetain the original packet unchanged. Bind and precheck with:\\n\\n```sh\\npython scripts/review_coverage.py --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --receipt <actual-receipt> --report <original-handback> --original-packet <original-packet> --current-packet <current-packet> --output <new-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py production-budget --repair-plan <new-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py completion-capacity --repair-plan <new-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py production-budget --repair-plan <new-plan>\\n```\\n\\nUse the environment wrapper for these commands. The coverage path requires one complete resumed\\ncode review plus the separate silent comparison and final timed phone reviews, with the complete\\nnative, audiovisual, scoring and delivery reserve. It requests no reboard, artwork generation or\\nproduction edit. Every actual resumed review is charged before SendMessage to the same Opus High\\nworker. Require every current mandatory guide and complete board to be read, and obtain the full\\ngate-ready handback with honest coverage. Neither the grant nor a disclosure approves a film.\\nReject a renamed duplicate grant, stale input, optional polish, self-review or provider switch.\\nClassify any remaining production defect independently under the current guides before its\\nseparate evidence-bound correction; the coverage path authorizes no correction.\\n\\n## Mandatory modern code floor before capture\\n\\nThe separate dated config/autonomous_completion_modern_code_v1.json amendment accepts an actual\\nindependent Opus High code rejection in the current motion, surface_finish, pacing or ending_artistry\\ncategories. It preserves their original classification. A renderer-only correction binds the\\ncomplete measured board and both complete treatments as read-only admission inputs, the complete\\nrenderer closure, current claims, current guide and policy bytes, and exact retained renderer\\nbaselines. It does not require changing the story merely to satisfy a funding schema.\\n\\nPrepare a new plan without overwriting the original proposal or independent report:\\n\\n```sh\\npython scripts/modern_code_recovery.py --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --plan <original-proposal> --packet <current-complete-code-packet> --output <new-bound-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py production-budget --repair-plan <new-bound-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py completion-capacity --repair-plan <new-bound-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py production-budget --repair-plan <new-bound-plan>\\n```\\n\\nUse scripts/run_with_env.sh with the active worktree's explicit internal cd. This records a\\nseparate adoption and exact capacity deficits, never review approval. It protects one charged\\nOpus corrective reboard and four independent critic calls: a source-backed recurrence pivot when\\nthe existing recurrence gate requires it, complete code rereview of all three current boards,\\nsilent comparison and final timed phone. Unused reserve is not a charge. Retain the full native,\\naudiovisual, three-scorer, narration and shipment path. Obtain any required independent pivot,\\nbind it into the new plan, then begin-repair and charge the actual reboard before the Opus builder.\\nThe pivot gate, all original policies, frozen allocation and spent evidence remain unchanged.\\n\\nAfter the source correction, use modern_code_recovery.rebound_board(plan, row) for each kind=board\\nrow in modern_code_evidence.inputs to refresh only the changed renderer's derived sha256 entries.\\nWrite those deterministic boards, preserving their prior exact bytes in the bound evidence.\\nAll narration, timing, actions, claims and artwork fields remain identical. Add only the actual\\nsource after_sha256 fields to the plan before authorize-repair. The controller refuses a changed\\nbound plan or any other board change. A source fix and bookkeeping rebind approve no pixels:\\nbind fresh packets and require the separate full code, silent phone and timed phone verdicts\\nbefore native production. Never replace a phone review with the code rejection or its grant.\\n\\n## Charged narration pivot recovery\\n\\nThe October 16th run exposed a missing path after a charged Opus High narration pivot returned\\nREVISE at the critic ceiling. For unfinished editions from October 15th, the separate pinned\\nconfig/autonomous_completion_narration_v1.json funds a properly precharged replacement review\\nand the conservative complete code, silent phone, timed phone, native, audiovisual, scoring and\\ndelivery path. It changes no original policy, envelope, charge or verdict. Fresh artwork is\\nnot requested by this capacity-only admission; existing relevant authored assets stay bound.\\n\\nPreserve the original full rejection, its actual reserved event, the complete original packet,\\nall referenced failed findings, audio, acoustic ASR and direction baselines. A director summary\\nis never the original handback. Build a dispatch_narration_pivot_recovery/1 receipt with actual\\nrun_id, director_identity, role recurrence-pivot, status completed, provider_unavailable false,\\nmodel claude-opus-5-5, effort high, actual agent_id and reviewer_identity. Bind report_sha256,\\nreservation_event_index, reservation_sha256 and the exact reservation_note. retained_inputs\\nlists path/sha256/kind references (failure, audio, asr, baseline and packet), including every\\nfailure hash named by the reviewer. Use canonical JSON for event hashes.\\n\\nEvery substantive review of a changed proposal is a new charged call, including SendMessage\\nto the same worker. Only mechanical format corrections on unchanged content are free.\\nIf an actual unreserved continuation has already occurred, keep its exact response, reviewed\\nproposal, actual time and disclosure unchanged. List it under unreserved_continuations with\\nagent_id, observed_at, precharged false, invalid_for_authorization true and path/sha256 objects\\nfor handback, proposal and disclosure. At most one such incident is admitted per charged\\nrejection. Account it once as a visibly LATE CHARGE; never backdate a reservation or present\\nthe old pass as a properly precharged review. An empty incidents list is valid.\\nIf an earlier candidate file was overwritten, first recover its actual checkpoint version.\\nIf its exact reviewed bytes remain unavailable, retain that explicit gap and bind the supported\\nrequest/handback and first durable proposal as limited context. Label reconstruction honestly;\\nit can document a late debit but cannot authorize work. The fresh charged review must inspect\\nthe complete retained current direction and current source evidence before production resumes.\\n\\n```sh\\npython scripts/narration_recovery.py --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --receipt <actual-receipt> --report <full-original-rejection> --output <new-capacity-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py production-budget --review-route host --repair-plan <new-capacity-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py completion-capacity --repair-plan <new-capacity-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py production-budget --review-route host --repair-plan <new-capacity-plan>\\npython scripts/narration_recovery.py --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --settle-unreserved <new-capacity-plan>\\n```\\n\\nUse the environment wrapper and explicit internal cd. Prepare grants no calls. Capacity records\\nonly exact deficits in a separate event. Do not begin-repair with this capacity-only plan.\\nValidate its protected allocation immediately after the grant, before debiting its obligations.\\nThe admission plan includes the late debit and replacement review. Rechecking that same snapshot\\nafter consuming them can count completed work again; it does not authorize a duplicate grant.\\nAfter --verify-review, use ordinary production-budget for the actual remaining production path.\\nFor a new mandatory failure, bind its own new evidence rather than reusing this admission.\\nRead escalation_ceiling and the replayed effective envelope when checking remaining calls;\\nthe limits field is the spend target, so a 9/9 target does not mean a recorded ceiling of 12 is gone.\\nAn already-funded path records a zero-increment capacity audit, without adding resources.\\nReserve the next actual critic before SendMessage to the same available Opus High worker.\\nAfter a supported fresh-host restore, retain the observed loss of the old task and start one\\nfresh isolated Opus High worker when that task cannot resume. This changes no provider or\\nprimary model. Retain the original receipt; a derived receipt may retarget only its file paths\\nfrom the saved checkout root to the restored root, verifying every unchanged file hash and\\nkeeping the original as provenance. Never alter the rejection, timings, charge or source data.\\nGive the reviewer the\\ncomplete current guides, exact rejected and current proposals, retained failures and current\\nsource bindings. It evaluates the proposed performance, without claiming to hear audio through\\nRead. Soundcheck and exact acoustic alignment still decide the actual take. Preserve an already\\ngenerated take once, even if it was generated after an invalid review; no fabricated precharge,\\ndiscarded spend or automatic replacement take is allowed.\\n\\nAfter a real independent PASS, create dispatch_precharged_narration_review/1 with run_id,\\ngrant_event_index/grant_sha256, reservation_event_index/reservation_sha256, actual model/effort,\\nagent_id, reviewer_identity, provider_unavailable false, started_at/completed_at, current\\ndirection_sha256, report_sha256 and mechanism_id. Times describe this actual new content call,\\nnot the worker's original lifetime. The reservation must precede it and cannot be a late debit.\\n\\n```sh\\npython scripts/narration_recovery.py --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --verify-review <new-capacity-plan> --receipt <actual-new-call-receipt> --report <unchanged-new-pass>\\n```\\n\\nDependent paid work remains refused until that verification and all actual unreserved work is\\naccounted. A later actual charged REVISE can admit a new bound scope; require a pass on the\\ncurrent proposal while preserving the retired proposal's rejection. The record approves no recorded\\nspeech, film or shipment. Keep all actual caption, timing, source, rights, current artwork,\\nnative PNG/CRF16, three independent scores and delivery gates. A later REVISE stays a rejection;\\nuse its own actual precharged evidence for the next mandatory recovery. Never ask the owner to\\napprove an internal ceiling, label a ceiling as host unavailability or substitute a new edition.\\n\\n## Actual recurrence pivot rejection recovery\\n\\nconfig/autonomous_completion_pivot_v1.json is a separate dated amendment for a charged independent\\nOpus High recurrence pivot that returns REVISE before an already funded mandatory modern code\\ncorrection. Keep the original source rejection, modern grant, original frozen allocation and every\\ncharge. It funds exact remaining deficits for the next pivot, code review and both phone reviews,\\nplus the complete native, audiovisual, scoring and shipment path. It never approves a pivot.\\n\\nWrite a supported-host receipt with schema dispatch_pivot_recovery/1, actual run_id, role\\nrecurrence-pivot, status completed, provider_unavailable false, model claude-opus-5-5, effort high,\\naction SendMessage_same_id and the actual agent_id. Record the source_grant_event_index and\\nsource_grant_sha256 of the original mandatory-modern-code grant, reservation_event_index and\\nreservation_sha256 of the failed pivot's actual reserved event. Hash events with\\nautonomous_completion.sha(autonomous_completion.canonical(event)). Include report_sha256,\\nreviewer_identity and reported_rejection copied exactly from the returned visible_difference.\\nKeep the complete exact pivot report and exact proposal it reviewed. The bound revised plan must\\nchange the proposed performed correction, while preserving the modern grant's read-only production\\ninputs, renderer baselines, resource request and failure family. Do not relabel a repeated family.\\n\\n```sh\\npython scripts/pivot_recovery.py --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --receipt <actual-receipt> --report <retained-pivot-rejection> --rejected-proposal <reviewed-proposal> --revised-plan <bound-modern-plan> --output <new-recovery-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py production-budget --repair-plan <new-recovery-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py completion-capacity --repair-plan <new-recovery-plan>\\npython scripts/run_controller.py production-budget --repair-plan <new-recovery-plan>\\n```\\n\\nUse scripts/run_with_env.sh with explicit internal cd. The controller records a separate pinned\\nadoption and only actual deficits, once per failed charged pivot reservation. No new reboard is\\nadded when the original correction remains funded. Reserve the next real pivot call first and\\nSendMessage to the same Opus High worker with full current guides, all relevant retained failures,\\nthe revised proposal and current source bindings. Preserve its actual response. An independent\\nsource-backed PASS must bind pivot_review before begin-repair. Then charge the existing corrective\\nreboard, use the existing Opus builder, and follow the same strict renderer-hash-only board rebind\\nand authorize-repair path above. Both fresh phone reviews and all shipment gates remain required.\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/BOUNDED_CREATIVE_RELEASE.md\":\"# Finite creative repair and autonomous shipment\\n\\nOwner instruction from October 3rd, 2026. Read knowledge/craft/AUTONOMOUS_COMPLETION.md before applying older resource-boundary language below. Internal review ceilings and host capacity errors trigger autonomous mandatory completion recovery, never an approval stop or an unfinished-capacity final response. Preserve exact failures, the original frozen envelope and cumulative charges. Only accepted finish --result shipped completes production.\\n\\nEffective September 29, 2026. The owner requires a shipped video and prohibits stopping for\\ncreative approval. The default limit is three creative repair rounds. Before September 30, each charged\\n`reboards` unit counts; later editions use the independently classified accounting below. Also stop optional creative\\nrepair earlier after at least one repair and three critic calls when the effective frozen\\ncritic ceiling has fewer than three calls left for another complete correction path. This\\nprotects the final timed-phone review. The controller never resets or silently expands usage.\\n\\nAt that boundary, preserve the strongest reviewed complete cut and finish voice, measured\\ncaptions, native hero, final render, every independent audiovisual lens and the three scorers.\\nDo not start another aesthetic reboard. Correct retained factual or technical failures within\\nthe recorded resources; do not reinterpret them as artistic or declare an incomplete delivery\\nshipped. Preserve real access/resource failures and continue the executable completion work.\\n\\nThe rubric, score and original pass/revise values remain unchanged. Only motion, surface\\nfinish, pacing polish, ending artistry and style can be deferred. Source accuracy, rights,\\nreadability, comprehension and misleading implications cannot. Native picture occupancy,\\ncurrent renderer/film hashes, actual audible access, observation coverage, audio measurements,\\ncaption alignment and every delivery gate continue to run. A missing review is never an\\nartistic defect. Structural motion-floor failures retain their original failed reports; native\\nproof retains measured failures in `bounded_creative_findings`.\\n\\nAn independent critic can classify an existing exact rejected report in a separate sidecar:\\n\\n```sh\\npython scripts/creative_release.py --template --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json --report out/dispatch/phone-critic-current.json --film out/dispatch/openings/b.mp4 --scope phone\\npython scripts/creative_release.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json --report out/dispatch/phone-critic-current.json --scope phone\\n```\\n\\nThe first command produces a deliberately unapproved template under `creative-assessments`.\\nOnly the original independent reviewer fills its observations and categories after examining\\nthe retained evidence. Bind a preserved film/report path that later retiming cannot overwrite.\\nEvery exact original blocker and failed phone observation must be classified once; unknown or\\nnon-artistic categories refuse release. Retained checks need affirmative observed evidence.\\nThe assessment binds the original report bytes, film, source claims and creative concept.\\nKeep all original reports untouched. Changes to source, concept or film need current evidence.\\n\\nNew provider/scorer responses include an honest `bounded_release` classification in their\\ninitial immutable response. Obtain all lenses even if the first rejects. The audiovisual tool\\nadds the classification prompt; scorers read this policy and the same schema helper. A rejected\\nphone/AV report without concrete defects cannot use a score-only claim. A below-bar panel may\\nuse score-only classification only when it has no separate rejected attention criterion.\\n\\n`finish --result publishable` records the distinct publication mode and original failures in\\ncontroller `bounded_release`; it leaves production active in publishing. The final report card\\nstill carries its genuine score, `ship` value and hard fails. Delivery copies assessments and\\ntheir exact rejected evidence. A passing later panel does not conceal earlier artistic\\ndeferrals. `first_panel` success stays false if the panel actually failed.\\n\\nCompletion still requires exact-head CI, merge, deployment, permanent reviewed media bytes,\\ncanonical phone playback through Computer Use, and a correctly addressed unsent Gmail draft\\nwith readback. Only `finish --result shipped` completes production. No approval question or\\nnew paid review is needed merely to classify retained evidence in the existing review scope.\\n\\n## Accounting and quality correction from September 30, 2026\\n\\nThe three-round cap counts creative corrections. Technical repairs still consume the same\\ncharged reboards, critic calls and frozen resources, but a predeclared technical-integrity\\nscope does not spend a creative round. The full-path headroom brake still counts all work;\\nthis distinction adds no allowance. Historical editions retain their original accounting.\\n\\nBefore begin-repair, the existing independent critic's exact failure report must include\\ntechnical_repair.findings. Each row contains the exact original finding and one category:\\nsource, rights, legibility, layout, technical_audio, captions or runtime. Every original\\nfinding must be covered exactly once, by a reviewer distinct from the director. Motion,\\npacing, story and style remain creative. Set repair_scope to technical-integrity in the plan.\\nIts evidence hash and scope are fixed before edits and checked again at authorization.\\nOnly one reboard per such batch is excluded from creative count; all other charges count.\\n\\nThe finite rule ends optional polish on a credible treatment. It cannot waive a held-slide\\nstructural motion failure or a failed dominant-action observation in new editions.\\nThe known whole-film editorial-v1 screenshot/box treatment and repeated cut directions\\nare rejected before spending. Use the accepted complete preview as the finishing baseline.\\nIf the initial comparison fails, change the mechanism promptly within the reserved path;\\ndo not spend the remaining budget classifying the same wholesale failure as optional polish.\\nKeep the original score and rejection when a genuinely limited artistic shortfall is released.\\nNever ask for creative approval, reset usage, or claim shipment before its real evidence.\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/CREATIVE_DIRECTION.md\":\"# Story-led cinematic direction\\n\\nEffective September 29, 2026; config/creative_production.json owns the date and version.\\nEarlier editions retain their original contracts. This policy replaces the dimensional opening\\nand runtime quota. All source, quality, independent review, native output, audio, caption,\\nbudget and shipment requirements remain. It adds no score threshold or review role.\\n\\n## Visual storytelling correction from October 2nd, 2026\\n\\nRead [the visual-storytelling selector](visual-storytelling/README.md) and the selected approach\\ndossier in full before boarding. Choose observed documentary, explanatory animation,\\nevidence-led imagery or a cinematic scene from the source-backed action and available assets.\\nVariety is a tie-breaker between suitable approaches, not a weekday quota.\\n\\nFor newly planned editions from October 3rd, also read the [viewer planning method](visual-storytelling/viewer-plan.md).\\nChoose News report, Educational explainer or Cinematic scene as a format, then name the primary\\napproach in medium_choice. Record why it fits the inspected assets, the plausible alternative,\\nlikely false inference and information sequence in the existing creative-direction, scene and\\ntransition fields. For a report read [news-reporting.md](visual-storytelling/news-reporting.md)\\nand choose its structure from the sourced action. A format is not a mandatory presenter or\\nfixed rundown. A chosen guide is not a new quality criterion or approval field.\\n\\nComplete the [sentence-to-shot worksheet](visual-storytelling/sentence-to-shot.md) in existing\\ncreative-direction notes and the compact critic packet. Give each spoken clause a recognizable\\npictured subject, visible relationship or action, inspectable result, source limit and connection\\nto the next shot. Do not add a new board schema, scoring weight, reviewer or render reservation.\\n\\nThe existing phone critic identifies the pictured input, action and result from the actual preview\\nbefore reading the director's explanation. Then it compares those observations with the spoken\\nclauses. A moving source-related prop is insufficient if a viewer can't recognize what it\\nrepresents. Missing or contradictory explanation stays a comprehension/source defect under the\\ncurrent contract; decorative motion can't turn it into a deferrable style issue.\\n\\nRetain the same two-treatment batch, frozen budget, native hero, independent reviews and\\nbounded-release route. The [October 2nd pavement diagnosis](visual-storytelling/october-2-pavement-case.md)\\nis a sampled-frame case study, not a replacement verdict or permission to alter the shipped film.\\n\\n## Treatment recovery from September 30, 2026\\n\\nSeptember 29 is a rejected creative reference. Its source screenshots, repeated fading boxes\\nand growing underlines never became an engaging film. Use the source to discover a physical\\ntask, obstacle and consequence. Preserve that action in the script and pictures. Authentic\\nimagery earns a shot when it reveals something; a relevant document is not automatically\\nthe film's subject. Original source-grounded illustration and demonstrated action remain\\nfirst-class choices. Reuse proven components, never prior-edition photographic assets.\\n\\nStart with one credible demonstrated treatment and one genuinely different visual treatment.\\nCompare their action, composition and viewer payoff in the existing batch. If both fail,\\nuse one consolidated mechanism-changing simplification before narration; do not keep tuning\\nthe same weak presentation. Preserve the strongest accepted complete preview as the fallback.\\nNo extra research pass, reviewer role, third speculative concept or bespoke rig is authorized.\\n\\nThe existing critic must judge the whole film against the prior successful visual standard.\\nNamed cities, correct labels and readable source text do not establish strong picture or place.\\nA code pass for geometry and provenance does not establish an engaging treatment. Inspect\\nthe opening, middle and ending as actual action before refining layout. Give each cut its own\\nvisible reason; repeated prose cannot direct ten different shots.\\n\\n## Choose the story from its tangible stakes\\n\\nBefore narration, selected.visual_stakes records affected_person, physical_subject,\\nvisible_change, consequence, opening_question, answer, asset_fit and source_urls. Name the\\nspecific worker, resident or group and what changes for them. Tie the opening question to the\\nanswer that the available evidence can support. A large announcement without useful pictures\\nis a weaker candidate than a smaller action with a visible consequence.\\n\\nInspect the real site, equipment, people, workflow and records during the existing bounded\\nvisual search. Prefer the most informative authentic image. Apply the no-repeat policy in\\nDAILY_PRODUCTION.md. Use source-still or source-excerpt candidate rows with asset_url and the\\nsame inspection/rights evidence as source-footage. Diagram rows need a sourced relationship\\nand disclosure Illustration. These are additional media, not permission to invent a workflow.\\n\\n## Choose the medium from the evidence\\n\\nSet cinema.version from the new policy. Keep hero_scene_id, optional hero_passage_end_scene_id,\\nvisible_action, human_consequence and source_limit. dimensional_scene_ids is an exact inventory\\nof the quality_plan scenes using 3D; an empty list is legitimate. Each scene still needs a\\nfilmable subject, action, consequence and source_basis. Geometry is useful when depth or contact\\nexplains something. Footage is useful when the action is actually visible. A still can establish\\na real place; an excerpt can expose the decisive words; a diagram can explain a sourced relation.\\nDo not force a character into a source image or draw a fake room to meet a quota.\\n\\nThe editorial-v1 route accepts each scene's picture with id, medium, event_id, disclosure and\\nsubject (the inspected subject, checked by the critic). Use camera_strategy sourcePicture and\\nempty planes for this route's non-dimensional scenes. visual_proof.must_show binds picture.id.\\nFootage/stills/excerpts require file and sha256 from native_media; footprint, provenance and\\nrights remain mandatory. Footage also supplies trim_start_s, trim_end_s, creator, source_url,\\nlicense_url or its existing editorial_excerpt evidence. It plays at original speed with its\\noriginal audio muted. Deliberate environmental audio is separately sourced and mixed.\\n\\nA crop is static x/y percentages. A focus box uses x/y/width/height percentages of the displayed\\nframe and reveals on event_id. Use it to reveal a real detail, never imply a machine detected it.\\nSource-excerpt renders the actual inspected page image, preserving its words. Diagram nodes\\ncarry short label and claim_id; two to four nodes appear on the event clock. The source and\\nnumeral gates cover those printed labels. No long paragraphs or substitute dashboards.\\nDimensional scenes omit picture and call the existing demonstrated action route; bespoke\\nsource-backed mechanisms retain their admission and native-hero requirements.\\n\\nEvery current scene receives full-resolution normal/subject-removed sample pairs. The existing\\nproof key without_stage now removes the principal picture for each medium. It never removes\\ncaptions or branding to manufacture visible action. A source still/excerpt may have a justified\\nintentional_hold within the policy duration after the opening; the phone and final lenses still\\njudge its purpose. Otherwise the principal picture must visibly develop on its event clock.\\nThe hero remains a finished native passage with sound, even when it uses no 3D.\\n\\n## Compare two openings once\\n\\nPrepare opening-a.json and opening-b.json beside storyboard.json. From September 30, both may\\nchange the complete visual treatment, including the middle and ending. Keep the same dated\\nfacts, narration, scene ids and timing, shared inspected asset set and viewer question. Their\\nfull visual concepts are hash-bound, including body scenes; retiming does not change identity.\\nFor September 29 captures only, the original first-scene-only comparison remains reproducible.\\nMake genuinely different visual approaches. Keep both inside the source and medium contracts.\\nThe existing independent code critic reviews both in one reserved assignment and returns\\nopening-a-critic.json and opening-b-critic.json using the ordinary exact concept/renderer/story\\nbindings. It can reject both before a render is spent. Do not add another reviewer identity.\\n\\nRun scripts/opening_compare.py once. It reserves one preflight batch, renders exactly two\\nquarter-scale full animatics with one browser/bundle, and saves openings/comparison.json.\\nBoth completed films receive exact-board, film, renderer and inspector-bound structural reports\\nbefore phone review. The comparison retains both reports and all failures, even if the first\\ninspection fails. Cached comparisons inspect the retained bytes without another render. The\\nnormal command exits nonzero on inspection failure. Its --retain-failed-inspection flag retains\\ndiagnostics for policy-authorized finishing only; it does not change a failed report or approve\\nphone review. These inexpensive options share the same narrative, so the chosen full preview is\\nalready available for continuity review. Failed attempts stay charged. A changed batch requires\\nthe existing consolidated repair path, never an automatic reset.\\n\\nFor a retained capture from the reviewed pre-inspection orchestration version, use\\nopening_compare.py --inspect-retained. This performs no render or reservation. It verifies the\\nknown original orchestration hash, every unchanged capture dependency, both original films and\\nboards, the renderer and source assets, and the original charged reservation. It archives the\\noriginal comparison and keeps its producer hash, then binds new inspection reports separately.\\nThe existing independent selection may keep its original comparison hash only while the exact\\noriginal capture record is unchanged. Unknown capture versions or changed dependencies refuse\\nadoption. Failed measurements remain failed under this path too.\\n\\nThe existing exact-phone critic watches both openings, then the chosen whole sequence. It writes\\nopenings/selection.json with comparison_sha256, selected (a or b), director_identity,\\nreviewer_identity, reason, rejected_reason and blocking_defects. Reasons describe observed\\npixels and the opening question. Copy the chosen frozen board to storyboard.json and its film\\nto preflight.mp4; retain its matching code critique as storyboard_critic.json, inspect that exact\\nfilm with preflight_animatic --inspect-only, then record the ordinary phone verdict on those\\nbytes. The unused option stays as evidence. Neither option authorizes a narration take until\\nthe chosen cut passes the current phone gate. No third concept or extra panel by default.\\n\\n## Direct performance, sound and cuts together\\n\\ncreative_direction binds policy_sha256 and records viewer_question, visible_answer,\\nemotional_turn and medium_choice. Its ordered edits rows contain scene_id, enter_on, leave_on,\\ncut_after_event_id and next_connection. The actual event must complete before the cut; a prose\\npromise cannot substitute for its clock. Describe the visible instant that earns each cut and the carried subject\\nor sourced relationship. The final row states the resolved answer and source limit. After any\\nstructural change, review the whole sequence. Measured narration retimes the event clock; do not\\nadd dead air to preserve an arbitrary grid or accelerate the voice to rescue too many words.\\n\\ncreative_direction.sound records perspective, music_arc, voice_arc and cues. Each cue has id,\\nevent_id, role (environment, contact, sonification or quiet), duration_s, intent and provenance.\\nUse truthful recorded ambience or an explicitly designed effect. Do not pretend a generated\\nsound was recorded at the actual site. Avoid a hit at every cut. Include one deliberate background\\ncontrast with a quiet cue and gain from the policy contract. The quiet cue reduces the music and\\neffects bus on its actual visual event; it never mutes, stretches or splices the narration.\\n\\nEach non-quiet cue has one sfx_events entry with matching id/event_id, wav, source and gain.\\nThe mixer anchors it to the current board event, trims to its declared duration at original\\nspeed, adds short edge fades and refuses undersized or nonfinite audio. It records every cue,\\nsource WAV hash and the exact sound/timing digest in mix.json. Retime the sfx event file with the\\nboard and remix after a changed clock. Old mix evidence fails the release check.\\n\\nThe existing voice director reads this sound arc and the selected opening. It binds\\nsound_direction_sha256 to the sound object and gives each line specific intent, relative energy\\nand an exact spoken emphasis phrase. Contrast curiosity, discovery and the final consequence\\nwithout a trailer voice. Numeric pause commands stay out of the TTS prompt. One continuous take\\nand its existing audible soundcheck remain the default; field completion cannot approve a flat\\nor synthetic read. The sound lens judges actual delivery, masking, sync and contrast in the MP4.\\n\\nAll three final audiovisual lenses and scoring agents remain. The legacy response field\\ndimensional_action describes the principal picture in any medium. A judge may reject a weak\\nimage, inert diagram, generic read or unearned cut with timestamped evidence; a medium preference\\nalone is not a defect. Passing quality moves directly to release and verified shipment.\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/MODERN_FILM.md\":{\"$text\":[\"# Direct the film before describing its look\\n\\nOwner instruction, October 7th, 2026. Active for newly planned editions from October 8th,\\nor an explicit `film_direction` opt-in. The original source, rights, minimum action,\\nnative PNG/CRF16, audio, caption, independent panel and autonomous shipment gates remain.\\n\\n## What the previous upgrade failed to change\\n\\nOctober 7th's shipped film passed its mechanical gates and scored 7.596. The owner rejected\\nits engagement and pace. It repeated an equipment tableau through six scenes, with a 9.5-second\\nclosing scene. Palette, camera poses and declared events did not create a visual argument.\\nThe bounded release contract could also defer pacing, motion, surface finish and ending artistry.\\nNeither a score nor a completed worksheet overrules that observed failure.\\n\\nThis upgrade therefore changes the executable route and review eligibility. It does not promise\\nan aesthetic result from a new renderer name. Current production uses `directed-film-v2` and a\\nregistered, story-specific episode. Missing plans, unknown views and legacy routes fail. Older\\nepisodes remain reproducible as historical evidence. A current film cannot defer the four\\ncategories above, even at a creative ceiling. Capacity recovery funds mandatory repair on the\\ncurrent route; it never restores the retired route or edits a rejected finding.\\n\\n## Lessons verified in AlaskaAIWeekly\\n\\nStudy pinned source and complete published films, rather than an isolated hero still. The current\\nreference revision is `e53f3f92e6cbe123e8802239d8172622d4f3a630`.\\n\\n- [Directors room](https://github.com/Talonsturgill/alaska-ai-weekly/blob/e53f3f92e6cbe123e8802239d8172622d4f3a630/prompts/dispatch_routine.md)\\n  commits an earned angle, cold open, escalation, performed turn and visual button. Translate its\\n  contrasting dramatic, comic, explanatory and curious lenses into the existing two complete\\n  Texas treatments. Do not add daily roles, extra pitches or another paid panel.\\n- [October 7th episode](https://github.com/Talonsturgill/alaska-ai-weekly/blob/e53f3f92e6cbe123e8802239d8172622d4f3a630/video-engine/src/Ep1007.tsx)\\n  uses a recurring physical object, distinct shot sizes, local reactions, carefully finished\\n  silhouettes and named visual reveals. A figure's state changes across scenes; the frame does\\n  not merely rescan the same equipment.\\n- [October 6th episode](https://github.com/Talonsturgill/alaska-ai-weekly/blob/e53f3f92e6cbe123e8802239d8172622d4f3a630/video-engine/src/Ep1006.tsx)\\n  gives its desk and phone a visual performance, with local anticipation, contact and result.\\n  Port that causal grammar and reusable finished assets. Do not copy its regional mascot,\\n  factual claims, source archive, ledger or old footage into Texas.\\n- The current Alaska master also corrects its old instruction to punctuate every beat with a\\n  camera kick. Preserve motivated cuts and object reactions. Frequent new information does not\\n  mean perpetual shake, strobing, overshoot or arbitrary camera motion.\\n\\n## Two complete treatments, one executable direction\\n\\nBefore voice, design exactly two feasible, complete alternatives. Each needs a first-frame\\nquestion, a recognizable throughline subject, an escalation, a fair source-backed turn, a\\nclosing picture that answers the opening, and a sound arc. Different shot ordering, staging\\nand visual emphasis must give a viewer a different experience. Two camera poses on the same\\ntableau are one treatment.\\n\\nWrite `film_direction` with the active policy version, registered episode, actual renderer\\nhashes, angle, opening promise, performed turn, closing answer, shot timeline and rewards.\\nThe shot timeline covers every story frame, conserves subject identity and source-bound scene\\ntiming, and names an implemented view and overlapping physical event. Use at least three useful\\nframings. A new action, reaction, comparison, consequence or evidence reveal earns each cut.\\nAn empty push, rotating fan or appearing label alone does not count as new understanding.\\n\\nBefore code review, freeze each shot's `scene_fraction_start` and `scene_fraction_end` within its source\\nscene, and each reward's `event_fraction` within its physical event. These authored anchors\\nbelong to the approved concept. `board_retime.py` derives the measured seconds from them after\\nvoice alignment, without compounding earlier timing. If the measured read breaks the limits\\nor event overlap, repair the edit; never stretch the narration or silently move a reward.\\n\\nThe current product limits are in `config/modern_film.json`: first visible change within 1.5\\nseconds, no shot longer than 5 seconds, and no unearned information interval longer than 4\\nseconds. These are explicit production constraints chosen after the owner rejection, not a\\nscientific claim about all audiences. Do not bypass them by relabeling a repeated view or\\ninventing event declarations. Independent review watches the execution at normal speed.\\n\\nGenerate this edition's fresh hero and supporting artwork under STORY_ART.md before animation.\\nFinish the hero silhouette, contact shadows, layered surfaces, motivated light and focal hierarchy\\nat native size and 390-pixel phone width before voice. Use authentic licensed footage when it\\nprovides useful action. Otherwise author a source-bound illustration. Do not infer a particular\\nfailure mechanism, measured value, actual operator, hardware design or completed outcome.\\n\\n## Perform and judge the complete edit\\n\\nNarration is an energetic, continuous explanation with purposeful contrasts. Begin the action\\nimmediately, keep connective phrases moving, and reserve emphasis and breathing room for the\\nturn and answer. Do not put a reverent pause after every clause. Shorten slow writing before\\nsynthesis, rather than accelerating the audio. Compare actual take timing with the approved\\nshot rewards and listen through the existing audiovisual path. Fast unreadable words fail too.\\n\\nThe existing phone critic and three separate final scorers receive this guide's actual text and\\nhash. At visual/final scope each returns exact-film `modern_observations` for first frame, visual\\nprogression, shot variety, performed turn, pace, closing answer and finished art. Each contains\\nan observed interval, concrete finding and pass flag. The ordinary rubric and actual failures\\nremain unchanged. A high average cannot replace a failed engagement or finish observation.\\n\\nOptional engineering stops at its reserved boundary. If a mandatory current-route observation\\nfails, preserve that cut and repair through the configured autonomous completion policy, using\\nthe retained independent source-backed pivot when needed. Neither artistic ceilings nor host\\ncapacity authorize a legacy episode, slideshow rescue or unaudited provider substitution.\\n\\n\\n## The region stands behind every current film\\n\\nOwner instruction, October 9th, 2026, on the plan's fifth step. Place was the show's weakest axis\\n(6.36 on the mean of the last ten report cards) and every current film stood in a flat gradient,\\nso a Harris County story and a Reeves County story looked like the same nowhere.\\n\\nFrom the date in `video-engine/src/modern/placePlates.json` (`policy.effective_date`), DirectedFilm\\ndraws each scene's region behind its episode through `modern/PlaceStage.tsx`. Each of the ten\\nregions has a plate, rendered once in the Docket's carousel engine from a scene page under\\n`assets/place/scenes/` by `scripts/place_bake.py`, as a sky, one ground and cards for the things\\nstanding on it. The bake measured that the layers reassemble into the picture and that every\\ncamera profile keeps the ground covering the frame and every base on its ground. The manifest\\nrecords those measurements, the Docket commit, every layer's sha256 and the hash of each module a\\nscene imports from `assets/place/`. Water is drawn by `assets/place/water.js` as a mirror of the\\nworld in its own plane, because a lake seen from eye height under a hazy sky otherwise reads as a\\npale slab, and no scatter grows on it.\\n\\n- **The plate is the county's when it has one, and the region's when it doesn't.** A region's own\\n  plate carries nothing that belongs to one place, no skyline and no refinery, because a Texan is\\n  not told they live somewhere they don't. Harris County stands in Houston across Buffalo Bayou,\\n  Dallas County over the Trinity floodplain, Travis County across Lady Bird Lake and Bexar County\\n  over the river south of downtown. A story at a plant on the upper coast names\\n  `place_plate: \\\"gulf-shipchannel\\\"` on its scenes for the refineries, which a board may do only for\\n  a county that plate lists. The fly gene film's labs are in the Medical Center, and a blind grade\\n  of its frames on October 9th marked the refinery view as the wrong place within the right county.\\n- **Outdoors** the plate fills the frame and the camera moves through it on the scene's\\n  `camera_strategy`, within a share of the plate's measured limits. The ground moves by the exact\\n  perspective transform, so it never tears. Wrap a subject that stands on the ground in\\n  `<PlaceSubject baseY={...}>` with the frame row its base touches, and it rides with its ground.\\n  Keep type and overlays outside it.\\n- **Indoors, wide and medium**, the region is outside a window in the back wall. It starts below\\n  the title band, it is held still and it is bright and soft, the way a camera exposed for the room\\n  sees a window, behind a light frame. The episode draws its own floor and props in front of it.\\n- **Indoors, close and detail**, there is no window, only its light: the region is a soft wash\\n  behind the subject, because a lens that close is focused on the subject and a window pane behind\\n  a fly makes the fly as tall as the pane. Any view the episode lists in `wash_views` takes the same\\n  wash at every framing. List a labelled comparison there, things set out on their own ground lines\\n  with a label over each, since a window's rails and skyline cross exactly that type and those lines.\\n- **Overhead**, and any view the episode lists in `wall_views` (a diagram or a document, which is\\n  not in a room), keep plain wall. No more than 40 percent of a film's shots may be wall views.\\n\\n**An episode never paints a full-frame background.** That one rect hides the whole region, and\\nthe film looks exactly as it did when place was the weakest axis. Paint the floor, the props and\\nanything the story needs in the room. `scripts/place_check.py --render` renders every shot with the\\nplate as solid magenta and fails a shot that shows less than its minimum share of region, by\\nname. Unboxed type over the window stays dark or gets its own panel, as type over any picture does.\\n\\nThe stage also draws a county locator from two seconds in. A small card draws the state's outline,\\nfills the first scene's county and rings it, on the vetted map-explainer timing (border 2.5\\nseconds, fill 1.0, label 0.7). It carries no words, because no claim stands behind a board's\\ncounty and the narration names the place. Its map is computed by `scripts/county_map.py`.\\n\\nA run never bakes a plate. A plate is added or changed by editing its scene page and running\\n`place_bake.py --docket <a TexasAIDocket checkout>`, and the layers and manifest are committed\\ntogether. CI fails a scene or a place module edited without a re-bake. Each plate names the engine\\nrecord it was drawn with, the Docket commit and the bytes of every engine file, so a plate rebaked\\nalone with a newer Docket leaves every other plate's record as it was. The bake measures the layers\\nas the stage loads them, encoded as lossless WebP and read back, and holds each limit to its\\nmeasurements: the last step that passed, the next step's failure and every profile end the stage\\nmoves to. CI measures cover and magnification again from the committed layers at every profile end\\nand requires the bake's numbers exactly. Open each baked plate's `out/place-bake/<plate>/full.png`\\nat film size before committing it: the bake measures whether the layers move as one world, never\\nwhether the water reads as water.\\n\\n## Narration and picture use one clock\\n\\n\",{\"$v\":\"265\"},\"\\n\\n\",{\"$v\":\"59\"},\"\\n\\n\",{\"$v\":\"140\"},\"\\n\\n\",{\"$v\":\"247\"},\"\\n\\n\",{\"$v\":\"283\"}]},\"knowledge/craft/STORY_ART.md\":\"# Fresh relevant artwork during every storyboard\\n\\nDirect owner instruction from October 7th, 2026. From the effective date in\\n`config/story_art.json`, generate two fresh images before animation and voice. This is a\\nrequired production step: a finished hero plus supporting props or a purposeful environment.\\nUse the built-in ImageGen tool and its skill. Do not silently substitute the old exceptional\\nGemini background-plate lane, library boxes or a prior edition's generated artwork.\\n\\n## Design a useful asset set\\n\\nAfter selecting the earned angle, write `story_art` in the actual board, with version\\n`fresh-story-art-v1` and two `requests`. Each has `id`, `role` (`hero` or `support`), the edition's\\n`generated/story-art/<date>/<request-id>.png` filename, relevant `scene_ids`, a concrete `purpose`,\\nthe complete generation `prompt`, and an immediate `source_limit`. Plan these images once for\\nboth complete treatments. A supporting atlas can hold several separated relevant props in one\\nimage; its independently movable slices must be measured against the actual output.\\n\\nSpecify recognizable silhouettes, rounded sculpted forms, coherent perspective, layered\\nmaterials, motivated key/fill/rim light, readable surface detail and grounded contact. Match the\\nstory's palette and shape language. A film about field work, policy or clinical decisions needs\\ndifferent objects and a different world. Neither decorative scenery nor a familiar stock\\nserver qualifies. Give every principal on-screen prop a clear story job.\\n\\nGenerate cutouts with genuine transparent alpha when they need to move independently. Preserve\\nthe original alpha and bytes. Use an environment image only when its setting is useful and\\nclearly generic. Generated art must not impersonate documentary footage, source evidence, a\\nnamed real operator, an actual unobserved installation, or measured data. Render exact facts,\\nlabels and captions with native verified text. Show the illustration disclosure.\\n\\n## Charge, generate, inspect, record\\n\\nRead the ImageGen skill and announce its first use. Reserve before each actual tool attempt:\\n\\n```sh\\npython scripts/story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json reserve \\\\\\n  --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --request <id> --out out/dispatch/art-<id>-charge.json\\n```\\n\\nThen invoke built-in ImageGen using that exact request, inspect the returned image at native\\nsize and phone size, and save its original output into the workspace. Record the actual\\ngeneration identity from the tool's output filename and its actual creation time, never an\\ninvented provider receipt, token usage or cost:\\n\\n```sh\\npython scripts/story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json record \\\\\\n  --source <original-output.png> --request <id> --generation-id <actual-tool-output-id> \\\\\\n  --generated-at <actual-output-creation-time> --charge out/dispatch/art-<id>-charge.json\\npython scripts/story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json verify\\n```\\n\\nAll commands use the Dispatch environment wrapper. Add measured image `width` and `height`\\nand, for an atlas, each named `slices` rectangle `[x,y,width,height]` to the recorded entry.\\nThe record binds exact request, original bytes, edition date and prior charge. A rejected\\ngeneration remains charged and retained; archive its board and image before replacing the\\ncurrent request with a separately named request and asset. Keep exactly two selected assets\\nin the active plan. Reuse unchanged\\nassets within this edition's two treatments and mandatory repairs. Resume recorded assets\\nwithout buying them again. An unfinished edition can generate its missing or corrected assets\\non a later day; its reservation still belongs to that edition's original cumulative ledger.\\nNo image from an earlier edition counts as fresh.\\n\\nThe new normal budget reserves two ImageGen calls, with a cumulative ceiling in run_limits.\\nEvery failed attempt counts. Mandatory art failures use the versioned autonomous completion\\npolicy and exact independent failure evidence to fund the complete remaining path. Optional\\nasset polish stops at its boundary. The saved primary model, schedule and existing review\\ncount remain unchanged.\\n\\n`deliver_run.sh` verifies and explicitly stages these exact images, even though the general\\ngenerated-asset directory is ignored by Git. The clean release checkout and future review\\npackets must contain the selected raster bytes. Do not commit unrelated generated files.\\n\\n## Make the images perform\\n\\nThe active episode consumes `board.story_art` through `StoryArtProvider` and `ArtSprite`, or an\\nequally explicit reviewed consumer for its story. No hard-coded old image path or vector-box\\nfallback is allowed. Crop an atlas in the renderer without changing original pixels. Render\\nthese cutouts through Remotion's load-aware `Img` inside the crop viewport. Unmanaged SVG\\n`image` tags produced missing props at the first frame of a newly mounted shot in the actual\\nengineering film. The retained cold-shot regression must reject that capture and accept the\\nloaded picture. Asset download or a good later still does not prove every captured frame.\\nAnimate\\nactual tasks with setup, contact, reaction and consequence on the global event clock. Change\\nshot size and viewpoint when the new information earns it. A generated still slowly zoomed\\nfor the whole narration is still a weak film.\\n\\nThe existing builder reports actual image consumers and known limitations. The existing phone\\ncritic and three final scorers inspect visible finish, subject recognition, contact and source\\ntruth on the exact film. Generate attractive art, then prove that it helps this specific story.\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/cinematic_reference_bank.json\":\"{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"dispatch-cinematic-reference-bank/1\\\",\\n  \\\"frozen_at\\\": \\\"2026-10-06\\\",\\n  \\\"use\\\": \\\"Calibrate observable craft decisions. References are never daily b-roll, current film approvals or comparable numerical scores. Inspect the current source-backed film independently.\\\",\\n  \\\"texas_revision\\\": \\\"506b4af9522d1576c8eb5d002448754e0a4588d4\\\",\\n  \\\"alaska_revision\\\": \\\"b35ab28072d7b1bd28d218b38bb23f748b9ff44c\\\",\\n  \\\"passages\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"alaska-door-world\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Every Door\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": \\\"https://alaskaaihq.com/videos/\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"https://github.com/Talonsturgill/alaska-ai-weekly/blob/b35ab28072d7b1bd28d218b38bb23f748b9ff44c/video-engine/src/Ep1005.tsx\\\",\\n      \\\"film_sha256\\\": \\\"c2267b30c0d34a1fc2637af8e1fd406180fc2f071ddf6b388d9127855b774453\\\",\\n      \\\"start_s\\\": 17,\\n      \\\"end_s\\\": 23,\\n      \\\"observe\\\": \\\"Plum door silhouettes, hardware, coral rule glyph and mint depth form one authored world. The truck reveals parallel doors; focal objects remain sharp.\\\",\\n      \\\"transfer\\\": \\\"Specify palette roles, finish and one signature reveal before coding. Rebuild for the current Texas mechanism, never reuse these doors as footage.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"alaska-ear-stone\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Who Counted\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": \\\"https://alaskaaihq.com/videos/\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"https://github.com/Talonsturgill/alaska-ai-weekly/tree/b35ab28072d7b1bd28d218b38bb23f748b9ff44c/runs/2026-10-02\\\",\\n      \\\"film_sha256\\\": \\\"a34e5e2d22cb936d9586f7ec58dbe7b1198b82677063126581cf3cedae4da726\\\",\\n      \\\"start_s\\\": 7.5,\\n      \\\"end_s\\\": 13.5,\\n      \\\"observe\\\": \\\"The ear stone and counting object have a readable outline, internal finish and distinct stage roles. Large meaningful detail carries the passage.\\\",\\n      \\\"transfer\\\": \\\"Finish the hero silhouette and its relevant surface before surrounding it with props. Inspect both native texture and phone recognition.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"texas-contact-baseline\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"The second point of contact\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": \\\"https://texasaidocket.com/videos/\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"https://github.com/Talonsturgill/TexasAIDispatch/blob/506b4af9522d1576c8eb5d002448754e0a4588d4/video-engine/src/CartonUnloadAction.tsx\\\",\\n      \\\"film_sha256\\\": \\\"8de8bd99228d17abeeda3e1c5cc8c4f244fcb097d3322db8e9489a533d71eebc\\\",\\n      \\\"start_s\\\": 8.2,\\n      \\\"end_s\\\": 14.78,\\n      \\\"observe\\\": \\\"A conserved carton and two plates establish the mechanism, but backing plates, broad primitive surfaces and similar views compete with the grip.\\\",\\n      \\\"transfer\\\": \\\"Expose the two contact faces and the changed clearance through silhouette, light and staging; source-related geometry alone is insufficient.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"texas-water-baseline\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Before the next watering\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": \\\"https://texasaidocket.com/videos/\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"https://github.com/Talonsturgill/TexasAIDispatch/blob/506b4af9522d1576c8eb5d002448754e0a4588d4/video-engine/src/CropWaterAction.tsx\\\",\\n      \\\"film_sha256\\\": \\\"53344f4e81f4ee51dd5d414e97f1d8ea5d5c9f8dd5f1038d4ec76f365f1ed57e\\\",\\n      \\\"start_s\\\": 13.8,\\n      \\\"end_s\\\": 19.8,\\n      \\\"observe\\\": \\\"Repeated plants, boxed soil and small sensing props explain a sourced relation, while similar framing and primitive foliage flatten the visual distinction.\\\",\\n      \\\"transfer\\\": \\\"Give the mechanism a recognizable finished hero and a specific state change. Useful observed imagery remains eligible when available and licensed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"counterexample\\\": {\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"https://github.com/Talonsturgill/alaska-ai-weekly/tree/b35ab28072d7b1bd28d218b38bb23f748b9ff44c\\\",\\n    \\\"observe\\\": \\\"Alaska's October 3 engineering correction removed repeated camera jolts after actual judge complaints. Older constant movement guidance is superseded.\\\",\\n    \\\"transfer\\\": \\\"Move the object first. Keep camera movement motivated and finite; do not copy every decorative effect from a stronger reference.\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/visual-storytelling/README.md\":\"# Visual storytelling for Dispatch\\n\\nResearch and direction revision: October 2nd, 2026.\\n\\nThe picture, narration and captions must describe the same unfolding story. The picture supplies a recognizable subject, relationship, action or consequence. Narration explains its significance and limits. Captions give access to the spoken account. A moving object is useful only when the viewer understands what it represents and what its change means.\\n\\nThese dossiers combine researched craft with proposed Dispatch practice. Source observations are identified and linked. The shot methods, selection procedure and worked example are our production recommendations, not claims that research guarantees audience engagement.\\n\\n## Choose the story's visual approach\\n\\nRead this index and the chosen dossier in full before boarding. Select by the available evidence and the explanation the viewer needs. Keep one primary approach; supporting footage or documents should connect to that approach through a clear subject or question.\\n\\n| Approach | Choose when | What it must show | Reject when |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| [Observed documentary](observed-documentary.md) | Authenticated footage shows the actual people, place, equipment or workflow | A real action and its observed result | Similar-looking stock replaces the story's actual identity |\\n| [Explanatory animation](explanatory-animation.md) | The central process or comparison is hard to see directly | Recognizable input, meaningful transformation and readable output | Abstract objects require a private legend to decode |\\n| [Evidence-led imagery](evidence-led-imagery.md) | Relevant photographs or documents carry the reporting | What the evidence establishes and how it changes the answer | A sequence of screenshots substitutes for the entire mechanism |\\n| [Cinematic scene](cinematic-scene.md) | A source-backed physical task, obstacle and consequence can sustain a scene | Spatially coherent action, a turn and a consequential ending | Lighting, orbiting props or music replace story development |\\n\\nUse this selection order:\\n\\n1. State the viewer's question, sourced action, affected person or group and honest ending.\\n2. Inventory inspected, usable assets and demonstrated components. Record what each can and can't show.\\n3. Choose the approach that makes the central relationship easiest to understand. Explain the rejected alternative in one sentence.\\n4. Complete the [sentence-to-shot worksheet](sentence-to-shot.md). Resolve missing pictures before locking narration.\\n5. Compare exactly two genuinely different complete treatments in the existing shared preview batch. Read the selected dossier for each treatment. Preserve the current contracts, frozen budget and existing independent roles.\\n6. Have the existing critic inspect the actual rendered sequence before reading the director's explanation. A filled worksheet does not prove comprehension.\\n\\nDo not impose a weekday rotation. Track the selected approach in the existing creative-direction rationale so the director can see recent repetition. When two approaches fit equally well, variety can break the tie. Never choose variety at the expense of truth or comprehension.\\n\\n## Choose a format and think through its sequence\\n\\nFor newly planned editions from October 3rd, read the [viewer planning method](viewer-plan.md) in full. Distinguish the format from the medium: a news report can use observed footage, illustration or documents; an educational explainer can return from a diagram to physical evidence; a cinematic scene still needs a truthful task and consequence.\\n\\nFor a news report read [the reporting dossier](news-reporting.md) and choose its human-led, mechanism-led or evidence-led structure from the actual story. Record why the order works, the likely false inference and the carried subject across each cut in the existing creative-direction and transition fields. The [national-news study](broadcast-cadence-study.md) identifies the observed examples and access limits. It does not prescribe a single bracketed rundown.\\n\\nThe director and workers use these short decision reasons to choose and challenge the treatment. A copied structure, named style or completed worksheet supplies no quality verdict. The packet tools bind the current method and relevant approach text; remote recovery supplies the actual text because a provider can't open local links.\\n\\n## Give the three channels distinct jobs\\n\\n**See:** Show the thing being discussed at the moment it is discussed. Preserve its identity across the cut. Make any comparison legible before asking the viewer to infer a result.\\n\\n**Hear:** Name the relationship, cause or uncertainty that the picture can't establish alone. Time emphasis and event sound to the actual reveal. A music swell can't supply an unreported outcome.\\n\\n**Read:** Retain complete measured captions. Use brief object labels only where they identify a picture or distinction. Avoid simultaneous paragraph copy competing with both the action and captions. Lay out the decisive result above the real caption band and hold it long enough to understand.\\n\\nMayer's research summary supports removing distracting content, placing related words near pictures and presenting corresponding animation and narration together. It also reports redundancy effects in multimedia learning. These are learning findings, not a forecast of short-video retention; they do not justify removing accessible captions. Our application is to reduce competing editorial text while maintaining captions. [Cambridge multimedia-learning chapter](https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/abs/cambridge-handbook-of-multimedia-learning/principles-for-reducing-extraneous-processing-in-multimedia-learning-coherence-signaling-redundancy-spatial-contiguity-and-temporal-contiguity-principles/C98AB3A6CE760DD63C048936EA0B3B44), [W3C caption guidance](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/captions-prerecorded).\\n\\n## Review what the viewer receives\\n\\nUse the existing review assignments and fixed rubric. Add these observations to their existing consolidated notes, not a new scorecard or paid role.\\n\\n- **Recognition:** Before reading the board, what does the principal object look like? Can the critic name it without guessing?\\n- **Alignment:** At each narrated clause, does the picture show the named subject and relationship? Record exact film times for contradictions or absent concepts.\\n- **Development:** What changed, and how does that change lead to the next shot? Distinguish subject transformation from decorative motion.\\n- **Continuity:** Is the same person, site, sample or document being followed? Is a different example disclosed?\\n- **Combined comprehension:** After one viewing with audio and captions, what happened, who can act and what remains unproven?\\n- **Picture contribution:** With narration muted and captions covered, which parts of the central process can the viewer actually see? Dates and attribution may rely on text; the principal action can't.\\n- **Ending:** Does the final picture answer the opening question without inventing implementation, savings, approval or repair?\\n\\nAn unrecognizable object, absent principal action or contradictory picture is a comprehension/source defect under the current contract. Do not classify it as merely style because pixels move. Surface polish and optional camera preferences remain artistic issues. Retain all real rejected verdicts and use the existing repair and bounded-release policies.\\n\\n## Apply this without expanding production\\n\\nUse the current budget precheck for the complete review and render path before spending. Keep the bounded visual search, source and rights evidence, prior-edition identity gate, two-treatment comparison, native hero, phone inspection, audiovisual lenses and independent scorers. The dossiers introduce no render quota, new reviewer or budget extension.\\n\\nRead [the October 2nd diagnosis and proposed sequence](october-2-pavement-case.md) for the difference between a source-related object and a picture that communicates the spoken claim.\\n\\n## Research status\\n\\nSources were accessed October 2nd, 2026. The four approach dossiers use published guidance, research summaries and practitioner accounts; their linked film examples are references rather than claimed viewing. The separate national-news study adds explicitly scoped transcripts and rendered samples. Today's diagnosis uses the listed native frame samples and retained board; it is not a replacement independent whole-film review. Research access does not grant reuse rights to any publisher's images, footage or soundtrack.\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/visual-storytelling/explanatory-animation.md\":\"# Explanatory animation\\n\\nRead the [shared visual-storytelling direction](README.md) first.\\n\\n## What this approach does\\n\\nIt makes a hidden process or comparison understandable: two inputs contributing different information, a record moving through a decision, or a physical condition producing a visible measurement. Original diagrams and illustration are often the clearest first choice.\\n\\nChoose this approach when the source establishes the relationship but useful observational footage is missing or can't reveal it. The explanation must preserve the source's uncertainty and distinguish a conceptual example from an actual system output.\\n\\n## Research findings and limits\\n\\nAdobe describes the storyboard as a bridge from script to picture, with panels recording action, dialogue and camera requirements, followed by an animatic to examine the sequence. Its guide includes side-by-side storyboard references for Luca and Up. Those links are study examples; we have not claimed a shot analysis of those films here. [Adobe storyboarding guide](https://www.adobe.com/uk/creativecloud/animation/discover/animation-storyboarding.html).\\n\\nThe [shared direction's learning research](README.md) motivates coordinated explanation and reduced distraction. It does not prove that more animation improves understanding. The following construction method is a Dispatch recommendation responding to the actual pavement-film defect.\\n\\n## Build the explanation\\n\\nWrite the relationship in plain words before choosing objects. For pavement research: surface imagery and depth information reveal different properties of the same road condition. This is a comparison of information, not a story about two blocks traveling on a conveyor.\\n\\n1. **Show the input.** Give it a recognizable form. A photograph should look like a surface image. A document should have a credible readable structure. A road should look like a road.\\n2. **Introduce one distinction.** Use short labels next to the relevant views. Keep the same sample identity and orientation.\\n3. **Show the operation.** Reveal a cross-section, align corresponding views or trace a source-supported relationship. The operation must change what the viewer can understand.\\n4. **Show the result.** Keep the resulting distinction readable. Do not hide it beneath captions, replace it with a flash or move immediately to another object.\\n5. **Show the decision or limit.** Connect the output to the source-backed choice. Leave unproven implementation visibly unresolved.\\n\\nUse arrows to connect a known relationship, not to pretend that an unavailable algorithm has been observed. A bright scan bar is not analysis proof by itself. Do not invent segmentation accuracy, measured depths, confidence percentages or a vendor interface.\\n\\nChoose 2D, 2.5D or 3D based on the relationship. A flat comparison often explains two images best. A cutaway can reveal depth. A three-dimensional scene earns its cost when spatial interaction is the explanation; a beveled box representing an unfamiliar object often adds interpretation work.\\n\\n## Stage and time the picture\\n\\nMake the principal forms identifiable before their transformation. Maintain consistent labels, positions and shape cues. Use color as support, with readable shape or text distinctions as well. Introduce a new concept only after the current relationship is clear.\\n\\nPlan the reveal around the relevant spoken clause, then use measured narration timing for the final event windows. Quiet or restrained sound can mark a visible comparison; a synthetic beep can't imply actual hardware recording. Preserve the existing sound and caption contracts.\\n\\nA changed state can be information made visible. It need not be a moving human or a mechanical handoff. The current minimum picture-action contract still applies: a full-film static diagram with decorative fades is a rejected treatment.\\n\\n## Worked pattern\\n\\n| Spoken idea | Useful picture | Inadequate substitute |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| A photo shows the surface | A recognizable top-down pavement image | An unlabeled gray slab |\\n| Depth adds another kind of information | Corresponding depth view or disclosed conceptual cutaway | A floating yellow rail |\\n| Damage differs from a stain | Stable side-by-side comparison with the difference revealed | Two different props swapping places |\\n| The result supports a report | A recognizable illustrative report linked to the example | Blank sheets flying into trays |\\n| Detection is not repair | Return to the unchanged physical damage | A celebratory completion animation |\\n\\nThis pattern is conceptual guidance, not a verified reconstruction of Texas State's UI or numerical output. See the [pavement case](october-2-pavement-case.md) for source limits.\\n\\n## Before voice and final review\\n\\nHave the existing critic first name the pictured objects and explain the relationship without the director's legend. Then compare exact spoken clauses to rendered moments. If the critic needs the board to identify the principal input or result, consolidate that as a comprehension defect before narration.\\n\\nUse proven components and the existing shared preview comparison. Test the hardest current transformation in the native hero. Preserve the strongest accepted complete treatment as the completion fallback. Additional labels, texture or camera movement can't repair a missing explanation.\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/visual-storytelling/news-reporting.md\":\"# Direct a coherent news report\\n\\nThe [cadence study](broadcast-cadence-study.md) records the evidence behind this dossier. The structures below are Dispatch production choices, not a universal network script. Apply them to newly planned editions from October 3rd, 2026; preserve shipped editions and their real reviews.\\n\\nA report has an editorial spine: a specific situation, a question, evidence that changes the answer, an explanation, an honest consequence and a close. Decide which of those jobs the next shot performs. A source-related image that supplies no new understanding is a weak insert, even if its colors and motion look expensive.\\n\\n## Choose the order from the story\\n\\n| Reporting structure | Choose it when | Sequence of reporting jobs | Ending test |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Human-led report | The evidence identifies a real person's task, obstacle or changed options | Show the task or consequence \\u2192 establish the dated change \\u2192 broaden with evidence \\u2192 explain the cause and limits \\u2192 return to the same person or task | Has the viewer learned what changes for that person, without an invented reaction or outcome? |\\n| Mechanism-led report | The central news is a process, measurement or decision that viewers can't readily see | Show a recognizable input and question \\u2192 orient the source and setting \\u2192 reveal the transformation \\u2192 show the result \\u2192 connect it to a human decision and its limits | Can the viewer explain the input, transformation and result, and distinguish an illustration from observed operation? |\\n| Evidence-led report | A filing, policy, measurement or public record changes the reported answer | Establish the dated decision or disputed claim \\u2192 expose the decisive source detail \\u2192 explain its effect with a concrete relationship \\u2192 show affected options or activity \\u2192 state the unresolved point and next decision | Does the ending answer what the record establishes, who can act next and what it does not establish? |\\n\\nChoose one structure. Compress or reorder it when the evidence and viewer's question justify that choice. Establish the essential source limitation when the affected claim appears; a later caveat can't undo a misleading picture. Keep the current early-picture payoff and event timing requirements. These sequences introduce no extra scenes, prescribed shot seconds or runtime quota.\\n\\nThe CBS transcript in the study provides a specific-to-broad-to-specific example. The CNN transcript shows a different package organization, and the MSNBC example is a question-led interview. They are different forms with different access to people and evidence. A short Dispatch should not imitate a lengthy panel simply because it resembles national television.\\n\\n## Assign each ingredient a reporting job\\n\\n**Opening:** Give the viewer something identifiable to understand immediately: a task interrupted, an input changing, a decision confronting evidence, or a completed consequence that creates a question. State the actual question soon enough to guide the picture. A dramatic claim must stay within the fetched evidence. Do not borrow an unrelated victim, emergency or reaction to manufacture stakes.\\n\\n**Orientation:** Establish who, where and what changed using the minimum needed narration and labels. This is the short-video equivalent of the paragraph that explains the focus of an article. The viewer should know why the next piece of evidence belongs in this story.\\n\\n**Reporter or presenter:** Use an actual reusable field passage when it demonstrates, verifies or bridges the explanation. A fabricated journalist, microphone prop or studio cut adds no verification. Dispatch's narrator can orient the viewer without appearing as a reporter. A person on screen must have a source-backed role and perform an understandable action.\\n\\n**Evidence:** Show the exact place, equipment, task, relevant photograph or decisive source words. Identify what the evidence establishes. A quotation is evidence of what its speaker said; it is not proof that their conclusion is true. Show a contrary finding or uncertainty when the story requires it. Use the existing source and rights lanes for every asset.\\n\\n**Explanation:** Introduce coded visuals when they reveal a relationship that the authentic image can't show. Keep the same physical subject or explicitly identify the new example. The diagram should answer the question created by the preceding shot. Return to the source image or human decision after the explanation when that return completes the thought.\\n\\n**Consequence and close:** Show how the action changes a state, choice, risk or next step. Answer the opening question through the completed visible action. Distinguish a demonstrated consequence, an expected effect and an unknown eventual outcome. Do not repeat the introduction merely to make the film seem circular. A return earns its place when the viewer now understands the original subject differently.\\n\\n## Move between authentic pictures and coded explanation\\n\\nMake each handoff explicit in the existing edit notes. Carry a stable identifying detail: the same road patch, sample, site, device, document passage or clearly disclosed example. Preserve orientation, useful scale and the relationship under explanation. An outline or highlight identifies a region; it does not prove that a machine detected, measured or classified it.\\n\\nFor example, an authenticated image can establish the input. An explicitly illustrated transformation can explain the source-supported relationship. A return to the actual task can show who uses the result. Cutting from an unrelated office image to anonymous blocks and then to a different city breaks that connection, even if every image is broadly about AI.\\n\\nOriginal illustration is a valid principal medium. Useful footage is also valid. An irrelevant insert should be omitted within the existing bounded search. Do not commission an unproven rig or prolong the stock hunt to imitate a particular outlet. Use the current source-backed action admission when a genuinely necessary mechanism needs implementation.\\n\\n## Direct the cadence across picture, voice and reading\\n\\nGive each beat one new idea the viewer needs for the next beat. Complete its decisive event before cutting. Preserve enough time to recognize the subject, follow the change and read the result. Trim repeated setup before requesting faster narration. Pace varies with information and action; a cut on a fixed timer is not an editorial reason.\\n\\nVoice should orient, reveal, explain, qualify or resolve. Tell the VO director which job a line performs and where the visual answer lands. Keep the approved continuous script and measured alignment. Use contrast in intent and emphasis rather than perpetual urgency. Do not turn a hypothesis into certainty through a triumphant delivery or sound cue.\\n\\nNatural sound, verified interview audio and motivated effects can connect thoughts when their provenance and actual event timing support that use. A sound bridge can carry the same action over a cut. Sound can't imply recorded access to a site we did not visit. Preserve intelligibility and all existing audio checks.\\n\\nRetain complete captions. Keep extra labels short and attached to the object they identify. Do not present a second paragraph, a busy diagram and a new location at the same time as a dense spoken sentence. Seeing, hearing and reading should reinforce the same unfolding account.\\n\\n## Review the actual report\\n\\nThe existing critic and scorers reconstruct the story from the current film before consulting the director's rationale. They identify what the opening asks, what new information arrives in the middle, how subject identity survives each handoff, and what the ending answers. Then they compare that understanding with the approved words and fetched evidence.\\n\\nUse exact intervals and the existing observation fields. A missing principal action, unrecognizable subject, false visual implication or failed explanation remains a source/comprehension failure under the current contract. Optional presenter preferences, shot polish and an alternative ordering alone do not create a new mandatory test. Keep the fixed rubric and retain every actual rejection.\\n\",\"knowledge/craft/visual-storytelling/viewer-plan.md\":\"# Make the editorial choice before the picture\\n\\nApply this method to newly planned editions from October 3rd, 2026. It guides decisions under the current contracts and does not certify quality. It adds no board schema, scorer, research pass or paid attempt.\\n\\n## Decide and record\\n\\nRead the selector and chosen approach dossier in full. For a news report also read the reporting dossier. Use the existing creative_direction and story_contract fields; keep the decision rationale compact and inspectable.\\n\\n1. **Focus.** In viewer_question and visible_answer, state what changes, for whom, through which sourced action. Name the expected viewer takeaway and the strongest honest limit. Distinguish the narrative answer from an unknown eventual outcome.\\n2. **Choose.** Begin medium_choice with the named format and approach: News report, Educational explainer or Cinematic scene; then Observed documentary, Explanatory animation, Evidence-led imagery or Cinematic scene. Explain why the available assets can carry the explanation and why a plausible alternative is weaker. Naming an approach is a routing aid, not an approval field.\\n3. **Order.** Put each beat's reporting job in the existing scene advances and edit notes. For a report choose human-led, mechanism-led or evidence-led ordering. Explain why this evidence appears here and what question it creates or answers. Educational explanation builds a recognizable example through successive states. A cinematic scene follows a task, obstacle, consequential turn and completed action. Do not apply one rundown to all three.\\n4. **Anticipate confusion.** Name the most likely false inference and the picture or immediate source limit that prevents it. In emotional_turn, connect the viewer's changing understanding to an evidenced stake. Do not invent a person's feelings or claim to know the audience's reaction.\\n5. **Connect.** In enter_on, leave_on, cut_after_event_id and next_connection, name the visible event, new information and carried subject. Complete the event before the cut. A footage-to-diagram handoff keeps the same identified example or discloses a new one. Finish the sentence-to-shot worksheet inside these existing notes.\\n6. **Direct and test.** Tie line intent, emphasis, motivated sound and captions to the actual reveal. Before spending, ask what remains understandable with narration muted and editorial labels covered, then test the combined account. Essential dates and attribution can use text; the principal action must read in the picture. Budget the entire remaining review/render path, including independent-provider recovery where required.\\n\\nThese are short decision reasons a colleague can inspect, not a request for a private stream of thought. Use concrete evidence and an alternative that could realistically be built. Do not fill every field with the same sentence, duplicate the research or commission a third treatment.\\n\\n## Each worker has a distinct decision\\n\\n- **Researcher:** Identify the most informative picture and the strongest limitation. Recommend an angle that the assets can actually show; flag the sentence for which no truthful picture exists.\\n- **Director:** Choose the story focus, format, medium and order. Resolve the weak handoff before narration, using the same two-treatment batch and consolidated ledger.\\n- **VO director:** Translate the approved beat jobs into a continuous performance. Explain a lift, drop or pause through the reveal it supports; preserve the words and alignment.\\n- **Code critic:** Determine whether the proposed implementation can perform the action and carry the explanation. A planned gesture is not a watched result.\\n- **Phone critic and scorers:** First describe what is recognizable and what changes in the actual film. Then compare with the approved account. Locate the weakest identity or information handoff and classify the observed defect under the existing criteria. Keep their separate assigned lenses and actual verdicts.\\n\\nFor remote independent recovery, the supplied packet contains the actual method, selector, reporting dossier and named approach text. If a director has not named an approach, all four approach guides are supplied rather than pretending an unread local path was available. The new teaching bundle is added only for editions from October 3rd. A text packet never establishes audiovisual access.\\n\\n## Why the handoff needs thought\\n\\nAn original film-comprehension study associated event boundaries with meaningful changes in characters, objects, place, goals and causes. Our application is to preserve those relationships across a cut and make a change understandable. This is an editorial inference, not a scientifically established short-video pacing interval or retention guarantee. [Zacks and colleagues, The Brain's Cutting-Room Floor](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/human-neuroscience/articles/10.3389/fnhum.2010.00168/full).\\n\\nThe director can consult the [observed news examples](broadcast-cadence-study.md) when a reporting choice needs a model. Workers use the supplied method, relevant guide and current artifacts without repeatedly reloading the research corpus. Retain real rejections; a well-written plan can't clear absent action, false implication or failed comprehension.\\n\",\"out/dispatch/captions.json\":{\"original_sha256\":\"a6b0e45a7a95340f5f264c625fe6aab281a34b66c292fa9174445d03fbb4ed86\",\"schema\":\"dispatch_lossless_json_file/1\",\"value\":{\"acoustic_words_matched\":132,\"boundaries_measured\":38,\"cues\":{\"$v\":\"224\"},\"grouping_profile\":\"compact-measured-clauses-v1\",\"method\":\"silence_anchored\",\"narration_clause_segmentation\":{\"contract_sha256\":\"57b1aab24aa2f6cb3942278b561f2904dd805d4644be54a0a81ca4a2ae0834fd\",\"min_pause_s\":0.24,\"version\":\"measured-clause-cues-v1\",\"word_content_sha256\":\"36fcf615540f21458d1afa01aedd94fb50934c4b8e9ba389d80c619a79aa8989\"},\"words_anchored\":37,\"words_file\":\"out/dispatch/words.json\",\"words_modelled\":95}},\"out/dispatch/mix.json\":{\"original_sha256\":\"46d860b91f031fa6d3252847b6c8a3a7aadf5abb6682a915b54f6330d41c755a\",\"schema\":\"dispatch_lossless_json_file/1\",\"value\":{\"bed\":true,\"bed_file\":\"out/dispatch/music_bed.wav\",\"bed_file_sha256\":\"5e19c41c175f7227c6673bc41725ca9997ec3e396f70a478b48c5d92df64cab8\",\"bed_gain_db\":-23.14,\"bed_gap_below_voice_db\":19.0,\"bed_preparation_manifest\":\"out/dispatch/music_bed.json\",\"bed_preparation_sha256\":\"2b3a2af3e7d5eae0745c4e690071469a8049d6cff087f812bff2e1a087b97ca6\",\"bed_source_lufs\":-16.44,\"bed_source_sha256\":\"1da4a58ebbae4f2bbdf297e441574788cc85cb59600b03b2dcc93f6a699927cc\",\"bed_track_id\":\"sincerely\",\"crest_factor_db\":1