versity's reported figure appears and holds.\",\"104\":\"64e66322741e50e6822614e827c1a15b7508aeb846bca8792c693339f0a3da72\",\"105\":{\"action_ids\":[\"flag-plume\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"tower-camera\",\"plume\",\"flag-box\"]},\"106\":\"e1ab789064da3f3aaf8c576593aafc991370144bef88d804d6e8f8e5854d74ff\",\"107\":\"7836b07cd7558d31cfa7d55d07900b832b613f70aa7d5c3220fcbdfb4a20a1ba\",\"108\":\"Rain, temperature, humidity and light lamps come on one by one, the other things the station watches.\",\"11\":{\"action_ids\":[\"complete-service\"],\"subject_ids\":{\"$v\":\"237\"}},\"110\":\"The same brown water and the same ankle height that the station's lowest lens will mark; no station stands in this yard\",\"111\":\"Rain on asphalt and a low trickle as brown water tops the limestone curb and spreads into the yard.\",\"112\":\"On the hub's screen, dots from several stations arrive and a tag names the second, larger model. Shaded flood paths spread out from the first dots along the creek and the low streets. At the desk the dashed higher-risk outlines settle on the screen, a responder's sleeved forearm comes to rest beside it and a for emergency responders tag pins.\",\"114\":\"At street level the rings run down a long street of bungalows to the hub at its far end, and a scale bar marked more than a half-mile draws along the street.\",\"115\":\"63368295e7519b2335bcaeea2dad0f67dc26649f9c65a0629e8ce15b29d0f2cd\",\"116\":\"This on-device AI evaluates current and recent sensor data to predict localized, imminent flood risk without relying on a central server.\",\"118\":\"A short soft designed tone as the warning banner lands on the phone, late.\",\"12\":\"Music settles; a soft paper tap as the deployment goal tag pins, with no water and no station sound.\",\"121\":\"The hub desk and its dashboard, then the flood path map with its risk zones\",\"124\":\"Campus Life\\nResearch\\nHealth\\nAthletics\\nColleges\\nCarlos Alvarez College of Business\\nCollege of AI, Cyber and Computing\\nCollege of Education and Human Development\\nCollege for Health, Community and Policy\\nCollege of Liberal and Fine Arts\\nCollege of Sciences\\nKlesse College of Engineering and Integrated Design\\nUniversity College\\nHonors College\",\"125\":\"Original designed sonification, not a recorded LoRa signal.\",\"126\":\"Flood water rises up the post past the second, third and fourth lenses, and each lens lights in turn as the waterline crosses it.\",\"127\":\"So it judges flood risk without a central server.\",\"128\":\"The one paper map pinned to the chain link fence at the curb, the same map in close up and wide.\",\"129\":\"c0a13a78a3d45206c3ef017420e013b52b29be07d8890977491cdb9f7efcbcfc\",\"13\":\"Inactive registered episode outside all selected executable closures\",\"130\":\"A paper flutter on the fence wire and a quiet sweep as the finger slides along the map.\",\"132\":[{\"id\":\"s5-tags\",\"kind\":\"applicationRecord\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"more than a half mile and up to five miles range tags\"},\"scale\":1,\"x\":540,\"y\":900},{\"id\":\"s5-fivemile\",\"kind\":\"applicationRecord\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"up to five miles in open country tag\"},\"scale\":1,\"x\":540,\"y\":900}],\"134\":\"Readings run in along thin traces from the four lenses and four weather sensors to one small chip, which begins to glow. The chip lights the large amber risk lamp, the risk bar beside the board climbs from one low step to four and a judged on the station tag pins. Across the road a distant dark server building stays unlit, and a dashed line from the station stops short of it and never connects.\",\"135\":\"af13d1b7c7441af66a265d7f4bac7bf13d085d1138dfcd14675f0bd818d0ff03\",\"136\":\"video-engine/src/lib/direction.ts\",\"137\":\"A disclosed design detail of the lowest lens going under, then a flooded yard with no station in it and the phone on the porch rail\",\"138\":\"Cut B opens on an isolated technical detail of a submerged sensor mark without environmental context, weakening