k bar, then the distant dark server building across the road\",\"20\":\"The view cranes down from the antenna tip and reveals the whole prototype flood station at a curb, and a prototype tag pins. Low sun reaches the small dark solar panel, a glint crosses its cells and the battery bar fills cell by cell. A dashed line leaves the antenna toward a far cell tower and stops halfway, and a no cell tower needed tag pins.\",\"200\":\"4811590400523e197125b1f3ca735d8c54f4ea28dcd2194672a2f63060307eda\",\"201\":\"9b103e1278eeb3deba9782fbda35f9fa868afdd65354c044b258ea029ed0654a\",\"202\":\"Radio rings from above, down the street and across open country to the hub\",\"203\":\"At the central monitoring site, custom server software aggregates data from multiple deployed nodes across a town or watershed.\",\"204\":\"A small rising tone as the second optical mark goes under and lights.\",\"205\":\"A second, larger AI model analyzes spatial and temporal patterns across the network to generate an interactive web dashboard with predictive maps.\",\"206\":\"The phone on the porch rail lights its flash flood warning only now, with the water already in the yard.\",\"208\":\"Accuracy was ninety eight point eight two percent.\",\"209\":{\"out/dispatch/sources/utsa.txt\":{\"$v\":\"353\"}},\"21\":\"The same flood station at the same curb, its lowest mark already lit by the water.\",\"210\":\"Four optical sensors at different heights watch the water.\",\"212\":\"2d78478b181b5be7b12f2c705f722d887cd103a3ea12b24b8d21f55fd3c1997d\",\"213\":\"6587fccd0d4d19f4ec18f7aa43eb956fae6a9175fca73849fb397c8141be09ce\",\"215\":\"Brown water tops the limestone curb, spreads across a San Antonio yard with no station in it and climbs a chain link post to its orange ankle mark.\",\"216\":\"A disclosed design detail with no yard around it: brown water climbs over the lowest optical lens at ankle height and the lens lights as it goes under.\",\"219\":\"A small chip on the station runs the AI itself. So it judges f