 card slides onto the board beside the validation card and a pushpin presses it home.\",\"329\":\"The resulting prototype combines temperature, humidity, light and precipitation sensing, as well as four optical water-level sensors mounted at varying heights.\",\"33\":\"At the hub desk the dashboard fills with station dots and a responder works beside the screen.\",\"330\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-11/TowerCameraHero.tsx\",\"331\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-09-claude-pilot/ChartHero.tsx\",\"332\":\"She tucks the folded plan into the front pocket of the prototype's closed carry case, beside the bench prototype station.\",\"333\":\"3758e9bcaa6364e2517e8e3c69a6eea904b5698efb427b87abad3bde99d5e88b\",\"334\":[{\"id\":\"s5-halfmile\",\"kind\":\"applicationRecord\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"more than a half mile scale bar along the street to the hub\"},\"scale\":1,\"x\":540,\"y\":900}],\"335\":\"1711186b55d89308069607d749a38a9c8740b6c6dbca433430b5f4cfc8188019\",\"337\":\"Shaded flood paths spread out from the first dots along the creek and the low streets.\",\"338\":\"549f090d1bbafed672161f37bb2948fa94ac8caa1308773e8be6ed4cbf7c4d47\",\"339\":\"Can a flood station judge rising street water with no power line and no cell tower?\",\"34\":\"6839b760ee6dd681d87e1a65e334a5b185636a98c02c3ad4b1c4505982533948\",\"340\":\"The whole prototype flood station is revealed on its post at a curb in shallow water and a prototype tag pins beside its housing.\",\"341\":\"The whole prototype station at a curb, its solar panel and battery bar, and a far cell tower\",\"342\":\"https://news.utsa.edu/2026/09/ut-san-antonio-researcher-builds-self-powered-smart-warning-system-to-catch-local-floods-before-disaster-strikes/\",\"343\":\"Researchers at The University of Texas at San Antonio have developed a self-sustaining, artificial intelligence-powered flood warning system designed to spot dangerous water accumulation at the street level.\",\"344\":[{\"id\":\"s5-antenna\",\"kind\":\"applicationRecord\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"station whip antenna sending a radio signal pulse, in the street and in an inset in open country\"},\"scale\":1,\"x\":540,\"y\":900}],\"345\":\"The same radio ring arriving as one of the station dots on the hub map.\",\"346\":{\"action_ids\":[\"carry-freight\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"freight-truck\",\"observer\"]},\"347\":\"On the same ankle height the picture cuts to a San Antonio yard with no station in it, the water spreading past the orange ankle mark on a chain link post as the view pulls back.\",\"348\":\"Reflective flood water rises past the optical lenses and each lights as the waterline crosses it. In B s1 it is a disclosed design detail with no yard around it.\",\"349\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-11/TowerAlertFilm.tsx\",\"35\":\"Pull the music back while the field result card stays blank and takes its none reported stamp.\",\"350\":\"7038e56cbed9fa0397c5caf67e0ae4b78af44721e0421f6e759199ae5b2ceacd\",\"351\":\"The design says yes. The proof so far is validation accuracy, and the announcement names no installation.\",\"352\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"353\":\"9ec493983d1b4b41a043b5eb934563ca37c64e1f98a2bb88bca90a8e49b551c9\",\"36\":\"The same station's design, now measured only by the university's reported validation figure.\",\"37\":{\"action_ids\":[\"restrict-movement\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"disabled-fly\"]},\"38\":\"The rings run down a long street of bungalows to the hub at its far end, and a scale bar marked more than a half-mile draws along the street.\",\"39\":\"At a folding table on the curb a technician folds the printed deployment plan in three along its creases. She tucks the folded plan into the front pocket of the prototype's closed carry case, beside the bench prototype station. She presses the case latch shut and takes her hand away, and a deployment goal tag hangs from the case.\",\"4\":{\"event\":{\"at\":\"2026-10-17T02:38:56.629864Z\",\"kind\":\"reserved\",\"note\":\"R15d corrective reboard: physical-water-sensor-range-map-pictures-v1 on film report f2dd8a81 (8 defects), pivot review 3 PASS\",\"preflight_identity\":null,\"resources\":{\"reboards\":1}},\"event_sha256\":\"8e0e13570cf62dc640f6e756ceb619f3b57b9669c78c79fe09ab11260b471398\",\"index\":293,\"kind\":\"production\"},\"40\":\"5a8c857d842185d738b91c00992354e1d691bf3c00e2a7bd71faa329899fe5f8\",\"41\":\"A technician at a folding table on the curb, the printed deployment plan, the prototype's closed carry case and the bench prototype beside it\",\"42\":\"authored://2026-10-15/street-hub-support\",\"43\":\"authored://2026-10-11/west-texas-support\",\"45\":\"The same station post and its four marks, the waterline rising from the first mark.\",\"46\":\"The same station housing, now opened, carrying the readings from the marks it just lit.\",\"47\":\"The flash flood warning banner finally slides onto the phone, after the water is already in the yard.\",\"49\":\"A quiet room tone at the hub and soft map shading strokes.\",\"5\":[\"c12\",\"c1\",\"c5\",\"c6\",\"c14\",\"c2\",\"c3\",\"c18\",\"c7\",\"c16\",\"c17\",\"c20\",\"c4\",\"c10\",\"c9\"],\"50\":\"Authored in this edition, type-checked and gate-checked; rendered pixels still need the independent code, phone and final reviews.\",\"51\":{\"anticipation\":0,\"curve\":\"contact\",\"settle\":0.03},\"52\":\"Original designed foley, not a real wireless emergency alert tone.\",\"53\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-15/StreetHubSupport.tsx\",\"54\":\"Seen from the street through the housing window, readings run along the thin traces to the small chip.\",\"55\":\"77b820836f3a874a831522a0e628ba6b5049b628d03a358d55f1270b16db3765\",\"56\":\"The lens column framed low and right with the rising water, then the housing's weather lamps\",\"57\":\"A flooded San Antonio yard with no station in it, the orange ankle mark on a chain link post and the phone on the porch rail\",\"58\":\"On the same notice board a hand brings a rubber stamp down onto the blank field result card, presses none reported and lifts it away.\",\"59\":\"Before voice exists, use timing_mode authored with an explicit provisional cue plan for the silent two-treatment comparison. These estimated windows approve only planning. After alignment, board_retime.py replaces them with measured_caption_boundaries from the actual captions and acoustic word stream. Timed capture, preship and delivery require those measured inputs and reject an authored clock.\",\"6\":\"In open country rings roll out from the station in its inset to the hub's mast, the mast lamp and the hub window light as the leading ring arrives and the five-mile tag pins.\",\"60\":\"The same curb, chain link fence and paper map, now behind the folding table.\",\"61\":\"From the street the housing window glows as readings arrive. Wide, a distant dark server building across the road stays unlit and a dashed line from the station stops short of it.\",\"62\":\"On the curb notice board the validation bar fills to the university's reported figure, which holds, and an after training tag pins under it.\",\"63\":\"On the same notice board a hand brings a rubber stamp down onto the blank field result card, presses none reported and lifts it away. Wide on the empty curb after the flood, the paper street map pinned to the chain link fence settles, with no pin on it. A hand slides one finger along the map's creek and up a street past its blank pin holes and lifts away. An announcement names no installation tag pins beside the map.\",\"64\":\"The second, larger model shades how flooding could spread and outlines the higher-risk zones.\",\"66\":{\"action_ids\":[\"show-estimate\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"alert-card\",\"ten-minute-arc\",\"estimate-tag\"]},\"67\":\"The team aims to refine the design into a sleeker, weatherized commercial product suitable for deployment by small coastal municipalities, homeowners\\u2019 associations, agricultural operations and i