          "schema": "dispatch_verified_prior_review/1",
          "original_sha256": "3f8d13187a4c26946bb835bf9e54517a02c945d2f6f833975c7346f751acc288",
          "scope": "Prior completed scope only. No observation or verdict approves the new current film.",
          "review": {
            "selected": "a",
            "comparative_reason": "Cut A establishes immediate human stakes and narrative clarity by opening wide on the flooded yard with the boots and porch rail, clearly demonstrating water accumulation before the phone warning arrives late. Its spatial progression is continuous and coherent: moving from the flooded residential block to the curbside station prototype, climbing the sensor post, examining the local TinyML chip decision, and tracing the radio signal down the physical street corridor into open country and the emergency hub. This staging creates an intuitive physical throughline that reinforces the problem-to-solution narrative.",
