were not located or downloaded.\",\"rights_basis\":\"None established. No reuse licence found, so no photograph is admitted.\",\"source_url\":{\"$v\":\"344\"},\"url\":{\"$v\":\"344\"},\"what_it_proves\":\"Nothing the film needs. The article is the source for the design.\"}],\"human_consequence\":\"Emergency responders and residents of street-level flood-prone blocks. No affected resident or responder is named in any source.\",\"mechanism\":\"Input: four optical water-level sensors plus temperature, humidity, light and rain sensing. Transformation: a compressed model on the chip judges flood risk locally. Result: a radio warning goes to a hub and a dashboard of predicted flood paths. Limit: validation accuracy only and no named installation.\",\"opening_action\":\"An illustrated solar station beside a street. Water rises past four sensor marks at different heights. Disclosed as Illustration.\",\"source_limit\":\"The design and accuracy claims rest on the university's own account. The accuracy figure is from initial assessments after training. No installed site, no field result and no price for a finished product are published.\",\"three_key_images\":[\"The solar station with four sensor heights, drawn as an illustration\",\"Water crossing the four marks one at a time while the chip lights a local risk judgment\",\"A radio pulse to a hub and a dashboard of predicted flood paths beside the card that says no installed site is named\"],\"viewer_question\":{\"$v\":\"341\"}},\"movement\":{\"action\":\"published a field-ready prototype flood warning node that runs its machine learning model on the chip\",\"actor\":\"University of Texas at San Antonio\",\"date\":\"2026-09-08\",\"event_type\":\"published\",\"object\":\"a solar powered street-level station with four optical water-level sensors at different heights\"},\"record_id\":\"tx-2026-0141\",\"record_status\":\"in-record\",\"record_url\":\"https://texasaidocket.com/item/tx-2026-0141/\",\"sources\":[{\"note\":\"UT San Ant