ossless_shared_packet/1\",\"values\":{\"0\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-11/WestTexasSupport.tsx\",\"1\":\"e3baef95838476732079875b9d922195be4b421ae9b2d8bcf08480f6b98ab5c6\",\"100\":{\"action_ids\":[\"coordinate-shipments\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"shipment-orders\",\"freight-truck\",\"observer\"]},\"101\":\"be9c00e439b031271f4e45677509aa74b630d630f7a0bdb9e2ab653d4e6ed9f7\",\"102\":\"444be8ad166895ce33a8ba6741627308380f9e59197b220e1538f6b3548ca346\",\"103\":{\"action_ids\":[\"show-quiet-months\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"launch-calendar\",\"attribution-tag\"]},\"104\":\"On the curb notice board an orange tape strip is pressed along the validation card's bar and the university's reported figure appears and holds.\",\"105\":\"64e66322741e50e6822614e827c1a15b7508aeb846bca8792c693339f0a3da72\",\"106\":{\"action_ids\":[\"flag-plume\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"tower-camera\",\"plume\",\"flag-box\"]},\"107\":\"e1ab789064da3f3aaf8c576593aafc991370144bef88d804d6e8f8e5854d74ff\",\"108\":\"7836b07cd7558d31cfa7d55d07900b832b613f70aa7d5c3220fcbdfb4a20a1ba\",\"109\":\"Rain, temperature, humidity and light lamps come on one by one, the other things the station watches.\",\"11\":{\"action_ids\":[\"complete-service\"],\"subject_ids\":{\"$v\":\"239\"}},\"111\":\"The same brown water and the same ankle height that the station's lowest lens will mark; no station stands in this yard\",\"112\":\"Rain on asphalt and a low trickle as brown water tops the limestone curb and spreads into the yard.\",\"113\":\"On the hub's screen, dots from several stations arrive and a tag names the second, larger model. Shaded flood paths spread out from the first dots along the creek and the low streets. At the desk the dashed higher-risk outlines settle on the screen, a responder's sleeved forearm comes to rest beside it and a for emergency responders tag pins.\",\"115\":\"At street level the rings run down a long street of bungalows to the hub at its far end, and a scale bar marked more than a half-mile draws along the street.\",\"116\":\"63368295e7519b2335bcaeea2dad0f67dc26649f9c65a0629e8ce15b29d0f2cd\",\"117\":\"This on-device AI evaluates current and recent sensor data to predict localized, imminent flood risk without relying on a central server.\",\"119\":\"A short soft designed tone as the warning banner lands on the phone, late.\",\"12\":\"Music settles; a soft paper tap as the deployment goal tag pins, with no water and no station sound.\",\"122\":\"The hub desk and its dashboard, then the flood path map with its risk zones\",\"125\":\"Campus Life\\nResearch\\nHealth\\nAthletics\\nColleges\\nCarlos Alvarez College of Business\\nCollege of AI, Cyber and Computing\\nCollege of Education and Human Development\\nCollege for Health, Community and Policy\\nCollege of Liberal and Fine Arts\\nCollege of Sciences\\nKlesse College of Engineering and Integrated Design\\nUniversity College\\nHonors College\",\"126\":\"Original designed sonification, not a recorded LoRa signal.\",\"127\":\"Flood water rises up the post past the second, third and fourth lenses, and each lens lights in turn as the waterline crosses it.\",\"128\":\"So it judges flood risk without a central server.\",\"129\":\"The one paper map pinned to the chain link fence at the curb, the same map in close up and wide.\",\"13\":\"Inactive registered episode outside all selected executable closures\",\"130\":\"c0a13a78a3d45206c3ef017420e013b52b29be07d8890977491cdb9f7efcbcfc\",\"131\":\"A paper flutter on the fence wire and a quiet sweep as the finger slides along the map.\",\"133\":[{\"id\":\"s5-tags\",\"kind\":\"applicationRecord\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"more than a half mile and up to five miles range tags\"},\"scale\":1,\"x\":540,\"y\":900},{\"id\":\"s5-fivemile\",\"kind\":\"applicationRecord\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"up to five miles in open country tag\"},\"scale\":1,\"x\":540,\"y\":900}],\"135\":\"Readings run in along thin traces from the four lenses and four weather sensors to one small chip, which begins to glow. The chip lights the large amber risk lamp, the risk bar beside the board climbs from one low step to four and a judged on the station tag pins. Across the road a distant dark server building stays unlit, and a dashed line from the station stops short of it and never connects.\",\"136\":\"af13d1b7c7441af66a265d7f4bac7bf13d085d1138dfcd14675f0bd818d0ff03\",\"137\":\"video-engine/src/lib/direction.ts\",\"138\":\"A disclosed design detail of the lowest lens going under, then a flooded yard with no station in it and the phone on the porch rail\",\"139\":\"Cut B opens on an isolated technical detail of a submerged sensor mark without environmental context, weakening the initial scroll-stopping hook and delaying understanding of the residential flood problem. In the radio transmission and hub sequence (s5-s6), Cut B cuts abruptly between an abstract overhead 2D map and ground views, causing unnecessary spatial disorientation compared to Cut A's cohesive camera tracking along the street corridor.\",\"14\":\"127f9df80c7da35d2d0ed201576b2f0eccea967fc6957925c98d259d61f31f22\",\"140\":\"The total cost of parts for one prototype sensing station ranges from roughly $150 to $220.\",\"141\":\"After acoustic alignment, compile every clause window from complete measured caption boundaries and the matched positional word stream. Use modern_film.compile_narration with the actual captions and words. Derive cut handoffs from silence between clauses. Only framing subdivisions inside the same subject/action may use fractions. Renderer performances consume requireNarration on the film-global clock, and retain completed consequences across cuts. Never stretch speech, scale cue times, or proportionally place a different narrated action inside a scene.\",\"142\":\"482b10e0d23c8f5bed626d8d62e92056ab9bfe7cc77a328ce7126ceea7bece1f\",\"144\":\"The view cranes down from the antenna tip and reveals the whole prototype flood station at a curb, and a prototype tag pins.\",\"147\":\"Brown water spreads across a San Antonio yard with no station in it and climbs a fence post to its ankle mark while the porch phone stays dark.\",\"148\":\"The same station antenna and its risk judgment, carried out by radio toward the hub\",\"149\":\"So its researchers built a flood station. It charges itself from light and needs no cell tower.\",\"15\":\"Disclosed original illustration of the design the university describes, not observed footage, an installed station or a real site.\",\"150\":\"The same radio ring arriving as one of the station dots on the hub map\",\"151\":\"On the hub's screen, dots from several stations arrive and a tag names the second, larger model.\",\"152\":\"23d3991400e67d27410665dd886bcb80c3fe24bf4b261bce799d107dfc36b578\",\"153\":\"At the desk the dashed higher-risk outlines settle on the screen, a responder's sleeved forearm comes to rest beside it and a for emergency responders tag pins.\",\"154\":\"4d572bbc708b9ad98bcb9a563738ec64b56eb98b1d0bcbdd319ac6521ce8fa3c\",\"155\":\"The announcement reports no field result. It names no town with an installed station.\",\"157\":\"An announcement names no installation tag pins beside the map.\",\"158\":\"A quiet electric run of clicks along the traces and a low hum as the chip lights.\",\"159\":\"It names no town with an installed station.\",\"16\":{\"anticipation\":0,\"curve\":\"linear\",\"settle\":0},\"160\":{\"action_ids\":[\"start-service\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"freight-truck\",\"origin-terminal\",\"observer\"]},\"161\":\"Its radio signal can carry more than a half-mile in streets.\",\"162\":\"Disclosed illustration of the design the university describes. The accuracy is validation accuracy from initial assessments after training, the announcement reports no field result and names no installation.\",\"163\":\"A clean thin pulse as the rings leave the antenna, thinning as they travel.\",\"164\":\"12573483d244e5631d42af7aa02d92b17406f625dd8a7bf90a8a29660b4a1684\",\"165\":\"bd368cce756d2a06e44a3602986bf00e6f2aadac71206683a2d8f4fd0fce2557\",\"166\":[\"flow-wide\",\"desk-close\",\"chart-boundary\",\"credential-gate\",\"citation-stack\",\"source-types\",\"share-grid\",\"unmeasured-card\",\"answer-close\"],\"167\":\"9ba6621f4fcec4cf50fbe2c87fdf161fa24371f9036ab663e76a823b66a0f9a8\",\"169\":\"Registered flood-station-v1 with the fresh authored FloodStationHero and StreetHubSupport groups performing board events on the film clock.\",\"17\":\"Higher-risk zones outline themselves in dashed amber and a for emergency responders tag pins.\",\"170\":\"A paper street map pinned to the chain link fence at the curb settles, streets and a creek with no pin on it.\",\"171\":\"Water lapping on steel and a small soft tone each time a mark lights.\",\"172\":\"The validation card beside the blank field result card, stamped, then the paper street map pinned to the chain link fence with blank pin holes and no pin\",\"173\":\"a9218a4fc0bed84acf53c9894d9847b004595d9ab69d76aa4d034c6b533b0da5\",\"174\":{\"label\":\"validation accuracy card reading 98.82 percent, the university reported figure\"},\"175\":\"af1001e96075fc4358426f01ef5dcf0d6d338df2a23493c4c253562ed680f9b2\",\"176\":\"Close on A technician at a folding table on the curb, the printed deployment plan, the prototype's closed carry case and the bench prototype beside it\",\"177\":\"Original designed ambience, not recorded at any San Antonio street.\",\"178\":{\"action_ids\":[\"retain-observer\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"freight-truck\",\"observer\"]},\"179\":\"Authored in this edition and type-checked; rendered pixels still need the independent code, phone and final reviews.\",\"18\":\"These low-power signals can travel more than a half-mile through city streets and up to five miles in open areas without needing cell towers or power lines. The data arrives instantly at a local central hub, where emergency teams can monitor conditions from miles away.\",\"180\":\"So far, the AI has performed well, achieving 98.82% validation accuracy in initial assessments post-training.\",\"181\":\"Four optical lenses at four different heights on the post catch the low light in turn.\",\"183\":\"A hand slides one finger along the map's creek and up a street past its blank pin holes and lifts away.\",\"184\":\"The viewer starts in the flooded yard with the late phone, then finds the station that could have warned sooner.\",\"185\":\"cf2f2ad89339249d312d5ea157c4097462a6485fa758b31d1c4ffab2a80d51a2\",\"187\":\"The dashboard assesses risk levels and shows how flooding could spread across monitored locations, highlighting higher-risk zones so local officials can act quickly.\",\"188\":\"From above, amber rings leave the station dot on the street map, the half-mile and five-mile labels appearing as each circle is reached. At street level the rings run down a long street of bungalows to the hub at its far end, and a scale bar marked more than a half-mile draws along the street. In open country rings roll out from the station in its inset to the hub's mast, the mast lamp and the hub window light as the leading ring arrives and the five-mile tag pins.\",\"19\":\"The chip lights the large amber risk lamp, the risk bar beside the board climbs from one low step to four and a judged on the station tag pins.\",\"190\":\"Our system is an off-grid solution. It generates its own power, evaluates flood risk locally right on the device and sends timely warnings without needing external electricity or expensive network lines.\",\"192\":{\"action_ids\":[\"no-town-named\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"s8-map\",\"s8-nopin\",\"s8-hand\",\"s8-tag\",\"s8-fence\"]},\"193\":\"At the hub, a second, larger AI maps flood paths for responders.\",\"194\":\"Its radio signal can carry more than a half-mile in streets. In open country, up to five miles, to a hub.\",\"195\":\"The university reports early chip AI validation. Accuracy was ninety eight point eight two percent.\",\"196\":\"Four optical lenses at four different heights on the post catch the low light in turn. Flood water rises up the post past the second, third and fourth lenses, and each lens lights in turn as the waterline crosses it. Rain, temperature, humidity and light lamps come on one by one on the housing, each with its label.\",\"198\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-15/FloodStationHero.tsx\",\"199\":\"UT San Antonio says the phone warning can come after that.\",\"2\":\"The housing window from the street as readings arrive, the chip lighting its large risk lamp and risk bar, then the distant dark server building across the road\",\"20\":\"The view cranes down from the antenna tip and reveals the whole prototype flood station at a curb, and a prototype tag pins. Low sun reaches the small dark solar panel, a glint crosses its cells and the battery bar fills cell by cell. A dashed line leaves the antenna toward a far cell tower and stops halfway, and a no cell tower needed tag pins.\",\"200\":\"0b5524473c295d96fc2d9439af0d760195ae43afddcd8813327105259d73f761\",\"201\":\"The same station's design, now measured only by the university's reported validation figure\",\"202\":\"4811590400523e197125b1f3ca735d8c54f4ea28dcd2194672a2f63060307eda\",\"203\":\"9b103e1278eeb3deba9782fbda35f9fa868afdd65354c044b258ea029ed0654a\",\"204\":\"Radio rings from above, down the street and across open country to the hub\",\"205\":\"At the central monitoring site, custom server software aggregates data from multiple deployed nodes across a town or watershed.\",\"206\":\"A small rising tone as the second optical mark goes under and lights.\",\"207\":\"A second, larger AI model analyzes spatial and temporal patterns across the network to generate an interactive web dashboard with predictive maps.\",\"208\":\"The phone on the porch rail lights its flash flood warning only now, with the water already in the yard.\",\"21\":\"The same flood station at the same curb, its lowest mark already lit by the water.\",\"210\":\"Accuracy was ninety eight point eight two percent.\",\"211\":{\"out/dispatch/sources/utsa.txt\":{\"$v\":\"355\"}},\"212\":\"Four optical sensors at different heights watch the water.\",\"214\":\"2d78478b181b5be7b12f2c705f722d887cd103a3ea12b24b8d21f55fd3c1997d\",\"215\":\"6587fccd0d4d19f4ec18f7aa43eb956fae6a9175fca73849fb397c8141be09ce\",\"217\":\"Brown water tops the limestone curb, spreads across a San Antonio yard with no station in it and climbs a chain link post to its orange ankle mark.\",\"218\":\"A disclosed design detail with no yard around it: brown water climbs over the lowest optical lens at ankle height and the lens lights as it goes under.\",\"221\":\"A small chip on the station runs the AI itself. So it judges flood risk without a central server.\",\"222\":\"The announcement reports no field result.\",\"223\":\"The same station housing, now opened, carrying the readings from the marks it just lit\",\"224\":\"A paper tap as the tag pins and a dull stamp on the blank card.\",\"226\":[{\"end\":3.58,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c1\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":0.58,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"258\"}},{\"end\":8.28,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c2\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":4.24,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"199\"}},{\"end\":11.22,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c3\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":8.96,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"31\"}},{\"end\":14.96,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c4\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":11.9,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"85\"}},{\"end\":19.14,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c5\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":15.9,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"212\"}},{\"end\":23.18,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c6\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":19.94,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"320\"}},{\"end\":26.52,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c7\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":23.8,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"128\"}},{\"end\":30.7,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c8\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":27.36,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"161\"}},{\"end\":34.74,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c9\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":31.56,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"233\"}},{\"end\":38.58,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c10\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":35.54,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":\"At the hub, a second, larger AI maps\"},{\"end\":40.24,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c11\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":38.7,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":\"flood paths for responders.\"},{\"end\":44.52,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c12\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":41.22,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"241\"}},{\"end\":48.48,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c13\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":45.24,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"210\"}},{\"end\":51.82,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c14\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":49.48,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"222\"}},{\"end\":54.8,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c15\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":52.5,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":{\"$v\":\"159\"}},{\"end\":57.36,\"end_measured\":true,\"id\":\"c16\",\"source\":\"measured_boundary\",\"start\":55.78,\"start_measured\":true,\"text\":\"Deployment is still the goal.\"}],\"227\":\"On the same notice board a hand brings a rubber stamp down onto the blank field result card, presses none reported and lifts it away. A paper street map pinned to the chain link fence at the curb settles, streets and a creek with no pin on it. A hand slides one finger along the map's creek and up a street past its blank pin holes and lifts away. An announcement names no installation tag pins beside the map.\",\"228\":\"The same brown water and the same ankle height that the station's lowest lens will mark; no station stands in this yard.\",\"229\":\"43d7449e181f