he leading ring arrives and the five-mile tag pins.\",\"271\":\"Low sun reaches the small dark solar panel, a glint crosses its cells and the battery bar fills cell by cell.\",\"272\":\"Original designed sonification, not a sound the prototype makes.\",\"273\":\"A low warm hum as the chip lights the amber risk lamp on the station.\",\"274\":\"Some people could have ankle-deep water in their yard. UT San Antonio says the phone warning can come after that.\",\"275\":\"Radio rings leave the antenna and run down a long city street to the hub at its far end, along a more than a half-mile scale bar.\",\"276\":\"Readings run in along thin traces from the four lenses and four weather sensors to one small chip, which begins to glow.\",\"277\":\"Existing commercial flood-monitoring stations also come with drawbacks, from prohibitively high costs to reliance on grid power or frequent battery replacements, which leaves them vulnerable during multi-day storms or power outages.\",\"278\":\"18a1f6b70a0008aeacd57e143a79ca5153d94d21bfb87f7ccf464641273a9c40\",\"28\":\"The prototype station revealed from its antenna down, then its panel and battery bar with a far cell tower behind\",\"280\":\"The opened housing with its traces and chip, a push in on the large risk lamp and risk bar, then the distant dark server building across the road\",\"282\":{\"action_ids\":[\"sweep-horizon\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"tower-camera\",\"dry-horizon\"]},\"283\":\"Water crosses the four sensor marks one at a time, the chip lights a risk judgment on the spot and a radio pulse carries it out to a hub.\",\"284\":\"Wide on the empty curb after the flood, the paper street map pinned to the chain link fence settles, with no pin on it.\",\"285\":\"A current clause must remain understandable with its captions covered. Introduce the spoken subject before its clause begins, perform the narrated change while it is heard, and retain the relevant result through the clause end. Distinguish selection, analysis, test condition, observed result and clinical limit. Generic clinical forms, a repeated test picture under an AI-selection line, or the normal condition under a patient-variant line fail this contract.\\n\",\"286\":\"A soft warm swell as the sun reaches the panel and small ticks as each battery cell fills.\",\"287\":\"A disclosed design detail with no yard around it: brown water climbs over the lowest optical lens at ankle height and the lens lights as it goes under. On the same ankle height the picture cuts to a San Antonio yard with no station in it, the water spreading past the orange ankle mark on a chain link post as the view pulls back. The water keeps rising to the rain boots on the porch step while the phone on the porch rail stays dark. The flash flood warning banner finally slides onto the phone, after the water is already in the yard.\",\"288\":\"Fresh original authored React and SVG illustration created for this edition; no third-party image.\",\"289\":\"A pulse flashes at the antenna tip and amber radio rings leave it.\",\"29\":{\"at_s\":5.452,\"at_s_authored\":4.916,\"clause_fraction_end\":0.56,\"clause_fraction_start\":0.3,\"duration_s\":1.0504,\"duration_s_authored\":0.9152,\"id\":\"s1-event-3\",\"item_ids\":[\"s1-phone\",\"s1-banner\"],\"motion\":{\"$v\":\"51\"},\"narration_id\":\"n1b\",\"what\":{\"$v\":\"47\"}},\"291\":\"Readings run along thin traces into one small chip in the housing, opened on its post, and in the detail framing the chip lights the large amber risk lamp and risk bar.\",\"292\":{\"action_ids\":[\"carry-radio-to-hub\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"s5-ring\",\"s5-tags\",\"s5-fivemile\",\"s5-hub\"]},\"293\":\"video-engine/src/modern/CoolingAssets.tsx\",\"294\":[\"s1\",\"s2\",\"s3\",\"s4\",\"s5\",\"s6\",\"s7\",\"s8\",\"s9\"],\"295\":{\"action_ids\":[\"restore-normal\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"normal-fly\"]},\"298\":\"44c88439942c2c40598bddd8a6d17088ed4b4eb0e1e06ffb3fac90385bb4b687\",\"299\":\"d601034eee7cce7a26257717db35f87f52e2440b8483983fda44fdfe014374be\",\"3\":\"The flood path map on the hub screen, then the desk and the responder's forearm\",\"300\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-15/FloodStationFilm.tsx\",\"301\":\"A dashed line leaves the antenna toward a far cell tower and stops halfway, and a no cell tower needed tag pins.\",\"302\":\"876c56b2a5d37aa079a6c57a359eaf0977830a3118ca9f3b7c3ebe03f5638911\",\"304\":{\"reason\":\"Hold the authored composition; the episode camera moves only with the performing water, ring or card.\",\"scale\":1,\"x\":0,\"y\":0},\"306\":\"An onboard power chip collects ambient light to charge a built-in battery and backup energy storage units, allowing the device to run indefinitely on a fraction of the energy used by a smartphone.\",\"307\":\"43e0e89ef4476b8d2ff5511e091878f9082314b80eae927e03b2d092279a3eae\",\"308\":\"5002fd2384a740e4e6eb5d56c6697776f9b96b1ff2437f5c3cb448903865ad72\",\"309\":\"Independent validator output, consolidated follow-up 3 of 3, saved unchanged in out/dispatch/evidence/validator-pass3-handback.json\",\"31\":\"So its researchers built a flood station.\",\"310\":\"The same station antenna and its risk judgment, carried out by radio toward the hub.\",\"311\":\"authored://2026-10-15/flood-station\",\"312\":\"Original designed foley, not recorded from real hardware.\",\"313\":\"565b69089f2f3355a83bc245ed7f3d0bd8b432b86af7e3614b091615ec9ac6c1\",\"314\":\"720f755d4ead7db10620a8eaf4ceb2b7d078a26861bc18fc8fe685c188b0353d\",\"316\":\"On the curb notice board an orange tape strip is pressed along the validation card's bar and the university's reported figure appears and holds. An initial assessments after training tag is pinned to the board under the validation card. The blank field result card slides onto the board beside the validation card and a pushpin presses it home.\",\"317\":{\"action_ids\":[\"show-missing-record\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"response-record\",\"empty-time-field\"]},\"318\":\"The water keeps rising to the rain boots on the porch step while the phone on the porch rail stays dark.\",\"319\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5 director, this session\",\"32\":\"d58b2dafa925f771e2f5d97bb90fe75f25dd1fe7baf5eaacf1d5f50c4c4cb101\",\"320\":\"A small chip on the station runs the AI itself.\",\"321\":\"Pan is currently pursuing patent protection for the hardware architecture.\",\"324\":\"0aaa59c0eadd355fd26348fe545c8314faa1869e7bea07a636780d9340246269\",\"326\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-09-claude-pilot/ClinicAnswerFilm.tsx\",\"327\":\"9b4db98e63d4f4306145b7fd40516a42d238a79a96c2dab2ff9e23a74e387a57\",\"328\":{\"action_ids\":[\"living-test\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"test-fly\",\"culture-vial\"]},\"33\":\"At the hub desk the dashboard fills with station dots and a responder works beside the screen.\",\"330\":\"The blank field result card slides onto the board beside the validation card and a pushpin presses it home.\",\"331\":\"The resulting prototype combines temperature, humidity, light and precipitation sensing, as well as four optical water-level sensors mounted at varying heights.\",\"332\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-11/TowerCameraHero.tsx\",\"333\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-09-claude-pilot/ChartHero.tsx\",\"334\":\"She tucks the folded plan into the front pocket of the prototype's closed carry case, beside the bench prototype station.\",\"335\":\"3758e9bcaa6364e2517e8e3c69a6eea904b5698efb427b87abad3bde99d5e88b\",\"336\":[{\"id\":\"s5-halfmile\",\"kind\":\"applicationRecord\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"more than a half mile scale bar along the street to the hub\"},\"scale\":1,\"x\":540,\"y\":900}],\"337\":\"1711186b55d89308069607d749a38a9c8740b6c6dbca433430b5f4cfc8188019\",\"339\":\"Shaded flood paths spread out from the first dots along the creek and the low streets.\",\"34\":\"6839b760ee6dd681d87e1a65e334a5b185636a98c02c3ad4b1c4505982533948\",\"340\":\"549f090d1bbafed672161f37bb2948fa94ac8caa1308773e8be6ed4cbf7c4d47\",\"341\":\"Can a flood station judge rising street water with no power line and no cell tower?\",\"342\":\"The whole prototype flood station is revealed on its post at a curb in shallow water and a prototype tag pins beside its housing.\",\"343\":\"The whole prototype station at a curb, its solar panel and battery bar, and a far cell tower\",\"344\":\"https://news.utsa.edu/2026/09/ut-san-antonio-researcher-builds-self-powered-smart-warning-system-to-catch-local-floods-before-disaster-strikes/\",\"345\":\"Researchers at The University of Texas at San Antonio have developed a self-sustaining, artificial intelligence-powered flood warning system designed to spot dangerous water accumulation at the street level.\",\"346\":[{\"id\":\"s5-antenna\",\"kind\":\"applicationRecord\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"station whip antenna sending a radio signal pulse, in the street and in an inset in open country\"},\"scale\":1,\"x\":540,\"y\":900}],\"347\":\"The same radio ring arriving as one of the station dots on the hub map.\",\"348\":{\"action_ids\":[\"carry-freight\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"freight-truck\",\"observer\"]},\"349\":\"On the same ankle height the picture cuts to a San Antonio yard with no station in it, the water spreading past the orange ankle mark on a chain link post as the view pulls back.\",\"35\":\"Pull the music back while the field result card stays blank and takes its none reported stamp.\",\"350\":\"Reflective flood water rises past the optical lenses and each lights as the waterline crosses it. In B s1 it is a disclosed design detail with no yard around it.\",\"351\":\"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/2026-10-11/TowerAlertFilm.tsx\",\"352\":\"7038e56cbed9fa0397c5caf67e0ae4b78af44721e0421f6e759199ae5b2ceacd\",\"353\":\"The design says yes. The proof so far is validation accuracy, and the announcement names no installation.\",\"354\":\"49b2379c63534c1685c5fcd480bbf0aa8cadee104811bfe9abb29cbb14f6438e\",\"355\":\"9ec493983d1b4b41a043b5eb934563ca37c64e1f98a2bb88bca90a8e49b551c9\",\"36\":\"The same station's design, now measured only by the university's reported validation figure.\",\"37\":{\"action_ids\":[\"restrict-movement\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"disabled-fly\"]},\"38\":\"The rings run down a long street of bungalows to the hub at its far end, and a scale bar marked more than a half-mile draws along the street.\",\"39\":\"At a folding table on the curb a technician folds the printed deployment plan in three along its creases. She tucks the folded plan into the front pocket of the prototype's closed carry case, beside the bench prototype station. She presses the case latch shut and takes her hand away, and a deployment goal tag hangs from the case.\",\"4\":{\"event\":{\"at\":\"2026-10-17T02:38:56.629864Z\",\"kind\":\"reserved\",\"note\":\"R15d corrective reboard: physical-water-sensor-range-map-pictures-v1 on film report f2dd8a81 (8 defects), pivot review 3 PASS\",\"preflight_identity\":null,\"resources\":{\"reboards\":1}},\"event_sha256\":\"8e0e13570cf62dc640f6e756ceb619f3b57b9669c78c79fe09ab11260b471398\",\"index\":293,\"kind\":\"production\"},\"40\":\"5a8c857d842185d738b91c00992354e1d691bf3c00e2a7bd71faa329899fe5f8\",\"41\":\"A technician at a folding table on the curb, the printed deployment plan, the prototype's closed carry case and the bench prototype beside it\",\"42\":\"authored://2026-10-15/street-hub-support\",\"43\":\"authored://2026-10-11/west-texas-support\",\"45\":\"The same station post and its four marks, the waterline rising from the first mark.\",\"46\":\"The same station housing, now opened, carrying the readings from the marks it just lit.\",\"47\":\"The flash flood warning banner finally slides onto the phone, after the water is already in the yard.\",\"49\":\"A quiet room tone at the hub and soft map shading strokes.\",\"5\":[\"c12\",\"c1\",\"c5\",\"c6\",\"c14\",\"c2\",\"c3\",\"c18\",\"c7\",\"c16\",\"c17\",\"c20\",\"c4\",\"c10\",\"c9\"],\"50\":\"Authored in this edition, type-checked and gate-checked; rendered pixels still need the independent code, phone and final reviews.\",