        "knowledge/craft/STORY_ART.md": "# Fresh relevant artwork during every storyboard\n\nDirect owner instruction from October 7th, 2026. From the effective date in\n`config/story_art.json`, generate two fresh images before animation and voice. This is a\nrequired production step: a finished hero plus supporting props or a purposeful environment.\nUse the built-in ImageGen tool and its skill. Do not silently substitute the old exceptional\nGemini background-plate lane, library boxes or a prior edition's generated artwork.\n\n## Design a useful asset set\n\nAfter selecting the earned angle, write `story_art` in the actual board, with version\n`fresh-story-art-v1` and two `requests`. Each has `id`, `role` (`hero` or `support`), the edition's\n`generated/story-art/<date>/<request-id>.png` filename, relevant `scene_ids`, a concrete `purpose`,\nthe complete generation `prompt`, and an immediate `source_limit`. Plan these images once for\nboth complete treatments. A supporting atlas can hold several separated relevant props in one\nimage; its independently movable slices must be measured against the actual output.\n\nSpecify recognizable silhouettes, rounded sculpted forms, coherent perspective, layered\nmaterials, motivated key/fill/rim light, readable surface detail and grounded contact. Match the\nstory's palette and shape language. A film about field work, policy or clinical decisions needs\ndifferent objects and a different world. Neither decorative scenery nor a familiar stock\nserver qualifies. Give every principal on-screen prop a clear story job.\n\nGenerate cutouts with genuine transparent alpha when they need to move independently. Preserve\nthe original alpha and bytes. Use an environment image only when its setting is useful and\nclearly generic. Generated art must not impersonate documentary footage, source evidence, a\nnamed real operator, an actual unobserved installation, or measured data. Render exact facts,\nlabels and captions with native verified text. Show the illustration disclosure.\n\n## Charge, generate, inspect, record\n\nRead the ImageGen skill and announce its first use. Reserve before each actual tool attempt:\n\n```sh\npython scripts/story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json reserve \\\n  --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --request <id> --out out/dispatch/art-<id>-charge.json\n```\n\nThen invoke built-in ImageGen using that exact request, inspect the returned image at native\nsize and phone size, and save its original output into the workspace. Record the actual\ngeneration identity from the tool's output filename and its actual creation time, never an\ninvented provider receipt, token usage or cost:\n\n```sh\npython scripts/story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json record \\\n  --source <original-output.png> --request <id> --generation-id <actual-tool-output-id> \\\n  --generated-at <actual-output-creation-time> --charge out/dispatch/art-<id>-charge.json\npython scripts/story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json verify\n```\n\nAll commands use the Dispatch environment wrapper. Add measured image `width` and `height`\nand, for an atlas, each named `slices` rectangle `[x,y,width,height]` to the recorded entry.\nThe record binds exact request, original bytes, edition date and prior charge. A rejected\ngeneration remains charged and retained; archive its board and image before replacing the\ncurrent request with a separately named request and asset. Keep exactly two selected assets\nin the active plan. Reuse unchanged\nassets within this edition's two treatments and mandatory repairs. Resume recorded assets\nwithout buying them again. An unfinished edition can generate its missing or corrected assets\non a later day; its reservation still belongs to that edition's original cumulative ledger.\nNo image from an earlier edition counts as fresh.\n\nThe new normal budget reserves two ImageGen calls, with a cumulative ceiling in run_limits.\nEvery failed attempt counts. Mandatory art failures use the versioned autonomous completion\npolicy and exact independent failure evidence to fund the complete remaining path. Optional\nasset polish stops at its boundary. The saved primary model, schedule and existing review\ncount remain unchanged.\n\n`deliver_run.sh` verifies and explicitly stages these exact images, even though the general\ngenerated-asset directory is ignored by Git. The clean release checkout and future review\npackets must contain the selected raster bytes. Do not commit unrelated generated files.\n\n## Make the images perform\n\nThe active episode consumes `board.story_art` through `StoryArtProvider` and `ArtSprite`, or an\nequally explicit reviewed consumer for its story. No hard-coded old image path or vector-box\nfallback is allowed. Crop an atlas in the renderer without changing original pixels. Render\nthese cutouts through Remotion's load-aware `Img` inside the crop viewport. Unmanaged SVG\n`image` tags produced missing props at the first frame of a newly mounted shot in the actual\nengineering film. The retained cold-shot regression must reject that capture and accept the\nloaded picture. Asset download or a good later still does not prove every captured frame.\nAnimate\nactual tasks with setup, contact, reaction and consequence on the global event clock. Change\nshot size and viewpoint when the new information earns it. A generated still slowly zoomed\nfor the whole narration is still a weak film.\n\nThe existing builder reports actual image consumers and known limitations. The existing phone\ncritic and three final scorers inspect visible finish, subject recognition, contact and source\ntruth on the exact film. Generate attractive art, then prove that it helps this specific story.\n",
        "config/story_art.json": "{\n  \"schema\": \"dispatch-story-art-policy/1\",\n  \"version\": \"fresh-story-art-v1\",\n  \"effective_date\": \"2026-10-08\",\n  \"tool\": \"built-in ImageGen\",\n  \"min_images\": 2,\n  \"max_images\": 2,\n  \"roles\": [\"hero\", \"support\"],\n  \"min_long_edge\": 1024,\n  \"note\": \"Generate two fresh relevant images per edition before animation: a finished hero and supporting prop atlas or purposeful environment. Share these new assets across exactly two treatments. Native overlays own exact facts and captions. Generated illustrations are disclosed and never treated as observational evidence. Charge every attempt, including rejected assets.\"\n}\n",
        "config/autonomous_completion_v2.json": "{\n  \"schema\": \"dispatch_autonomous_completion/2\",\n  \"version\": \"2026-10-08\",\n  \"effective_date\": \"2026-10-08\",\n  \"eligible_resources\": [\"reboards\", \"storyboard_critics\", \"preflight_renders\", \"full_renders\", \"audiovisual_reviews\", \"panel_rounds\", \"scorer_calls\", \"tts_calls\", \"voice_directors\", \"image_generations\"],\n  \"mandatory_scopes\": [\"finish-current\", \"retained-integrity\", \"minimum-action\", \"modern-film-floor\"],\n  \"excluded_work\": [\"optional creative polish\", \"new research\", \"extra treatment\", \"director review of own film\"],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"Preserve the original frozen envelope, cumulative charges and exact failed evidence.\",\n    \"Fund the complete remaining code, fresh story art, silent phone, final timed phone, native, audiovisual, scoring and delivery path before mandatory correction.\",\n    \"Record exact conservative capacity deficits separately; capacity never approves a film.\",\n    \"Reserve every actual image-generation, provider and render attempt before execution.\",\n    \"Current films cannot return to a legacy renderer or defer the modern engagement and artwork floor.\",\n    \"Retain all source, rights, minimum action, native PNG/CRF16, audio, caption, independent review and shipment gates.\",\n    \"Old policy bytes and already frozen ledgers remain reproducible.\"\n  ],\n  \"authorization_statement\": \"The owner requires a substantial modern film upgrade and fresh relevant ImageGen artwork during each run's storyboard stage. The standing autonomous shipment instruction funds mandatory current-route repair, including fresh story-art failures. Optional polish stops at its boundary; original ledgers and failed evidence remain intact.\",\n  \"authorization_source_label\": \"Direct owner instructions on October 7th, 2026, including mandatory fresh storyboard images\",\n  \"owner_source_text_sha256\": \"00329fb90ccefe54e8314977b63b790756ef18d45ecd36bd4526762e28a30d68\"\n}\n",
        "knowledge/craft/AUTHORED_STORY_ART.md": "# Fresh authored story pictures\n\nThe owner selected this Claude substitute on October 9th, 2026. It applies only to a board with\n`story_art.version` set to `authored-story-art-v1` and runtime `claude-sonnet-v1`. Older boards\ncontinue to use their original raster ImageGen policy. The finished-art, modern engagement and\nindependent rendered observations remain unchanged.\n\nCreate two original story-specific source groups, hero and support, in\n`video-engine/src/modern/episodes/<edition-id>/`. Use source-bound physical actions to choose the\nforms. Design recognizable silhouettes, purposeful surface detail, coherent perspective and\nlighting, grounded weight and contact, and a performed answer. Use the current regional stage.\nShared primitives can support the work; a renamed old hero or untouched decorative module is not\nfresh story artwork. No previous edition's footage or generated art becomes this edition's hero.\n\nThe board's `story_art` plan has `version`, `runtime`, `edition_id`, exactly two `requests` and\nexactly two recorded `entries`. Each request declares `id`, `role`, source `file`, named `export`,\n`scene_ids`, the directed `prompt`, `purpose`, `source_limit` and concrete `action_uses`. An action\nuse declares `scene_id`, `event_id`, `view`, `action_id` and `subject_ids`. Bind each to the actual\nscene event, directed shot and registry narration view. Register the two files in the episode's\n`assets` and its `authored_art` rows, each with `role`, `module`, `export` and implemented `views`.\nUse those exports in the episode's actual source. Keep the full renderer closure hash-bound.\n\nReserve the existing builder reboard before authoring either group. That one actual worker can\ncreate both source groups; it is not two external image calls. Do not consume `image_generations`\nor invent generation ids, image sizes, PNG source files or image-service charges. Record actual\nsource file creation times, exact bytes, unique creation identities, current claims and the prior\nbuilder reservation through the helper. It retains original modules and receipts in scratch;\nlater corrections must retain those actual failures and cumulative charges.\n\n```sh\npython scripts/authored_story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json record --state out/dispatch/run_state.json\npython scripts/authored_story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json verify\npython scripts/story_art.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json stage\n```\n\nShare the two source groups across exactly two complete treatments. Both phone films execute the\ndeclared actions. Before narration inspect their actual pictures with labels covered, identify\nthe principal subject and result, and select the stronger chain. A module, export, receipt or\naction id proves a binding only. The existing critic, native hero review, three audiovisual\nlenses and three final scorers judge the current pixels and audible performance. Reject unused\ndecoration, generic boxes, static slideshow sequences and ambiguous physical contact.\n\nPreserve the current caption, source, rights, timing, modern engagement, native PNG/CRF16 and\nshipment gates. The substitute changes the artwork's origin, not the finished film standard.\n",
        "config/authored_story_art.json": "{\n  \"version\": \"authored-story-art-v1\",\n  \"runtime\": \"claude-sonnet-v1\",\n  \"effective_date\": \"2026-10-09\",\n  \"roles\": [\"hero\", \"support\"],\n  \"tool\": \"original authored source\",\n  \"namespace\": \"video-engine/src/modern/episodes/\",\n  \"note\": \"Owner-authorized Claude substitute for unavailable ImageGen. Two original source asset groups perform current story actions in exactly two complete treatments. Existing builder reservations fund actual authoring. Independent pixel review and every modern film floor remain required. Historical raster editions retain their original policy.\"\n}\n",
        "prompts/claude_routine.md": "# Texas AI Dispatch on Claude\n\nOwner directive, October 9th, 2026. This is the Claude host entry point. Read the current\n`prompts/dispatch_routine.md` and execute its five phases in full, loading each phase and its\nrequired contracts when entering it. This entry point replaces only the host routing, unavailable\nImageGen service and local workspace bootstrap. Every source, rights, action, modern film, audio,\ncaption, independent scoring, native rendering and shipment requirement remains in force.\n\n## One outcome\n\nCreate a great fresh Texas film and ship it. Continue through the controller's mandatory recovery\nuntil `finish --result shipped` accepts current release evidence, canonical phone playback and a\ncorrectly addressed, read-back unsent Gmail draft. Verify its durable public-safe archive too.\nNever send email or post socially. A cloud session marked successful is not shipment evidence.\nNever fabricate a review, replace a rejected verdict, discard charges, or loosen an integrity gate.\n\nThe owner's October 16th instruction forbids routine permission stops. When an internal tool,\npacket, review, storage or controller defect blocks the next command, retain the actual error,\nrepair its owning code in a clean isolated checkout, run the narrow regression and required CI,\nmerge the repair, and resume the same edition autonomously. Use standing completion capacity\nfor mandatory deficits. An internal repair never needs another owner approval. Keep account\nfunding, credentials, sends and destructive history outside this authority. Notify an external\ndependency failure once, retain its executable recovery, and resume on restored access; never\ncall the run successful or shipped while a required gate is missing.\n\nThe owner explicitly requested Sonnet as director and original authored graphics instead of the\nbuilt-in image service that Claude does not provide. Apply `config/claude_runtime.json` to newly\nplanned Claude editions. Do not retrofit this policy into historical or unfinished frozen runs.\nHistorical October 8th and October 9th films keep their original exact bytes and evidence.\n\n## Wake and safe edition selection\n\nUse a clean current `origin/main` checkout of `Talonsturgill/TexasAIDispatch`, alongside\n`Talonsturgill/TexasAIDocket`. Preserve any unrelated work. Read `CLAUDE.md` and the existing\nworklog. Cloud worklogs belong in `out/dispatch/WORKLOG.md`; protected settings are edited through\nthe repository's bootstrap tooling, never by requesting a daily approval.\n\nRun every Dispatch shell command through `bash scripts/run_with_env.sh`. In a worktree explicitly\n`cd` into that worktree inside the wrapped shell. Configure the owner's Git identity from\n`CLAUDE.md`; never append assistant attribution. Required bindings come from the routine's\nexisting environment, never source files or printed secrets. Validate voice, full FFmpeg/FFprobe,\nfonts, locked dependencies, managed browser, audiovisual provider and the connected Gmail profile\nbefore any paid production work. Install only missing or changed pinned dependencies. Local\nworkspace housekeeping is used when available. Cloud uses scripts/dispatch_housekeeping.py with\nthe same protection rules and its actual two checkout paths; never delete active or unrelated work.\n\nThe Texas environment must run `scripts/claude_environment_setup.sh` before Claude Code launches.\nSetup supplies truthful selected-repository and application-durability context in Claude's user\nsettings through `claude_environment_context.py`. It preserves all permission rules, defaults,\nhooks, model, effort and bindings; project settings do not supply auto-mode context. Retain the\nhelper's preservation receipt and use `claude auto-mode config` to verify the effective context\non a fresh host. Keep existing credential and no-send boundaries.\nThe saved prelaunch setup includes this command before Claude starts:\n\n```sh\nbash scripts/run_with_env.sh python3 scripts/claude_environment_context.py --workspace /home/user --apply\n```\n\nThe versioned setup provisions pinned tools and registers the workspace capture router once,\nbefore auto mode begins. Do not attempt mid-session registration or repeat a classifier-denied\ninstallation. Preserve the denied command evidence and use a fresh supported routine launch\nafter the environment setup is corrected. Setup success does not prove a loaded hook; retain\nthe actual harmless probe denial before production capture.\n\nIn a fresh Linux cloud checkout run the idempotent setup, then re-enter the wrapper so its\nexternal cache is active. The first command installs only absent or changed pinned tools;\nthe second actually proves voice/alignment and render access before reservations:\n\n```sh\nbash scripts/run_with_env.sh python3 scripts/cloud_bootstrap.py --bind-only\nbash scripts/run_with_env.sh python scripts/cloud_bootstrap.py\nbash scripts/run_with_env.sh python scripts/claude_contract_check.py\n```\n\nResolve the actual sibling checkout paths and their shared workspace parent. Run the versioned\nhousekeeping helper at startup and after the verified shipped archive:\n\n```sh\nbash scripts/run_with_env.sh python scripts/dispatch_housekeeping.py --workspace <shared-parent> --dispatch-repo <actual-dispatch-checkout> --docket-repo <actual-docket-checkout> --apply --fetch --summary\n```\n\nBefore every native render, calculate scripts/native_headroom.py on the current board, then repeat\nthat housekeeping command with --require-headroom --min-free-gib set to its required_free_gib.\nRetain at least two completed packages. Missing process inspection or unverifiable archives never\nauthorize cleanup; recover the actual capacity condition through the controller.\n\nRead knowledge/craft/AUTHORED_STORY_ART.md and config/authored_story_art.json during the\npicture phase. Use its actual record, verify and stage commands. There is no ImageGen call\nin this lane and no fabricated image-generation charge.\n\nRun `run_controller.py pending` and resume the oldest unfinished production before making a new\nedition. A cloud container is reclaimed, so `pending` alone sees only worktrees that still exist.\nAlso run `python scripts/claude_checkpoint.py discover`. Select the OLDEST unfinished edition by its run identity and creation time\n(`claude_checkpoint.py discover --oldest-unfinished`, never the first row of the newest-save-first list)\nand resume its existing ledger. It is restored\nwith `python scripts/claude_checkpoint.py restore --run-id <id> --dest <new empty directory>`. That\ncreates an isolated checkout of the recorded source commit (the complete committed renderer, art and\npublic closure), overlays the verified scratch outputs and uncommitted source, and rebuilds the same\nledger, frozen envelope, charges, failed reviews and paid outputs with its paths moved. It never\ntouches another checkout or an existing ledger, has no force option, and refuses a finished edition.\nBind its exact lockfile dependencies from the preinstalled environment using the current\n`scripts/cloud_bootstrap.py --bind-only --repo <restored-checkout>` helper, then resume.\nImmediately after restore, before any paid worker reservation, run that binding through the\ncurrent-main wrapper, then explicitly cd into the restored checkout inside the wrapped shell\nand run its `python scripts/env_check.py --require-voice`. Retain both exit codes. The wake\ncheck on the primary checkout is not a runtime check on the restored checkout. A missing\nPython import, Node module, browser or pinned alignment tool must be repaired from the\npreinstalled cache before a paid builder or render. Never use a scratch tsconfig or scratch\nsource copy as a substitute for the production checkout's actual typecheck. Run the actual\n`cd video-engine && npx tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` before accepting a builder hand-back.\nNever initialise a second\nledger for an edition that has a checkpoint.\n\nBefore authorizing capture in a restored or nested worktree, establish a real clean Docket\ncheckout at `<dispatch-checkout-parent>/TexasAIDocket`, starting at current origin/main. An owned\nisolated clone or a suitable registered worktree satisfies this requirement.\nThe capture helper runs housekeeping against that sibling and their shared parent. A symlink to\nthe primary Docket checkout fails the bounded-workspace check. Preserve the primary checkout and\nall unrelated or dirty work; use this owned sibling for the narrow Dispatch feed release. Retain\nany failed path inspection and its charged reservation, then verify the normal housekeeping gate.\n\nDerive today's calendar date in the schedule timezone from config/claude_runtime.json;\nthe cloud host's UTC date does not select an Eastern edition. A terminal shipped run is immutable.\nThe first owner-authorized migration test uses a\nfresh current story and an intentional distinct run identity `<today>-claude-pilot`, including its\nown branch, scratch, permanent media, feed identity, draft and archive. The board's calendar date\nis still today. Run this migration pilot only if no prior Claude pilot has accepted `shipped`\nstatus and a verified durable archive in `runs/`. Resume an unfinished pilot instead of creating\nanother. After that one pilot is archived, every scheduled invocation uses normal daily production.\nNormal scheduled production uses today's date. If today's scheduled film is\nalready shipped, verify that shipment and do not manufacture another ordinary edition.\n\n## Durable checkpoints and effective effort\n\n`out/` is gitignored and dies with the container. For an edition marked by\n`out/dispatch/claude-host.json`, every controller ledger write is mirrored to\n`claude/checkpoint/<run-id>` before the writer returns, so each reservation is durable before its\npaid call is dispatched. After each paid call returns and its output is on disk, the same mirror\nruns again through the next ledger write, and `python scripts/claude_checkpoint.py save --note <what>`\ncovers outputs written without one. Prefer `claude_checkpoint.py guard --note <what> -- <paid command>`,\nwhich makes state durable, runs the command and makes its outputs durable, and exits 75 when it can't.\nA checkpoint that cannot be made after storage and transport recovery writes\n`out/dispatch/checkpoint-unbacked.json`, raises, and blocks every new reservation until\n`claude_checkpoint.py recover` succeeds. Never continue paid work on an unbacked ledger.\nThe controller also verifies the current snapshot before it changes any reservation counter.\nIf a newer writer already advanced the remote edition, this stale invocation preserves its\nunchanged ledger and failed evidence without buying another attempt. Keep the newer checkpoint\nauthoritative, preserve both hosts, and resume that edition through the existing restoration and\ncontinuation workflow. Never overwrite newer history or repeat the paid command from the stale host.\n\nThe checkpoint keeps the sanitized ledger, authored source, claims, board, voice takes, alignment,\nreview responses, failed images and every receipt. It skips only known rebuildable directories\n(frames, tmp, cache). It leaves out Gmail, routing and credential material by any path component or\ndata structure, redacts shipped Gmail identifiers and local paths from the ledger, refuses to save when\na credential value appears, and refuses any save that would lower usage, limits or increments, change the\nfrozen envelope or alter the earlier event history. A file too large to retain fails the save visibly.\nFrom the October 17 edition, the cinema producer creates its duplicate render cache under\n`out/dispatch/tmp/cinema-render-cache`. Canonical proof images, hero, provenance and every failed\nproof remain under `cinema/` and are retained. Earlier editions keep their original cache path.\nAfter `finish --result shipped` and the metadata archive, save once more so the checkpoint reads finished.\n\nImmediately after selecting or restoring the production ledger, arm its preinstalled completion\nguard through the current checkout. Resolve the actual primary workspace parent, then run:\n\n```sh\nbash scripts/run_with_env.sh python scripts/routine_continuation.py --workspace <shared-parent> --arm out/dispatch/run_state.json\n```\n\nRepeat this after a later restoration too. If the earlier armed path no longer exists, the\nhelper can retarget the same edition only after verifying the immutable checkpoint ledger,\nunchanged frozen envelope and complete cumulative event history. It retains a rebind audit.\nA live earlier ledger or another edition stays protected. Do not hand-edit the marker or\nre-register hooks to get around a refused rebind.\n\nThe prelaunch Stop hook sends an early final response back to this same ledger. It approves no\ntool, changes no permissions and adds no capacity. It remains inactive for ordinary coding and\nleaf agents. Collect required task results through the actual task tools, repair internal failures\nthrough the versioned routes, and continue until accepted shipment, the matching public archive\non fetched origin/main, and the final shipped checkpoint exist. Do not re-register hooks in a\nrunning host. A supported fresh environment can prove the actual event with\n`routine_continuation.py --workspace <shared-parent> --probe` before any production is armed;\nthat one-shot nonproduction probe creates no ledger and cannot replace an armed production run.\n\nAt wake also record `python scripts/claude_contract_check.py --effective out/dispatch/effective-effort.json`.\nIt reads the root session's host effort, any `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` override, and each leaf's\nfrontmatter. Fail on a mismatch; never set a global effort override.\n\n## Claude-native worker routing\n\nThe director is `claude-sonnet-5-5` at medium effort. Read the exact role map from\n`config/claude_runtime.json`; do not use Codex `spawn_args` in Claude's Agent tool. Use the existing\nrole roster, adding only the named `scene-builder` leaf definition for the existing builder task.\nPin exact model ids and supported effort in versioned agent frontmatter and project settings.\nThe owner refined the route on October 9th: scene-builder, storyboard-critic and validator use\nOpus 5.5 at high effort. These calls own the authored picture, its independent critique and source\ntruth. Research and voice direction remain Haiku high; three separate final scorers remain\nSonnet medium. The director stays Sonnet medium. Measure rework and quality before claiming that\nthe stronger creative workers reduced total run cost.\nSpawn `scene-builder` for the existing reserved two-treatment builder assignment, using\n`.claude/agents/scene-builder.md` and `prompts/roles/scene-builder.md`. Reuse it for corrections.\nDo not globally force `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` to medium, because that overrides the leaf's high\neffort. Detect and report any inherited override and resolve it before worker execution.\n\nGive each worker a compact current packet with actual input paths and SHA256 bindings, the\nrelevant phase, full current guide text and hashes, role brief and exact rubric. Isolate its\nconversation. Every assignment says to do the work itself and launch no additional agents.\nReserve its actual controller resource before starting. Reuse the builder and critic for bounded\nfollow-ups, consolidate linked defects and keep one render owner. Three final scorer responses\nremain distinct identities and an atomic charged panel on the same finished film. The director\ncannot count self-review as independence. Provider recovery is used only after actual observed\nhost unavailability, under the existing recovery policy.\n\nWhile a background worker owns required work, use the host's supported task-status and output\ntools to wait for that exact task and collect its full handback. Do not end the response merely\nto say that you are yielding or waiting; continue the next owned production step when its\nresult arrives. Confirm the task is actually running before waiting, and explicitly resume a\ncompleted worker when assigning new charged content work. Keep one active owner and never\ndispatch a duplicate because a response is slow. An unfinished controller is still active\nproduction even when the cloud UI marks an assistant response successful.\n\n## Fresh authored picture lane\n\nFollow Alaska's strongest production methods in `Talonsturgill/alaska-ai-weekly`: recognizable\nstory-specific cast and equipment, motivated depth, physical actions and consequences, sound\nconnected to the picture, varied useful framing, early earned changes and a performed ending.\nInspect the current source and shipped film; never copy Alaska's history, dedupe ledger, footage,\nplace or character defaults. Texas place, source-bound actions and house voice remain Texas.\n\nCreate exactly two fresh relevant authored asset groups, hero and support, shared by exactly two\ncomplete visual treatments. Build finished recognizable forms with coherent perspective, regional\npalette, motivated lighting, surface detail and believable contact. Original SVG, React/CSS-depth\nand Three.js through the current Remotion engine are allowed. Do not imitate ImageGen metadata or\nclaim an external generation happened. Record actual creation time, exact source module bytes,\nedition identity, source claim hashes, declared exports and each performed on-screen use. Bind the\ncomplete renderer dependency closure. Changed shared parts do not become fresh artwork by renaming\nthem. A reused prior-edition hero, unused decorative asset, generic boxes, slideshow or legacy\nwhole-episode rescue fails the new lane.\n\nImplement the authored lane as a dated, explicit Claude opt-in, retaining the original raster\nImageGen policy and all historical tests. Its mechanical gate must reject missing/stale modules,\nunrelated sources, absent current action use, repeated old asset identities and unresolved imports.\nThe existing independent phone, native hero and exact-film reviews judge the actual pixels under\nall seven modern observations. Mechanically correct bindings do not establish visual quality.\nRetain the active `directed-film-v2` route and complete source/event/clause-bound shot timeline.\n\nProve both complete silent phone treatments before voice, then measured timed phone, native hero\nwith sound, final cut, all audiovisual lenses, panel and delivery. Before native renders calculate\nthe complete uncompressed PNG frame set plus retained-output reserve with `native_headroom.py`.\nRecover only eligible storage if the actual plan lacks room. Never lower native 1080x1920 capture,\nPNG, CRF16 or mandatory reviews. Reserve every actual attempt before execution. Fund the complete\nremaining review and delivery path before correcting a failed cut. Keep the frozen envelope,\ncumulative usage, individual authorized increments and exact failure evidence.\n\nFor an independently rejected mandatory code defect before a film exists, use the merged\ncode-evidence amendment in knowledge/craft/AUTONOMOUS_COMPLETION.md. Keep the original failed\nreport and before-files. Bind a new plan with scripts/autonomous_completion.py\n--prepare-code-plan <original-plan> --claims <claims> --output <new-plan>, then run the controller's\nproduction-budget and completion-capacity on that new plan before beginning its correction.\nThis preserves the original frozen adoption and adds only exact conservative deficits.\nCode evidence cannot approve pixels or replace either complete phone treatment or final reviews.\nDo not request a daily decision at the internal critic ceiling.\n\nAfter an independent passing code review, stop optional editing. If contract failures consumed\nthe funded reviews, use the actual new independent passing report in a finish-current plan with\nno changed_inputs. The adopted code route protects two pending phone critics. Run production-budget\nand completion-capacity on that new finish plan, retaining every prior failure, grant and charge.\nDo not retry the original failure's grant or replace a film verdict with code approval.\n\n## Efficiency and actual usage\n\nFinal Read-only scorers use the complete exact-film motion-image sequence documented in\nprompts/phases/04-review.md. Build and verify it before creating their three compact packets.\nThese film-decoded images provide chronological visual access; retain separate actual\naudiovisual receipts for movement and sound. Never pretend that Read plays an MP4 or hears it.\nPreserve prior unknown access findings, fund the complete path and reserve the new atomic panel\nbefore a content resume. Do not repeatedly purchase schema-only replies for missing media access.\n\nIf the already charged exact-phone Opus worker exceeds one hour and two supported host\nobservations at least five minutes apart show unchanged tool/token totals and no error, load\nconfig/autonomous_completion_handback_v1.json. Preserve the original native status evidence,\ntask ID and reservation. Use scripts/review_handback.py to bind that receipt, the unchanged\napproved board, claims, both exact films, original packet and output contract to the retained\nfinish-current plan. Normal completion-capacity may grant exactly one separately recorded\ncritic increment once per run, only when every other remaining resource is funded. This is\nsame-worker handback capacity, never host unavailability or approval. Reserve the resumed\ncritic call before director TaskStop, wait for its stopped run to exit, then SendMessage to\nthat exact ID for the complete bounded report using its original context and prompt cache.\nKeep Opus High, every required guide and observation, the final timed critic and all release\ngates. Do not use manual UI cancellation, a new Agent, another provider or a new correction.\n\nKeep phase loading, compact assignments, exact-byte audiovisual caching including failures, and\nthe current provider media deduplication. Run cheap mechanical checks before paid review. Group\ndependent production commands into one exit-code-checked job with retained logs and a compact\nsummary, stopping at the first mandatory failure. Use exact job handles and completion markers;\navoid repeated full-context polling. Use supported nonblocking worker status or waits of at most\n60 seconds; do not block steering or completed handbacks with long Bash sleep loops. Reuse the\nsame worker for output-format corrections with exact gate errors. Give it the current report\ncontract and computed bindings before execution; use bounded gate-function excerpts for missing\nformat details instead of rereading entire controller modules. Every required guide, source,\nexact film and independent observation stays in scope. Continue independent work while a render\nruns. Never end the turn with a promise to perform the next phase.\n\nFor a GitHub PR CI wait, use the native `claude-code-remote: subscribe pr activity` tool on the\nexact owning repository and PR, and retain its actual external-event wake acknowledgment.\nA turn may yield to that registered wake or a real background task; production stays open and\nmust resume through shipped and durable closure. Recheck the exact head and every required\nconclusion after waking. For post-merge deployment, retain the actual workflow and process\nhandles; a merged PR alone does not prove a deployment. Never wait with `pgrep -f` on a substring\nof the wait shell's own command. Retain completed check receipts and stop only a confirmed\nobsolete wait. Keep long command output in its log and return the producer's exit code plus a\nshort tail. Use `set -euo pipefail` for Bash command chains, or explicitly capture and check each\nproducer status before continuing. A successful `tail` never establishes that synthesis,\nsoundcheck, alignment, rendering or a delivery gate passed. Retain the full failure log.\n\nIf the critic's own handback admits unread mandatory guides or incomplete boards, retain it and\nhold capture. Use the review-coverage amendment in AUTONOMOUS_COMPLETION.md on the unchanged\nproduction inputs. Fund the complete path, charge the resumed review and SendMessage to the same\nOpus High worker for full coverage. This is content review, not a free formatting correction or\nhost unavailability. Never request a policy decision at that internal ceiling.\nPrepare its evidence-bound plan with `python scripts/review_coverage.py --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --receipt <actual-receipt> --report <original-handback> --original-packet <original-packet> --current-packet <current-packet> --output <new-plan>`\nthrough scripts/run_with_env.sh, then use the documented production-budget and completion-capacity\ncommands before reserving the resumed review.\n\nA complete code critic can also prove a nondeferrable modern motion, surface finish, pacing or\nending-artistry failure before any film exists. For an actual renderer-only rejection, retain\nthe report and baseline and run `python scripts/modern_code_recovery.py --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --plan <original-proposal> --packet <current-complete-code-packet> --output <new-bound-plan>`\nthrough scripts/run_with_env.sh. Follow AUTONOMOUS_COMPLETION.md for the separate pinned modern\ncode adoption, complete-path funding, recurrence pivot when required, precharged Opus correction,\nstrict derived board rebinds and both fresh phone reviews. Do not invent a board story edit,\nrelabel the reviewer or request an owner decision at this internal admission boundary.\n\nIf an actual charged same-worker recurrence pivot returns REVISE before that funded correction,\nretain its exact handback and rejected proposal. Use `python scripts/pivot_recovery.py --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --receipt <actual-receipt> --report <retained-pivot-rejection> --rejected-proposal <reviewed-proposal> --revised-plan <bound-modern-plan> --output <new-recovery-plan>`\nthrough scripts/run_with_env.sh and follow the receipt and funding procedure in\nAUTONOMOUS_COMPLETION.md. Charge the next same Opus High pivot review before SendMessage.\nIts independent source-backed PASS remains required before begin-repair or any production edit.\n\nUse compact frame strips for director decisions and native crops when detail decides the result.\nIndependent reviewers still receive the exact current film and every required unique media byte.\nStop optional polish at the configured creative boundary; mandatory failures recover through the\nexisting source-backed pivot. Stop engineering unrelated to this film after the reserved boundary.\nMeasure actual Claude input, cache creation/read and output tokens by phase and worker, external\nprovider usage separately, retries, scores, first-panel result, runtime and accepted shipment.\nDeduplicate transcript content blocks by API message identity. Never equate list prices or account\nusage percentages with the actual bill, and never claim a tenfold saving or quality improvement\nwithout measured comparable evidence. Refresh the separate next-five-edition observations.\nAt entry to each phase run `python scripts/claude_runtime.py phase <phase-name>`. These private\nUTC markers establish observed phase timing; missing transcript fields stay unknown.\n\n## Initial migration implementation and end-to-end test\n\nThe first Claude invocation is authorized to finish this migration before production. If the\nClaude host adapter is not implemented yet, inspect the current Alaska pipeline and implement the\nsmallest complete adapter in this repository: supported leaf model/effort binding, idempotent cloud\nenvironment setup, controller-compatible compact packets, fresh authored art receipts and gates,\nrenderer support, usage accounting, and a contract check. Wire the adapter into the master, phase\nfiles, builder/reviewer briefs and required CI. Do not remove old policies or tests to make it pass.\nRequired historical isolation must be tested with the already-shipped October 8th/9th evidence.\nTest negative authored inputs and a valid actual render through the existing narrow gates.\n\nKeep engineering telemetry separate from the new production ledger. Commit only intended public\nsource and instructions; push, open a ready PR, obtain exact-head required CI and merge, then verify\nmatching-main CI. The daily saved prompt remains a thin current-main pointer. Once implementation\nis merged, perform the still-unfinished pilot in this same actual Sonnet cloud run; if its accepted\nshipment and durable archive already exist, proceed with normal daily production instead.\nDo not stop after the engineering\nPR, a preview, a passing panel or an uploaded file. Complete the original five-phase master through\nverified accepted shipment, the unsent draft and durable archive. Report the film, scores, actual\nusage, delivery state and any retained failed attempts concisely.\n\n## Canonical phone playback on the cloud host\n\n### Complete silent phone evidence before voice\n\nImage delivery is load-aware for every Claude phone and final image-only reviewer. The host\nhas actually stripped image results from large Read batches. A complete index on disk does\nnot prove that the model received its pages. The current packet pins one image Read per model\nstep, no parallel image Reads, and concrete per-page notes before the next Read. Read full\nguides and all chronological pages, retaining the actual textual notes as older images leave\nthe host window. Never infer an unseen image from code or earlier stills. Return partial\nimmediately on a stripped image; do not repeat bulk reads. First smoke-test one known missing\npage when recovering an observed delivery failure, then continue the complete sequence only\nif it is actually visible. This is part of the separately charged content follow-up, not a\nnew uncharged review or a creative approval.\n\nEach worker also returns its separate `dispatch_claude_image_coverage/1` object following the\npacket's contract. Save that actual response unchanged and run:\n\n```sh\npython scripts/claude_runtime.py verify-images --packet <exact worker packet> --coverage <retained coverage JSON> --out <coverage verification JSON>\n```\n\nRequire complete coverage before accepting a Claude image-only phone pass or final scorer handback. The check\nbinds the packet, every index/page byte, chronological page identities and retained concrete\nobservations. It never supplies a finding, score or approval. Retain partial reports and\nfailed coverage checks exactly; their missing images are access failures, not invented film\ndefects. Fund the complete remaining path and reserve the same worker's bounded content\nfollow-up autonomously; never end with a request to choose between charging and waiting.\nKeep coverage objects and verification receipts with current review evidence in the\ncheckpoint and public-safe metadata archive. Coverage verification starts no worker. Image\nextraction keeps its prepaid capture charge; every actual content follow-up remains reserved\nbefore execution. A known host\nimage delivery failure uses this small-read path first, without inventing provider unavailability.\n\nIf the actual single-image attempt still returns exactly `[media removed: request limit]`, retain\nthat observed host media-limit error, the original charged role reservation, and `media_probe`\nreferences for the exact image, packet, failed coverage and corrected full handback. Each reference\nhas path and SHA256; set `single_image_read: true` and `media_received: false`, and preserve the\nliteral error as both `error` and `raw_error`. Do not rename it to a different capacity error.\nThe configured independent transport admits this precise case only with the real owned bytes,\nthe current single-read packet and an actual unseen-page coverage entry. Artistic rejection,\na missing file, a resource boundary and an untested bulk read do not qualify. No more native\ncontent retries are needed after this observed single-image delivery failure.\n\nUse the deterministic preparation command to bind the latest actual native role reservation\nand existing evidence. It records the observed failure and starts no new worker or provider:\n\n```sh\npython scripts/independent_review.py --prepare-media-limit --role phone --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json --claims out/dispatch/claims.json --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --actor <actual failed worker id> --source-packet <original failed packet> --coverage <actual failed coverage JSON> --handback <original corrected handback> --probe-image <actual stripped PNG> --compare-openings --out <new failure JSON>\n```\n\nFor the initial comparison, use the existing provider under its ordinary charged transport:\n\n```sh\npython scripts/independent_review.py --role phone --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json --claims out/dispatch/claims.json --failure <retained transport failure JSON> --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --compare-openings --selection-out out/dispatch/openings/selection.json --out out/dispatch/provider-phone-report.json\n```\n\nThis attaches BOTH exact movies and both complete boards, the actual source evidence and full\ncurrent guides. The provider independently chooses a or b and returns separate complete phone\nreports for both. The transport projects the selected original report and selection mechanically;\nit changes no verdict, score, finding or chosen option. Verify both artifacts with\n`independent_review.py --verify <artifact.json>`, then stage the chosen original board/movie and\napply the existing phone gates. A provider rejection remains a rejection and uses normal funded\nmandatory repair. Cached comparison media cannot be repurchased by changing labels or guide prose.\nThe actual direct-video provider response and its verified provenance replace the unavailable\nClaude image-access receipt; all seven observations, source, rights, native, audio, caption and\nshipment gates remain. Later timed-phone and final-role fallback use the ordinary exact-film\ntransport only after their own observed assigned-host failure. Keep three separate final scorer\nresponses and their actual atomic panel charges. Preserve the primary model and saved schedule.\n\nFor an observed provider HTTP 402 with no response or verdict, use the restored-generation\nprocedure in prompts/phases/review-availability.md after external service recovery. Retain the\noriginal request and charge. No billing purchase or completed-verdict retry is authorized.\n\nFor current provider inputs use config/independent_packet_compaction.json. Run artifacts are\nlossless structured JSON; complete treatment documents may be encoded as checked JSON-pointer\ndeltas against the complete common board. Preserve original byte hashes and verify reconstruction\nbefore sending. Current guides stay original full text, source evidence and receipts stay complete,\nand all unique media stays attached. For pixel review, only registered inactive episode source\noutside every selected executable closure may become a hash inventory. Code review retains full\ncallable source. At phone pixel scope, source bodies may become exact hash inventories only after\nthe ordinary code gate verifies actual independent code-plan passes for every current board and\nboth treatments against current concepts, renderer bytes and claims. Carry those complete original\nreports into the phone packet. Missing or stale code approval keeps the full source. Those code\npasses supply no pixel observation, selection or film approval. Full boards, source evidence and\nguides remain. The complete episode registry is structured JSON with every field, its original\nbyte hash and all entries retained. Use compact JSON whitespace on the wire. The same text-size ceiling is enforced on\nthe final request after comparison context and retained failure evidence are added. No new provider\ncharge begins on an oversized input. Historical packets retain their original contents and policy.\n\nThe Read-only Opus phone critic cannot play MP4s or compute missing hashes with Bash.\nOne midpoint still per scene cannot prove timed motion or continuity. After both structural\nopening inspections pass, extract the complete chronological sequence from each exact encoded\n270 by 480 preview with `claude_motion_review.py --phone-option a` and then `--phone-option b`.\nFor each option use its canonical `--board out/dispatch/openings/a.json` and matching\n`--film out/dispatch/openings/a.mp4` (or b), `--state out/dispatch/run_state.json`, and a fresh\n`--out out/dispatch/openings/motion-a` (or b). Use the ordinary wrapped capture authorization\nwith `--prepare` and that exact board/command. Each extraction reserves one preflight before\ndecoding, and claims its consumed authorization once without another charge. Headroom,\nhousekeeping, authored art and all hook protections still apply. Never use the native final\nprofile on a phone movie or present a phone index as final native evidence.\n\nBuild the normal current `daily_production.py --packet storyboard-critic` packet, then:\n\n```sh\npython scripts/claude_runtime.py phone-packet --packet out/dispatch/critic-packet.json --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --sequence-a out/dispatch/openings/motion-a/index.json --sequence-b out/dispatch/openings/motion-b/index.json --out out/dispatch/phone-critic-packet.json\n```\n\nPlan the existing storyboard critic with that packet and an explicit phone scope. The planner\nrefuses missing, changed or incomplete movie-derived imagery and computes the report bindings\nbefore the paid call. The critic reads every chronological page for both options and returns\nits independent selection and exact-phone report as JSON in the handback. The director saves\nthe actual response unchanged; Read-only leaves cannot write files. No extraction or mechanical\nhash supplies a creative verdict. Missing observed actions stay unresolved. Retain an earlier\nsparse-image response and charge a content follow-up before executing it; it is not a free\nformatting call or a provider-unavailability event.\n\nAfter measured narration changes the board and preview timing, use the same authorized extractor\nwith `--phone-option current --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json --film out/dispatch/preflight.mp4`\nand a fresh output directory. It requires the current exact `preflight.json` inspection, edition,\nboard, renderer and movie bytes. It honors only the existing structural release policy; extraction\nstill supplies no verdict. Its separate operation reserves and claims once. Build a fresh ordinary\ncritic packet, then use `claude_runtime.py phone-packet --sequence-current <new index.json>` instead\nof the two comparison sequence flags. Keep the same packet, state and output arguments. This\nsingle-film packet binds the measured current board and film, returns a fresh exact-phone report,\nand does not choose the silent treatment again. The silent comparison index cannot prove the\ntimed movie; neither phone profile can satisfy the native final profile. Inspect all chronological\npages, consolidate one handback and recheck only specific uncertain intervals. Report unresolved\nobservations directly instead of repeatedly viewing the film to pursue approval.\n\nA cloud session has no desktop for Computer Use. Use `scripts/phone_playback.py`, real Chromium UI\nautomation at 390x844 with touch input, against the published canonical URL:\n\n```sh\npython scripts/phone_playback.py --edition-id <id> --film-sha256 <reviewed master sha256> --out-dir out/dispatch/phone\n```\n\nIt taps the page's own Play control (pause, then play again), taps \"tap for sound\", samples\ncurrentSrc, currentTime, readyState, paused, muted and error while the clock runs, records whether\nthe page received trusted input events, hashes the published master and phone bytes, and saves\nhashed screenshots. Its `tool` field says browser automation, not Computer Use. Put its\n`phone_playback.json` in the shipment manifest unchanged. `shipment_check.py` applies every\nhistorical assertion plus `claude_playback_problems`. The Codex Computer Use route and its evidence\nformat stay valid. Never fabricate observations. If the page, media or browser fails, production\nstays active and the real failure is recorded.\n\n## Haiku mechanical route (future editions only)\n\nEffective for editions from the date in `mechanical_route.effective_from` in `config/claude_runtime.json`.\nOne graded trial showed Haiku at high effort can diagnose and mechanically repair a caption layout gate when\nthe case is strictly specified. The route admits only that shape of work and refuses everything else, which\nleaves the unchanged Opus assignment. Its evidence is `runs/2026-10-11/experiments/haiku-calibration-1`,\nincluding the trial limitations, and it supports no wider claim.\n\n- Two tasks only. `code-only-review` runs the storyboard critic read only on named gate tests.\n  `mechanical-correction` runs the scene builder on named gate tests with one failing case, named acceptance\n  results, named unchanged controls and named mutation checks.\n- Only gate tests are in scope: files under `video-engine/tests/` and `scripts/*_test.py`. Renderer source,\n  art, story, claims, config, prompts, ledgers and every run path are refused, as is the initial authored build.\n  The three final scorers, the validator, the researcher and the voice director never use this route.\n- The packet stays the normal complete hash-bound role packet with every current guide. Add a `mechanical`\n  object to it before planning, naming the task, the exact existing files as `{path, sha256}` pairs and the required fields, and keep expected\n  findings out of the packet. The scope text may name only those files, and a correction's named results,\n  controls and mutation checks are non-empty lists of names. Plan with `python scripts/claude_runtime.py plan ... --mechanical-task <task>`.\n  An admitted plan adds only the Haiku spawn model and effort. The role, brief, packet and controller resource\n  are the unchanged ones, so reservations, charges and every gate are unchanged. A refusal is not an error to\n  work around. Plan the same task without the flag.\n- A Haiku result is never a verdict. Re run the named results, controls and mutation checks yourself, record the\n  actual agent identity, requested effort and observed usage, keep observed effort and billing unknown where\n  the host omits them, and let an Opus or Sonnet reviewer judge anything rendered.\n\n## Capture authorization\n\nFor a multi-repository cloud session, the environment setup registers the capture hook at its\nactual primary workspace before launch with\n`python scripts/bootstrap_claude_hooks.py --workspace /home/user --prelaunch-router`.\nThe preinstalled router selects the actual production checkout from the command's explicit\nworking directory, including restored checkouts, and runs the unchanged authorization gate.\nNever replace this registration during an agent turn. The helper preserves model, effort,\nenvironment, permissions and unrelated hooks. It replaces only its own earlier registration and\npoints the handler at the active checkout, whose ledger and assets the handler verifies. This is\nregistration, never proof that the host loaded it and never capture authorization. Keep the actual\nnative denial of the harmless capture-form probe before a real capture. If the host has not loaded\nthe registration, retain that observation and restart from the durable checkpoint using the supported\nroutine launch; do not replay synthetic PreToolUse events as a substitute or weaken auto mode.\nIf the host denies registration, preserve the denial and apply the same versioned registration in\nthe authorized environment setup before the next supported launch rather than retrying a denied edit.\n\nEvery native capture or render command (Remotion stills and renders, preflight, opening compare, cinema proof,\nrender_dispatch) is denied by the PreToolUse hook `scripts/capture_guard.py hook` unless the director has\nissued a current authorization for that exact command. Reserve a fresh render with the controller first\n(a late-accounting charge never counts), then name the exact boards and the exact wrapped commands:\n\n```sh\npython scripts/capture_guard.py authorize --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --board out/dispatch/opening-a.json --command \"bash scripts/run_with_env.sh python scripts/opening_compare.py --root out/dispatch --state out/dispatch/run_state.json\"\n```\n\nFor `preflight_animatic.py`, `cinema_proof.py` and `claude_motion_review.py`, use the\nprepared operator handoff instead of manually reserving a note and letting the operator reserve\nagain. `authorize --prepare` derives the operation from the exact checkout command, checks the\nsame art, headroom and housekeeping gates, then charges it once. The real host hook consumes\nthe exact authorization, and that operator claims its matching prepaid event once. A phone\npreview cannot claim a native hero charge; motion extraction has its own exact-film identity.\nAn unchanged operation cannot be prepared again. Preserve all earlier charges and denied commands.\nDo not create a self-written failure note or request `retry-preflight` to correct an operation\nlabel. Fix the actual versioned operator handoff and retain its before/after source evidence.\n\n```sh\npython scripts/capture_guard.py authorize --prepare --state out/dispatch/run_state.json --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json --command \"bash scripts/run_with_env.sh python scripts/cinema_proof.py --board out/dispatch/storyboard.json --mix out/dispatch/mix.wav --state out/dispatch/run_state.json\"\n```\n\nIt writes `out/dispatch/capture-authorization.json` only from facts: an unused fresh charged render reservation,\npassed native headroom, portable housekeeping run with `--apply --fetch --summary --require-headroom` and the\ncomputed minimum (its receipt is kept), and genuine recorded authored receipts. The authorization is bound to the\nexact board, renderer and art hashes and to the listed commands. The hook rechecks them and current headroom,\ndenies unreadable, unresolved or unrelated --props and --board inputs and placeholder art, and consumes each\nauthorized command once, so the next capture needs a new reservation. Builders never capture. Before the first\nreal capture of a run, prove the hook is active with a harmless capture-form command that must be denied,\nand keep that denial as evidence.\n",
        "config/claude_runtime.json": "{\n  \"version\": \"claude-sonnet-v1\",\n  \"authorized_at\": \"2026-10-09\",\n  \"measurement_editions\": 5,\n  \"baseline_editions\": [\"2026-10-08\", \"2026-10-09\"],\n  \"primary\": {\"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"effort\": \"medium\"},\n  \"schedule\": {\"timezone\": \"America/New_York\", \"daily_time\": \"01:00\"},\n  \"context\": \"isolated compact hash-bound packets; no recursive agents\",\n  \"artwork\": \"fresh original authored Remotion, SVG, CSS-depth or Three.js scenes\",\n  \"roles\": {\n    \"researcher\": {\"agent\": \"researcher\", \"model\": \"claude-haiku-5-5\", \"effort\": \"high\", \"resource\": \"research_agents\"},\n    \"validator\": {\"agent\": \"validator\", \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\", \"effort\": \"high\", \"resource\": \"validator_agents\"},\n    \"scene-builder\": {\"agent\": \"scene-builder\", \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\", \"effort\": \"high\", \"resource\": \"reboards\"},\n    \"storyboard-critic\": {\"agent\": \"storyboard-critic\", \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\", \"effort\": \"high\", \"resource\": \"storyboard_critics\"},\n    \"vo-director\": {\"agent\": \"vo-director\", \"model\": \"claude-haiku-5-5\", \"effort\": \"high\", \"resource\": \"voice_directors\"},\n    \"picture\": {\"agent\": \"scorer\", \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"effort\": \"medium\", \"resource\": \"scorer_calls\"},\n    \"story\": {\"agent\": \"scorer\", \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"effort\": \"medium\", \"resource\": \"scorer_calls\"},\n    \"sound\": {\"agent\": \"scorer\", \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"effort\": \"medium\", \"resource\": \"scorer_calls\"}\n  },\n  \"mechanical_route\": {\n    \"version\": \"haiku-mechanical-v1\",\n    \"effective_from\": \"2026-10-14\",\n    \"model\": \"claude-haiku-5-5\", \"effort\": \"high\", \"spawn_model\": \"haiku\",\n    \"tasks\": {\n      \"code-only-review\": {\"role\": \"storyboard-critic\", \"mode\": \"read-only\"},\n      \"mechanical-correction\": {\"role\": \"scene-builder\", \"mode\": \"edit\"}\n    },\n    \"allowed_paths\": [\"video-engine/tests/*\", \"scripts/*_test.py\"],\n    \"forbidden_prefixes\": [\".claude/\", \"config/\", \"prompts/\", \"knowledge/\", \"runs/\", \"out/\", \"ledger/\",\n                           \"video-engine/src/\", \"video-engine/public/\", \"assets/\", \"docs/\"],\n    \"correction_requires\": [\"failing_case\", \"acceptance_results\", \"unchanged_controls\", \"mutation_checks\"],\n    \"evidence\": \"runs/2026-10-11/experiments/haiku-calibration-1\",\n    \"scope_note\": \"Proven only on a caption layout gate and its test: one diagnostic and one repair, two named repaired cases, two unchanged controls, two mutation checks and a revert check. Unsupported renderers, art, story and source work stay on the Opus assignment. The three final scorers, the validator and the initial authored build are never admitted.\"\n  },\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents\",\n    \"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/model-config\",\n    \"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/routines\"\n  ],\n  \"accounting\": \"Record actual transcript usage, models, requested and observed effort, phase and worker. Account billing remains unknown unless the host provides it. Preserve separate external-provider telemetry.\",\n  \"quality\": \"Retain the current rubric, independent exact-film reviews, modern engagement observations and every mandatory shipment gate. Historical editions and frozen charges remain unchanged.\"\n}\n",
        "knowledge/craft/ART_DIRECTION.md": "# Direct a world before building a scene\n\nTeaching sources: [Pixar's cinematography account](https://renderman.pixar.com/stories/incredible-cinematography)\nfor coordinated staging, light and camera; [OpenAI evaluation practices](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/evaluation-best-practices)\nfor reference calibration, pairwise comparison and order bias. Current filmed evidence decides\nwhich choices work here.\n\nRead this with the viewer method, selected approach dossier, fixed quality contract and\ncurrent rubric. It adds executable craft inputs and calibration, not a score, quota,\nnew judge or extra paid attempt. Existing source, rights, action, native, audio, captions,\ncumulative resources, finite artistic recovery and shipment requirements continue.\n\n## Director\n\nBefore coding, choose the visual approach from actual source access. Think through four\nlenses in the existing director assignment: the comedian finds an observable mismatch;\nthe dramatist finds pressure and a changed state; the explainer finds the causal relation;\nthe enthusiast finds a specific surprising detail. Do not invent a joke, conflict or\noutcome. Choose exactly two complete treatments within the current comparison allowance.\n\nWrite `art_direction` in each board using `config/art_direction.json`. Explain seven palette\nroles, contrasting shapes, the recognizable hero silhouette and its finish, motivated\nlight, focal hierarchy, action timing, and one signature shot tied to an actual event.\nName the current asset and actual subject ids. Use the source image itself when it is the\nhero. Give a dimensional scene a `shots[scene_id]` camera position, target, lens and reason;\nan event-bound `to` pose is optional. For the illustrated carton route, use `flat_shots`\nwith native-coordinate offsets, scale and a reason. Numeric shot choices must be executed\nby the routed scene, not left as board prose. A custom renderer must consume the same\nprofile or explain its retained source lighting and implement its relevant choices.\n\nThe focal object stays sharp. Depth blur must arise from actual separation and preserve\ncontact detail. Never add blur, floating shapes, lens flares, camera kicks or orbiting as\nautomatic cinematic decoration. Hold the camera while an object performs. Move it to reveal\na relation or follow a finite action. Give a completed result a comprehension hold.\n\n## Scene builder and render owner\n\nUse `prompts/roles/scene-builder.md` in the existing code assignment. Build the finished\nhero first, then light and stage it before extending the scene. Recognizable geometry,\nedges, seams, hardware, texture and grounded shadows beat a field of placeholder primitives.\nAuthored 2.5D, useful footage and a readable source image can outperform complicated 3D.\nDo not restrict the daily story to the demonstration subject or copy reference b-roll.\n\nThe shared `ArtDirectionProvider` carries current choices in both entry points. Three.js\n`CinematicStage`/`Studio` execute the light recipe and exposure. `directedShot` executes\nauthored event-bound cameras. The illustrated carton component executes its flat framing,\nfinished surfaces, occlusion and contact assemblies. Source footage retains original speed\nand practical lighting. Existing boards without this profile retain their original defaults.\n\nEvery new event specifies a motion curve within its existing measured window: `travel`\naccelerates and brakes; `contact` approaches and settles; `linear` serves constant-speed\nmovement; `smoothstep` is available for a justified gentle transition. `anticipation` and\n`settle` reserve fractions inside that window, never new runtime or voice stretching.\n`landing` has a small overshoot and needs a free-prop reason; never use it for a constrained\ncontact, a foot planted on ground, or a source-implied machine limit. Check music and foley\nagainst the executed contact, not the old curve. No incidental sway substitutes for action.\n\nJudge motion at the delivered 30 fps. A regular frame clock does not excuse abrupt starts,\nfast screen-space travel or repeated stop-and-go strokes. Directed `travel` and `contact`\ncurves start and finish with zero velocity and acceleration. Give a heavy load enough of\nthe existing scene window to accelerate and brake. Holds consume that window; do not squeeze\nthe entire stroke into the remaining few frames. Inspect velocity at event joins as well\nas the start and end. Keep a clear contact view and a stable camera when tracking amplifies\nthe load's movement. Do not conceal stepping with blur, frame interpolation or faster audio.\nAn event-bound moving camera uses `travel` or `contact`; the input check refuses constant-speed\nstarts and landing overshoot on a camera. Hold it when the object needs a different curve.\n\nWhen two named events describe successive stages of one uninterrupted movement, author\nadjacent windows with no interior anticipation or settle, then explicitly use\n`joinedActionWindow`. The helper rejects gaps, scene boundaries and erased rests. The\nillustrated carton route consumes `continuous_withdrawal_event_ids` only in its withdrawal\nscene. Retiming a movement keeps the source relation, scene runtime and measured captions.\n\n## Existing independent critic and three scorers\n\nWatch the actual muted sequence first. Name the object, action, changed state and answered\nquestion before reading the profile. Then test whether its choices are visible: compare\nsilhouette, contact, surface finish, hierarchy, framing, rhythm and hold at phone size and\nnative crop scale. Inspect the beginning, contact and end of every action. Keep narration\nand labels covered on the first pass. A good explanation in the profile cannot clear an\noccluded grip, generic slab, unrecognizable subject or absent transformation.\n\nWatch uninterrupted playback at normal speed. Check for velocity jumps, stop-and-go camera\ntracking, repeated frames during movement and excessively large per-frame displacement.\nSeparate deliberate shot cuts and completed holds from a continuous stroke that stutters.\nRecord the exact interval and affected object or camera. Smooth motion is a visible property,\nnot a consequence of a passing score or a high frame rate.\n\nRead `knowledge/craft/cinematic_reference_bank.json`. Its frozen passages teach specific\ndecisions; their old scores use different rubrics and are not comparable ratings. They are\nreferences, never production assets or current approval. Compare two current complete cuts,\ndescribe a preference with exact times, then record mandatory defects under the existing\ncriteria. A different palette preference alone does not create another correction. Retain\nall original rejections. At the configured artistic boundary, finish the strongest credible\ncut; source, comprehension and technical failures still take the mandatory recovery route.\n\n## Learn from shipped and failed footage\n\n`scripts/cinematic_learning.py` records the next five editions from the policy's effective\ndate, including unfinished editions, first-panel success, scores, all actual resource usage,\nprovider tokens, elapsed time, correction counts and artistic deferrals. Unknown account\ntokens remain null. Do not claim future results or a numerical improvement multiplier.\n\nAfter durable shipment, refresh the report and the recurring-defect packet from the last\nfourteen days. At most once per seven days, give the existing builder a fresh compact packet:\nup to five recurring findings, exact rejected evidence and one proposed shared capability.\nReproduce the failed interval; add a useful regression; prove the correction inside the next\nedition's already reserved two-treatment comparison. Mark the actual advance or honest skip\nin the packet. This is one shared engineering advance, not five new stylistic attempts.\nFund the entire remaining production/review/delivery path before changing the renderer.\nDo not delay an accepted cut for optional engineering or add roles, reviews or resource grants.\n",
