                "text": " and operates independently of cellular towers. The station mounts four optical sensors at varying heights along its post to track rising water while"
              },
              {
                "text": " auxiliary sensors monitor rain, temperature, humidity, and light. An integrated TinyML chip processes these environmental readings locally, determining"
              },
              {
                "text": " flood risk without contacting an external server. The station transmits its alert via long-range radio up to a half-mile"
              },
              {
                "text": " through city streets or five miles across open terrain to a central monitoring hub. There, a secondary AI model aggregates station data"
              },
