od, the paper street map pinned to the chain link fence settles, with no pin on it. A hand slides one finger along the map's creek and up a street past its blank pin holes and lifts away. An announcement names no installation tag pins beside the map.\",\"64\":\"The second, larger model shades how flooding could spread and outlines the higher-risk zones.\",\"66\":{\"action_ids\":[\"show-estimate\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"alert-card\",\"ten-minute-arc\",\"estimate-tag\"]},\"67\":\"The team aims to refine the design into a sleeker, weatherized commercial product suitable for deployment by small coastal municipalities, homeowners\\u2019 associations, agricultural operations and industrial sites.\",\"68\":\"At a folding table on the curb a technician folds the printed deployment plan in three along its creases.\",\"7\":{\"action_ids\":[\"await-approval\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"plan-folder\",\"approval-stamp-slot\",\"expected-tag\",\"tower-camera\"]},\"70\":{\"anticipation\":0,\"curve\":\"travel\",\"settle\":0.03},\"71\":\"video-engine/src/modern/FreightFilm.tsx\",\"72\":{\"anticipation\":0,\"curve\":\"smoothstep\",\"settle\":0.03},\"73\":\"Rain, temperature, humidity and light lamps come on one by one on the housing, each with its label.\",\"74\":[\"s1\",\"s2\",\"s3\",\"s4\",\"s5\",\"s6\",\"s7\",\"s8\"],\"75\":\"Brown water tops the limestone curb, spreads across a San Antonio yard with no station in it and climbs a chain link post to its orange ankle mark. The water keeps rising to the rain boots on the porch step while the phone on the porch rail stays dark. The flash flood warning banner finally slides onto the phone, after the water is already in the yard.\",\"76\":{\"action_ids\":[\"restore-partial\"],\"subject_ids\":[\"normal-fly\",\"variant-fly\"]},\"77\":\"d22b35bbef63ae6f34713c555beb54cd696c6dc08c09da4f9bae73ffd7e388b4\",\"79\":\"video-engine/src/modern/FlyGeneFilm.tsx\",\"8\":\"The same flood station at the same curb, its lowest mark already lit by the water\",\"80\":